        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the use or disclosure is necessary for research, or the compilation or analysis of statistics, relevant to public health or public safety;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16b-ss-3-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "!",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Impracticability for consent",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) it is impracticable for the organisation to obtain the individual’s consent to the use or disclosure;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16b-ss-3-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "!",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Conduct in accordance with guidelines",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) the use or disclosure is conducted in accordance with guidelines approved under section 95A for the purposes of this paragraph;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16b-ss-3-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "!",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Reasonable belief about recipient’s actions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(d) in the case of disclosure—the organisation reasonably believes that the recipient of the information will not disclose the information, or personal information derived from that information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16B(4) Permitted health situations in relation to the collection, use or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-16b-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A permitted health situation exists in relation to the use or\ndisclosure by an organisation of genetic information about an\nindividual (the first individual) if:\n\n(a) the organisation has obtained the information in the course of\nproviding a health service to the first individual; and\n\n(b) the organisation reasonably believes that the use or disclosure\nis necessary to lessen or prevent a serious threat to the life,\nhealth or safety of another individual who is a genetic\nrelative of the first individual; and\n\n(c) the use or disclosure is conducted in accordance with\nguidelines approved under section 95AA; and\n\n(d) in the case of disclosure—the recipient of the information is a\ngenetic relative of the first individual.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 1  Australian Privacy Principles\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nDisclosure—responsible person for an individual",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A permitted health situation exists in relation to the use or\ndisclosure by an organisation of genetic information about an\nindividual (the first individual) if:\n\n(a) the organisation has obtained the information in the course of\nproviding a health service to the first individual; and\n\n(b) the organisation reasonably believes that the use or disclosure\nis necessary to lessen or prevent a serious threat to the life,\nhealth or safety of another individual who is a genetic\nrelative of the first individual; and\n\n(c) the use or disclosure is conducted in accordance with\nguidelines approved under section 95AA; and\n\n(d) in the case of disclosure—the recipient of the information is a\ngenetic relative of the first individual.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 1  Australian Privacy Principles\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nDisclosure—responsible person for an individual",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16b-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16b-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16b-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d48b0fa172f167f0b63c6bbf34bfd1f3d766e82cfc37daeddee2f40bd83b6fd9",
      "skos:note": "Permitted health situations for the use or disclosure of genetic information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-16b-ss-4",
