    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16b-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines conditions under which disclosure is permitted",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(5) A permitted health situation exists in relation to the disclosure by an organisation of health information about an individual if...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the disclosure is permitted if the conditions are met"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16b-ss-5-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines scope of permitted disclosure",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(f) the disclosure is limited to the extent reasonable and necessary for a purpose mentioned in paragraph (d)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the disclosure must be limited to what is reasonable and necessary"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16b-ss-5-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines exceptions to permitted disclosure",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(e) the disclosure is not contrary to any wish expressed by the individual before the individual became unable to give or communicate consent",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the disclosure must not contradict the individual's wishes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16b-ss-5-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines exceptions to permitted disclosure",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(e) of which the carer is aware, or of which the carer could reasonably be expected to be aware",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the disclosure must not contradict wishes known to the carer"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16C Acts and practices of overseas recipients of personal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-16c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "information\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an APP entity discloses personal information about an\nindividual to an overseas recipient; and\n\n(b) Australian Privacy Principle 8.1 applies to the disclosure of\nthe information; and\n\n(c) the Australian Privacy Principles do not apply, under this\nAct, to an act done, or a practice engaged in, by the overseas\nrecipient in relation to the information; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nAustralian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) the overseas recipient does an act, or engages in a practice, in\nrelation to the information that would be a breach of the\nAustralian Privacy Principles (other than Australian Privacy\nPrinciple 1) if those Australian Privacy Principles so applied\nto that act or practice.\n\n(2) The act done, or the practice engaged in, by the overseas recipient\nis taken, for the purposes of this Act:\n\n(a) to have been done, or engaged in, by the APP entity; and\n\n(b) to be a breach of those Australian Privacy Principles by the\nAPP entity.",
      "skos:definition": "information\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an APP entity discloses personal information about an\nindividual to an overseas recipient; and\n\n(b) Australian Privacy Principle 8.1 applies to the disclosure of\nthe information; and\n\n(c) the Australian Privacy Principles do not apply, under this\nAct, to an act done, or a practice engaged in, by the overseas\nrecipient in relation to the information; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nAustralian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) the overseas recipient does an act, or engages in a practice, in\nrelation to the information that would be a breach of the\nAustralian Privacy Principles (other than Australian Privacy\nPrinciple 1) if those Australian Privacy Principles so applied\nto that act or practice.\n\n(2) The act done, or the practice engaged in, by the overseas recipient\nis taken, for the purposes of this Act:\n\n(a) to have been done, or engaged in, by the APP entity; and\n\n(b) to be a breach of those Australian Privacy Principles by the\nAPP entity.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16c-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dea7111a8406e27cfc8bf5f49c5d40898402b0b584b3285f069170a36f9eec31"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-16c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16C Acts and practices of overseas recipients of personal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "information\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an APP entity discloses personal information about an\nindividual to an overseas recipient; and\n\n(b) Australian Privacy Principle 8.1 applies to the disclosure of\nthe information; and\n\n(c) the Australian Privacy Principles do not apply, under this\nAct, to an act done, or a practice engaged in, by the overseas\nrecipient in relation to the information; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nAustralian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) the overseas recipient does an act, or engages in a practice, in\nrelation to the information that would be a breach of the\nAustralian Privacy Principles (other than Australian Privacy\nPrinciple 1) if those Australian Privacy Principles so applied\nto that act or practice.\n\n(2) The act done, or the practice engaged in, by the overseas recipient\nis taken, for the purposes of this Act:\n\n(a) to have been done, or engaged in, by the APP entity; and\n\n(b) to be a breach of those Australian Privacy Principles by the\nAPP entity."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-16c-ss-1",
