      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "(a) the APP entity determines that the entity could not have\ncollected the personal information; and\n\n(b) the information is not contained in a Commonwealth record;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nAustralian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nthe entity must, as soon as practicable but only if it is lawful and\nreasonable to do so, destroy the information or ensure that the\ninformation is de-identified.",
      "skos:definition": "(a) the APP entity determines that the entity could not have\ncollected the personal information; and\n\n(b) the information is not contained in a Commonwealth record;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nAustralian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nthe entity must, as soon as practicable but only if it is lawful and\nreasonable to do so, destroy the information or ensure that the\ninformation is de-identified.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-4-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-4-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-4-5-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
