        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-4-5-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-4-5-logic-argumentation-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e6de39068972e1d7e8f10ab61c5839ebd68582673919f59c1e4569b62d94a75e",
      "skos:note": "Destroy personal information if it cannot be collected or is not in a Commonwealth record."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-4-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 3 If:",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "(a) the APP entity determines that the entity could not have\ncollected the personal information; and\n\n(b) the information is not contained in a Commonwealth record;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nAustralian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nthe entity must, as soon as practicable but only if it is lawful and\nreasonable to do so, destroy the information or ensure that the\ninformation is de-identified."
    },
