    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-6-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 1 If an APP entity holds personal information about an individual",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-6-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "that was collected for a particular purpose (the primary purpose),\nthe entity must not use or disclose the information for another\npurpose (the secondary purpose) unless:\n\n(a) the individual has consented to the use or disclosure of the\ninformation; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nAustralian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) subclause 6.2 or 6.3 applies in relation to the use or\ndisclosure of the information.\nNote:\nAustralian Privacy Principle 8 sets out requirements for the disclosure\nof personal information to a person who is not in Australia or an\nexternal Territory.",
      "skos:definition": "that was collected for a particular purpose (the primary purpose),\nthe entity must not use or disclose the information for another\npurpose (the secondary purpose) unless:\n\n(a) the individual has consented to the use or disclosure of the\ninformation; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nAustralian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) subclause 6.2 or 6.3 applies in relation to the use or\ndisclosure of the information.\nNote:\nAustralian Privacy Principle 8 sets out requirements for the disclosure\nof personal information to a person who is not in Australia or an\nexternal Territory.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-6-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-6-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-6-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "751f62147f93ab5810ce6c3a305a748d5ed7da445aa0c6b3d9a67fb42864540e",
      "skos:note": "Must not use or disclose personal information for a secondary purpose without consent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-6-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 1 If an APP entity holds personal information about an individual",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "that was collected for a particular purpose (the primary purpose),\nthe entity must not use or disclose the information for another\npurpose (the secondary purpose) unless:\n\n(a) the individual has consented to the use or disclosure of the\ninformation; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nAustralian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) subclause 6.2 or 6.3 applies in relation to the use or\ndisclosure of the information.\nNote:\nAustralian Privacy Principle 8 sets out requirements for the disclosure\nof personal information to a person who is not in Australia or an\nexternal Territory."
    },
