    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 1 Before an APP entity discloses personal information about an",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-8-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "individual to a person (the overseas recipient):\n\n(a) who is not in Australia or an external Territory; and\n\n(b) who is not the entity or the individual;\nthe entity must take such steps as are reasonable in the\ncircumstances to ensure that the overseas recipient does not breach\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 1  Australian Privacy Principles\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nthe Australian Privacy Principles (other than Australian Privacy\nPrinciple 1) in relation to the information.\nNote:\nIn certain circumstances, an act done, or a practice engaged in, by the\noverseas recipient is taken, under section 16C, to have been done, or\nengaged in, by the APP entity and to be a breach of the Australian\nPrivacy Principles.",
      "skos:definition": "individual to a person (the overseas recipient):\n\n(a) who is not in Australia or an external Territory; and\n\n(b) who is not the entity or the individual;\nthe entity must take such steps as are reasonable in the\ncircumstances to ensure that the overseas recipient does not breach\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 1  Australian Privacy Principles\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nthe Australian Privacy Principles (other than Australian Privacy\nPrinciple 1) in relation to the information.\nNote:\nIn certain circumstances, an act done, or a practice engaged in, by the\noverseas recipient is taken, under section 16C, to have been done, or\nengaged in, by the APP entity and to be a breach of the Australian\nPrivacy Principles.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6fcd72070efc3adeed76d4030332a6fd6aa5d47e5f831e07a9ef9f68c430d8ef",
      "skos:note": "Entity must ensure overseas recipient does not breach Australian Privacy Principles"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-8-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 1 Before an APP entity discloses personal information about an",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "individual to a person (the overseas recipient):\n\n(a) who is not in Australia or an external Territory; and\n\n(b) who is not the entity or the individual;\nthe entity must take such steps as are reasonable in the\ncircumstances to ensure that the overseas recipient does not breach\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 1  Australian Privacy Principles\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nthe Australian Privacy Principles (other than Australian Privacy\nPrinciple 1) in relation to the information.\nNote:\nIn certain circumstances, an act done, or a practice engaged in, by the\noverseas recipient is taken, under section 16C, to have been done, or\nengaged in, by the APP entity and to be a breach of the Australian\nPrivacy Principles."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Entity has an obligation to ensure overseas recipient does not breach Australian Privacy Principles",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 2 Subclause 8.1 does not apply to the disclosure of personal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-8-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "information about an individual by an APP entity to the overseas\nrecipient if:\n\n(a) the entity reasonably believes that:\n\n(i) the recipient of the information is subject to a law, or\nbinding scheme, that has the effect of protecting the\ninformation in a way that, overall, is at least\nsubstantially similar to the way in which the Australian\nPrivacy Principles protect the information; and\n\n(ii) there are mechanisms that the individual can access to\ntake action to enforce that protection of the law or\nbinding scheme; or\n\n(b) both of the following apply:\n\n(i) the entity expressly informs the individual that if he or\nshe consents to the disclosure of the information,\nsubclause 8.1 will not apply to the disclosure;\n\n(ii) after being so informed, the individual consents to the\ndisclosure; or\n\n(c) the disclosure of the information is required or authorised by\nor under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(d) a permitted general situation (other than the situation referred\nto in item 4 or 5 of the table in subsection 16A(1)) exists in\nrelation to the disclosure of the information by the APP\nentity; or\n\n(e) the entity is an agency and the disclosure of the information\nis required or authorised by or under an international\nagreement relating to information sharing to which Australia\nis a party; or\n\n(f) the entity is an agency and both of the following apply:\n\n(i) the entity reasonably believes that the disclosure of the\ninformation is reasonably necessary for one or more\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nAustralian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nenforcement related activities conducted by, or on\nbehalf of, an enforcement body;\n\n(ii) the recipient is a body that performs functions, or\nexercises powers, that are similar to those performed or\nexercised by an enforcement body.\nNote:\nFor permitted general situation, see section 16A.",
      "skos:definition": "information about an individual by an APP entity to the overseas\nrecipient if:\n\n(a) the entity reasonably believes that:\n\n(i) the recipient of the information is subject to a law, or\nbinding scheme, that has the effect of protecting the\ninformation in a way that, overall, is at least\nsubstantially similar to the way in which the Australian\nPrivacy Principles protect the information; and\n\n(ii) there are mechanisms that the individual can access to\ntake action to enforce that protection of the law or\nbinding scheme; or\n\n(b) both of the following apply:\n\n(i) the entity expressly informs the individual that if he or\nshe consents to the disclosure of the information,\nsubclause 8.1 will not apply to the disclosure;\n\n(ii) after being so informed, the individual consents to the\ndisclosure; or\n\n(c) the disclosure of the information is required or authorised by\nor under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(d) a permitted general situation (other than the situation referred\nto in item 4 or 5 of the table in subsection 16A(1)) exists in\nrelation to the disclosure of the information by the APP\nentity; or\n\n(e) the entity is an agency and the disclosure of the information\nis required or authorised by or under an international\nagreement relating to information sharing to which Australia\nis a party; or\n\n(f) the entity is an agency and both of the following apply:\n\n(i) the entity reasonably believes that the disclosure of the\ninformation is reasonably necessary for one or more\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nAustralian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nenforcement related activities conducted by, or on\nbehalf of, an enforcement body;\n\n(ii) the recipient is a body that performs functions, or\nexercises powers, that are similar to those performed or\nexercised by an enforcement body.\nNote:\nFor permitted general situation, see section 16A.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-4-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-4-logic-cogai-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-8-4-logic-shacl-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "985fdc878e0df849e4036ad987b52be81a47a8b8efaa3a64db01295709ab29e0",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of personal information is permitted under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-8-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 2 Subclause 8.1 does not apply to the disclosure of personal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "information about an individual by an APP entity to the overseas\nrecipient if:\n\n(a) the entity reasonably believes that:\n\n(i) the recipient of the information is subject to a law, or\nbinding scheme, that has the effect of protecting the\ninformation in a way that, overall, is at least\nsubstantially similar to the way in which the Australian\nPrivacy Principles protect the information; and\n\n(ii) there are mechanisms that the individual can access to\ntake action to enforce that protection of the law or\nbinding scheme; or\n\n(b) both of the following apply:\n\n(i) the entity expressly informs the individual that if he or\nshe consents to the disclosure of the information,\nsubclause 8.1 will not apply to the disclosure;\n\n(ii) after being so informed, the individual consents to the\ndisclosure; or\n\n(c) the disclosure of the information is required or authorised by\nor under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(d) a permitted general situation (other than the situation referred\nto in item 4 or 5 of the table in subsection 16A(1)) exists in\nrelation to the disclosure of the information by the APP\nentity; or\n\n(e) the entity is an agency and the disclosure of the information\nis required or authorised by or under an international\nagreement relating to information sharing to which Australia\nis a party; or\n\n(f) the entity is an agency and both of the following apply:\n\n(i) the entity reasonably believes that the disclosure of the\ninformation is reasonably necessary for one or more\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nAustralian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nenforcement related activities conducted by, or on\nbehalf of, an enforcement body;\n\n(ii) the recipient is a body that performs functions, or\nexercises powers, that are similar to those performed or\nexercised by an enforcement body.\nNote:\nFor permitted general situation, see section 16A."
    },
