      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-9-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 2 An organisation must not use or disclose a government related",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-9-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "identifier of an individual unless:\n\n(a) the use or disclosure of the identifier is reasonably necessary\nfor the organisation to verify the identity of the individual for\nthe purposes of the organisation’s activities or functions; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure of the identifier is reasonably necessary\nfor the organisation to fulfil its obligations to an agency or a\nState or Territory authority; or\n\n(c) the use or disclosure of the identifier is required or authorised\nby or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(d) a permitted general situation (other than the situation referred\nto in item 4 or 5 of the table in subsection 16A(1)) exists in\nrelation to the use or disclosure of the identifier; or\n\n(e) the organisation reasonably believes that the use or disclosure\nof the identifier is reasonably necessary for one or more\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 1  Australian Privacy Principles\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nenforcement related activities conducted by, or on behalf of,\nan enforcement body; or\n\n(f) subclause 9.3 applies in relation to the use or disclosure.\nNote 1:\nAn act or practice of an agency may be treated as an act or practice of\nan organisation, see section 7A.\nNote 2:\nFor permitted general situation, see section 16A.\nRegulations about adoption, use or disclosure",
      "skos:definition": "identifier of an individual unless:\n\n(a) the use or disclosure of the identifier is reasonably necessary\nfor the organisation to verify the identity of the individual for\nthe purposes of the organisation’s activities or functions; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure of the identifier is reasonably necessary\nfor the organisation to fulfil its obligations to an agency or a\nState or Territory authority; or\n\n(c) the use or disclosure of the identifier is required or authorised\nby or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(d) a permitted general situation (other than the situation referred\nto in item 4 or 5 of the table in subsection 16A(1)) exists in\nrelation to the use or disclosure of the identifier; or\n\n(e) the organisation reasonably believes that the use or disclosure\nof the identifier is reasonably necessary for one or more\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 1  Australian Privacy Principles\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nenforcement related activities conducted by, or on behalf of,\nan enforcement body; or\n\n(f) subclause 9.3 applies in relation to the use or disclosure.\nNote 1:\nAn act or practice of an agency may be treated as an act or practice of\nan organisation, see section 7A.\nNote 2:\nFor permitted general situation, see section 16A.\nRegulations about adoption, use or disclosure",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-9-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-1-sec-9-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d75cfd2d376f4e6045a44b56eb4aaa8316f7f7d4c1ed76971af7066fc3243190",
      "skos:note": "Organisation must not use or disclose government-related identifier unless certain conditions apply."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-1-sec-9-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 2 An organisation must not use or disclose a government related",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "identifier of an individual unless:\n\n(a) the use or disclosure of the identifier is reasonably necessary\nfor the organisation to verify the identity of the individual for\nthe purposes of the organisation’s activities or functions; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure of the identifier is reasonably necessary\nfor the organisation to fulfil its obligations to an agency or a\nState or Territory authority; or\n\n(c) the use or disclosure of the identifier is required or authorised\nby or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(d) a permitted general situation (other than the situation referred\nto in item 4 or 5 of the table in subsection 16A(1)) exists in\nrelation to the use or disclosure of the identifier; or\n\n(e) the organisation reasonably believes that the use or disclosure\nof the identifier is reasonably necessary for one or more\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 1  Australian Privacy Principles\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nenforcement related activities conducted by, or on behalf of,\nan enforcement body; or\n\n(f) subclause 9.3 applies in relation to the use or disclosure.\nNote 1:\nAn act or practice of an agency may be treated as an act or practice of\nan organisation, see section 7A.\nNote 2:\nFor permitted general situation, see section 16A.\nRegulations about adoption, use or disclosure"
    },
