      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6H Agents of credit providers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-6h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an organisation or small business operator (the agent) is acting\nas an agent of a credit provider (the principal) in performing, on\nbehalf of the principal, a task that is reasonably necessary:\n\n(a) in processing an application for credit made to the principal;\nor\n\n(b) in managing credit provided by the principal;\nthen, while the agent is so acting, the agent is a credit provider.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the principal is an organisation or\nsmall business operator that is a credit provider because of a\nprevious application of that subsection.\n\n(3) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit that has been provided\nby the principal, the credit is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to\nhave been provided by both the principal and the agent.\n\n(4) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit for which an\napplication has been made to the principal, the application is taken,\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nfor the purposes of this Act, to have been made to both the\nprincipal and the agent.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an organisation or small business operator (the agent) is acting\nas an agent of a credit provider (the principal) in performing, on\nbehalf of the principal, a task that is reasonably necessary:\n\n(a) in processing an application for credit made to the principal;\nor\n\n(b) in managing credit provided by the principal;\nthen, while the agent is so acting, the agent is a credit provider.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the principal is an organisation or\nsmall business operator that is a credit provider because of a\nprevious application of that subsection.\n\n(3) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit that has been provided\nby the principal, the credit is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to\nhave been provided by both the principal and the agent.\n\n(4) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit for which an\napplication has been made to the principal, the application is taken,\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nfor the purposes of this Act, to have been made to both the\nprincipal and the agent.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6h-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6h-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c8735a4b62d955151fc40f86e82c4c37391a3b5ba1783f529fc858116d3f44fc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-6h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6H Agents of credit providers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an organisation or small business operator (the agent) is acting\nas an agent of a credit provider (the principal) in performing, on\nbehalf of the principal, a task that is reasonably necessary:\n\n(a) in processing an application for credit made to the principal;\nor\n\n(b) in managing credit provided by the principal;\nthen, while the agent is so acting, the agent is a credit provider.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the principal is an organisation or\nsmall business operator that is a credit provider because of a\nprevious application of that subsection.\n\n(3) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit that has been provided\nby the principal, the credit is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to\nhave been provided by both the principal and the agent.\n\n(4) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit for which an\napplication has been made to the principal, the application is taken,\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nfor the purposes of this Act, to have been made to both the\nprincipal and the agent."
    },
