      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit for which an\napplication has been made to the principal, the application is taken,\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nfor the purposes of this Act, to have been made to both the\nprincipal and the agent.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit for which an\napplication has been made to the principal, the application is taken,\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nfor the purposes of this Act, to have been made to both the\nprincipal and the agent.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6h"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6h-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6h-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "081c4d2894567efd4d52ca8072f1d815bae508921eb7c3db9b4de76cc1303a62",
      "skos:note": "Application to principal is taken as made to both principal and agent for purposes of this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-6h-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6H(4) Agents of credit providers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit for which an\napplication has been made to the principal, the application is taken,\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nfor the purposes of this Act, to have been made to both the\nprincipal and the agent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6h-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6h-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6h-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Application to principal is taken as made to both principal and agent.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6J Securitisation arrangements etc.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-6j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.69",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an organisation or small business operator (the securitisation\nentity) carries on a business that is involved in either or both\nof the following:\n\n(i) a securitisation arrangement;\n\n(ii) managing credit that is the subject of a securitisation\narrangement; and\n\n(b) the securitisation entity performs a task that is reasonably\nnecessary for:\n\n(i) purchasing, funding or managing, or processing an\napplication for, credit by means of a securitisation\narrangement; or\n\n(ii) undertaking credit enhancement in relation to credit; and\n\n(c) the credit has been provided by, or is credit for which an\napplication has been made to, a credit provider (the original\ncredit provider);\nthen, while the securitisation entity performs such a task, the\nsecuritisation entity is a credit provider.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the original credit provider is an\norganisation or small business operator that is a credit provider\nbecause of a previous application of that subsection.\n\n(3) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit that has been provided\nby the original credit provider, the credit is taken, for the purposes\nof this Act, to have been provided by both the original credit\nprovider and the securitisation entity.\n\n(4) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit for which an\napplication has been made to the original credit provider, the\napplication is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been\nmade to both the original credit provider and the securitisation\nentity.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an organisation or small business operator (the securitisation\nentity) carries on a business that is involved in either or both\nof the following:\n\n(i) a securitisation arrangement;\n\n(ii) managing credit that is the subject of a securitisation\narrangement; and\n\n(b) the securitisation entity performs a task that is reasonably\nnecessary for:\n\n(i) purchasing, funding or managing, or processing an\napplication for, credit by means of a securitisation\narrangement; or\n\n(ii) undertaking credit enhancement in relation to credit; and\n\n(c) the credit has been provided by, or is credit for which an\napplication has been made to, a credit provider (the original\ncredit provider);\nthen, while the securitisation entity performs such a task, the\nsecuritisation entity is a credit provider.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the original credit provider is an\norganisation or small business operator that is a credit provider\nbecause of a previous application of that subsection.\n\n(3) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit that has been provided\nby the original credit provider, the credit is taken, for the purposes\nof this Act, to have been provided by both the original credit\nprovider and the securitisation entity.\n\n(4) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit for which an\napplication has been made to the original credit provider, the\napplication is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been\nmade to both the original credit provider and the securitisation\nentity.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6j-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6j-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6j-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9bc41774e4820cef03ea413bdc8978b0f1c11beb372a5fe9d106089c9f297306"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-6j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6J Securitisation arrangements etc.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 69,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an organisation or small business operator (the securitisation\nentity) carries on a business that is involved in either or both\nof the following:\n\n(i) a securitisation arrangement;\n\n(ii) managing credit that is the subject of a securitisation\narrangement; and\n\n(b) the securitisation entity performs a task that is reasonably\nnecessary for:\n\n(i) purchasing, funding or managing, or processing an\napplication for, credit by means of a securitisation\narrangement; or\n\n(ii) undertaking credit enhancement in relation to credit; and\n\n(c) the credit has been provided by, or is credit for which an\napplication has been made to, a credit provider (the original\ncredit provider);\nthen, while the securitisation entity performs such a task, the\nsecuritisation entity is a credit provider.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the original credit provider is an\norganisation or small business operator that is a credit provider\nbecause of a previous application of that subsection.\n\n(3) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit that has been provided\nby the original credit provider, the credit is taken, for the purposes\nof this Act, to have been provided by both the original credit\nprovider and the securitisation entity.\n\n(4) If subsection (1) applies in relation to credit for which an\napplication has been made to the original credit provider, the\napplication is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been\nmade to both the original credit provider and the securitisation\nentity.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15"
    },
