    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6M Meaning of credit and amount of credit",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-6m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.71",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Credit is a contract, arrangement or understanding under which:\n\n(a) payment of a debt owed by one person to another person is\ndeferred; or\n\n(b) one person incurs a debt to another person and defers the\npayment of the debt.\n\n(2) The amount of credit is the amount of the debt that is actually\ndeferred, or that may be deferred, but does not include any fees or\ncharges payable in connection with the deferral of the debt.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (1), credit includes:\n\n(a) a hire-purchase agreement; and\n\n(b) a contract, arrangement or understanding of a kind referred to\nin that subsection that is for the hire, lease or rental of goods,\nor for the supply of services, other than a contract,\narrangement or understanding under which:\n\n(i) full payment is made before, or at the same time as, the\ngoods or services are provided; and\n\n(ii) in the case of goods—an amount greater than, or equal\nto, the value of the goods is paid as a deposit for the\nreturn of the goods.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Credit is a contract, arrangement or understanding under which:\n\n(a) payment of a debt owed by one person to another person is\ndeferred; or\n\n(b) one person incurs a debt to another person and defers the\npayment of the debt.\n\n(2) The amount of credit is the amount of the debt that is actually\ndeferred, or that may be deferred, but does not include any fees or\ncharges payable in connection with the deferral of the debt.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (1), credit includes:\n\n(a) a hire-purchase agreement; and\n\n(b) a contract, arrangement or understanding of a kind referred to\nin that subsection that is for the hire, lease or rental of goods,\nor for the supply of services, other than a contract,\narrangement or understanding under which:\n\n(i) full payment is made before, or at the same time as, the\ngoods or services are provided; and\n\n(ii) in the case of goods—an amount greater than, or equal\nto, the value of the goods is paid as a deposit for the\nreturn of the goods.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6m-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6m-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6m-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "411059c6b392da91d8e6a844a274086bc3876328055b1966164c0a80b6484302"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-6m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6M Meaning of credit and amount of credit",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 71,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Credit is a contract, arrangement or understanding under which:\n\n(a) payment of a debt owed by one person to another person is\ndeferred; or\n\n(b) one person incurs a debt to another person and defers the\npayment of the debt.\n\n(2) The amount of credit is the amount of the debt that is actually\ndeferred, or that may be deferred, but does not include any fees or\ncharges payable in connection with the deferral of the debt.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (1), credit includes:\n\n(a) a hire-purchase agreement; and\n\n(b) a contract, arrangement or understanding of a kind referred to\nin that subsection that is for the hire, lease or rental of goods,\nor for the supply of services, other than a contract,\narrangement or understanding under which:\n\n(i) full payment is made before, or at the same time as, the\ngoods or services are provided; and\n\n(ii) in the case of goods—an amount greater than, or equal\nto, the value of the goods is paid as a deposit for the\nreturn of the goods."
    },
