    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6P Meaning of credit reporting business",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-6p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A credit reporting business is a business or undertaking that\ninvolves collecting, holding, using or disclosing personal\ninformation about individuals for the purpose of, or for purposes\nincluding the purpose of, providing an entity with information\nabout the credit worthiness of an individual.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the information about the\ncredit worthiness of an individual is:\n\n(a) provided for profit or reward; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) provided, or intended to be provided, for the purposes of\nassessing an application for consumer credit.\n\n(3) In determining whether a business or undertaking carried on by a\ncredit provider is a credit reporting business, disregard the\nprovision of information about the credit worthiness of an\nindividual to a related body corporate by the provider.\n\n(4) Despite subsection (1), a business or undertaking is not a credit\nreporting business if the business or undertaking is included in a\nclass of businesses or undertakings prescribed by the regulations.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A credit reporting business is a business or undertaking that\ninvolves collecting, holding, using or disclosing personal\ninformation about individuals for the purpose of, or for purposes\nincluding the purpose of, providing an entity with information\nabout the credit worthiness of an individual.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the information about the\ncredit worthiness of an individual is:\n\n(a) provided for profit or reward; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) provided, or intended to be provided, for the purposes of\nassessing an application for consumer credit.\n\n(3) In determining whether a business or undertaking carried on by a\ncredit provider is a credit reporting business, disregard the\nprovision of information about the credit worthiness of an\nindividual to a related body corporate by the provider.\n\n(4) Despite subsection (1), a business or undertaking is not a credit\nreporting business if the business or undertaking is included in a\nclass of businesses or undertakings prescribed by the regulations.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6p-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6p-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6p-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6c773f9ad571b2b4ad471629c6b3a5b98c2697e7782709fffe95ab4213466d6f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-6p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6P Meaning of credit reporting business",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 72,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A credit reporting business is a business or undertaking that\ninvolves collecting, holding, using or disclosing personal\ninformation about individuals for the purpose of, or for purposes\nincluding the purpose of, providing an entity with information\nabout the credit worthiness of an individual.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the information about the\ncredit worthiness of an individual is:\n\n(a) provided for profit or reward; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) provided, or intended to be provided, for the purposes of\nassessing an application for consumer credit.\n\n(3) In determining whether a business or undertaking carried on by a\ncredit provider is a credit reporting business, disregard the\nprovision of information about the credit worthiness of an\nindividual to a related body corporate by the provider.\n\n(4) Despite subsection (1), a business or undertaking is not a credit\nreporting business if the business or undertaking is included in a\nclass of businesses or undertakings prescribed by the regulations."
    },
