      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Default information about an individual is information about a\npayment (including a payment that is wholly or partly a payment of\ninterest) that the individual is overdue in making in relation to\nconsumer credit that has been provided by a credit provider to the\nindividual if:\n\n(a) the individual is at least 60 days overdue in making the\npayment; and\n\n(b) the provider has given a written notice to the individual\ninforming the individual of the overdue payment and\nrequesting that the individual pay the amount of the overdue\npayment; and\n\n(c) the provider is not prevented by a statute of limitations from\nrecovering the amount of the overdue payment; and\n\n(d) the amount of the overdue payment is equal to or more than:\n\n(i) $150; or\n\n(ii) such higher amount as is prescribed by the regulations.\nGuarantor defaults",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Default information about an individual is information about a\npayment (including a payment that is wholly or partly a payment of\ninterest) that the individual is overdue in making in relation to\nconsumer credit that has been provided by a credit provider to the\nindividual if:\n\n(a) the individual is at least 60 days overdue in making the\npayment; and\n\n(b) the provider has given a written notice to the individual\ninforming the individual of the overdue payment and\nrequesting that the individual pay the amount of the overdue\npayment; and\n\n(c) the provider is not prevented by a statute of limitations from\nrecovering the amount of the overdue payment; and\n\n(d) the amount of the overdue payment is equal to or more than:\n\n(i) $150; or\n\n(ii) such higher amount as is prescribed by the regulations.\nGuarantor defaults",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6q"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6q-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6q-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8567d71fc08aa9331c2c7723216724cea1b9ea8ed6826884701590d7a2ddf324",
      "skos:note": "Default information about an individual is required to be provided by a credit provider.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-6q-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6Q(1) Meaning of default information",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Default information about an individual is information about a\npayment (including a payment that is wholly or partly a payment of\ninterest) that the individual is overdue in making in relation to\nconsumer credit that has been provided by a credit provider to the\nindividual if:\n\n(a) the individual is at least 60 days overdue in making the\npayment; and\n\n(b) the provider has given a written notice to the individual\ninforming the individual of the overdue payment and\nrequesting that the individual pay the amount of the overdue\npayment; and\n\n(c) the provider is not prevented by a statute of limitations from\nrecovering the amount of the overdue payment; and\n\n(d) the amount of the overdue payment is equal to or more than:\n\n(i) $150; or\n\n(ii) such higher amount as is prescribed by the regulations.\nGuarantor defaults"
    },
    {
