    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6v",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6V Meaning of repayment history information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-6v"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.77",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a credit provider provides consumer credit to an individual, the\nfollowing information about the consumer credit is repayment\nhistory information about the individual:\n\n(a) whether or not the individual has met an obligation to make a\nmonthly payment that is due and payable in relation to the\nconsumer credit;\n\n(b) the day on which the monthly payment is due and payable;\n\n(c) if the individual makes the monthly payment after the day on\nwhich the payment is due and payable—the day on which the\nindividual makes that payment.\n\n(2) The regulations may make provision in relation to:\n\n(a) whether or not an individual has met an obligation to make a\nmonthly payment that is due and payable in relation to\nconsumer credit; and\n\n(b) whether or not a payment is a monthly payment.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a credit provider provides consumer credit to an individual, the\nfollowing information about the consumer credit is repayment\nhistory information about the individual:\n\n(a) whether or not the individual has met an obligation to make a\nmonthly payment that is due and payable in relation to the\nconsumer credit;\n\n(b) the day on which the monthly payment is due and payable;\n\n(c) if the individual makes the monthly payment after the day on\nwhich the payment is due and payable—the day on which the\nindividual makes that payment.\n\n(2) The regulations may make provision in relation to:\n\n(a) whether or not an individual has met an obligation to make a\nmonthly payment that is due and payable in relation to\nconsumer credit; and\n\n(b) whether or not a payment is a monthly payment.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6v-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-6v-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "53957390be43a5fa6bede548adf58ece3f2ec461b26b20ee55516f66674ac848"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-6v",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6V Meaning of repayment history information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 77,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a credit provider provides consumer credit to an individual, the\nfollowing information about the consumer credit is repayment\nhistory information about the individual:\n\n(a) whether or not the individual has met an obligation to make a\nmonthly payment that is due and payable in relation to the\nconsumer credit;\n\n(b) the day on which the monthly payment is due and payable;\n\n(c) if the individual makes the monthly payment after the day on\nwhich the payment is due and payable—the day on which the\nindividual makes that payment.\n\n(2) The regulations may make provision in relation to:\n\n(a) whether or not an individual has met an obligation to make a\nmonthly payment that is due and payable in relation to\nconsumer credit; and\n\n(b) whether or not a payment is a monthly payment.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15"
    },
