    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-19-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19 Guide to this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-19-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "In general, this Part deals with the privacy of information relating\nto credit reporting.\nDivisions 2 and 3 contain rules that apply to credit reporting bodies\nand credit providers in relation to their handling of information\nrelating to credit reporting.\nDivision 4 contains rules that apply to affected information\nrecipients in relation to their handling of their regulated\ninformation.\nDivision 5 deals with complaints to credit reporting bodies or\ncredit providers about acts or practices that may be a breach of\ncertain provisions of this Part or the registered CR code.\nDivision 6 deals with entities that obtain credit reporting\ninformation or credit eligibility information by false pretence, or\nwhen they are not authorised to do so under this Part.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nDivision 7 provides for compensation orders, and other orders, to\nbe made by the Federal Court or Federal Magistrates Court.",
      "skos:definition": "In general, this Part deals with the privacy of information relating\nto credit reporting.\nDivisions 2 and 3 contain rules that apply to credit reporting bodies\nand credit providers in relation to their handling of information\nrelating to credit reporting.\nDivision 4 contains rules that apply to affected information\nrecipients in relation to their handling of their regulated\ninformation.\nDivision 5 deals with complaints to credit reporting bodies or\ncredit providers about acts or practices that may be a breach of\ncertain provisions of this Part or the registered CR code.\nDivision 6 deals with entities that obtain credit reporting\ninformation or credit eligibility information by false pretence, or\nwhen they are not authorised to do so under this Part.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nDivision 7 provides for compensation orders, and other orders, to\nbe made by the Federal Court or Federal Magistrates Court.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-19-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-19-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-19-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-19-2-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-19-2-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-19-2-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9ce0d87babc3e36a1292886060da010f30ded0c2320bfd91687a9f08fabd176c",
      "skos:note": "Rules for credit reporting bodies and providers regarding handling of information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-19-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19 Guide to this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "In general, this Part deals with the privacy of information relating\nto credit reporting.\nDivisions 2 and 3 contain rules that apply to credit reporting bodies\nand credit providers in relation to their handling of information\nrelating to credit reporting.\nDivision 4 contains rules that apply to affected information\nrecipients in relation to their handling of their regulated\ninformation.\nDivision 5 deals with complaints to credit reporting bodies or\ncredit providers about acts or practices that may be a breach of\ncertain provisions of this Part or the registered CR code.\nDivision 6 deals with entities that obtain credit reporting\ninformation or credit eligibility information by false pretence, or\nwhen they are not authorised to do so under this Part.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nDivision 7 provides for compensation orders, and other orders, to\nbe made by the Federal Court or Federal Magistrates Court."
    },
