    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20B(4) Open and transparent management of credit reporting",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20b-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Without limiting subsection (3), the policy of the credit reporting\nbody must contain the following information:\n\n(a) the kinds of credit information that the body collects and how\nthe body collects that information;\n\n(b) the kinds of credit reporting information that the body holds\nand how the body holds that information;\n\n(c) the kinds of personal information that the body usually\nderives from credit information that the body holds;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) the purposes for which the body collects, holds, uses and\ndiscloses credit reporting information;\n\n(e) information about the effect of section 20G (which deals with\ndirect marketing) and how the individual may make a request\nunder subsection (5) of that section;\n\n(f) how an individual may access credit reporting information\nabout the individual that is held by the body and seek the\ncorrection of such information;\n\n(g) information about the effect of section 20T (which deals with\nindividuals requesting the correction of credit information\netc.);\n\n(h) how an individual may complain about a failure of the body\nto comply with this Division or the registered CR code and\nhow the body will deal with such a complaint.\nAvailability of policy etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Without limiting subsection (3), the policy of the credit reporting\nbody must contain the following information:\n\n(a) the kinds of credit information that the body collects and how\nthe body collects that information;\n\n(b) the kinds of credit reporting information that the body holds\nand how the body holds that information;\n\n(c) the kinds of personal information that the body usually\nderives from credit information that the body holds;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) the purposes for which the body collects, holds, uses and\ndiscloses credit reporting information;\n\n(e) information about the effect of section 20G (which deals with\ndirect marketing) and how the individual may make a request\nunder subsection (5) of that section;\n\n(f) how an individual may access credit reporting information\nabout the individual that is held by the body and seek the\ncorrection of such information;\n\n(g) information about the effect of section 20T (which deals with\nindividuals requesting the correction of credit information\netc.);\n\n(h) how an individual may complain about a failure of the body\nto comply with this Division or the registered CR code and\nhow the body will deal with such a complaint.\nAvailability of policy etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20b-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20b-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0ca711672681aa127d9a9f483160b4286261c92b52323ae6f41c4ac2b19b3ca2",
      "skos:note": "The credit reporting body must provide certain information to individuals.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20B(4) Open and transparent management of credit reporting",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Without limiting subsection (3), the policy of the credit reporting\nbody must contain the following information:\n\n(a) the kinds of credit information that the body collects and how\nthe body collects that information;\n\n(b) the kinds of credit reporting information that the body holds\nand how the body holds that information;\n\n(c) the kinds of personal information that the body usually\nderives from credit information that the body holds;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) the purposes for which the body collects, holds, uses and\ndiscloses credit reporting information;\n\n(e) information about the effect of section 20G (which deals with\ndirect marketing) and how the individual may make a request\nunder subsection (5) of that section;\n\n(f) how an individual may access credit reporting information\nabout the individual that is held by the body and seek the\ncorrection of such information;\n\n(g) information about the effect of section 20T (which deals with\nindividuals requesting the correction of credit information\netc.);\n\n(h) how an individual may complain about a failure of the body\nto comply with this Division or the registered CR code and\nhow the body will deal with such a complaint.\nAvailability of policy etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20b-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
