    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20e-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20E(4) Use or disclosure of credit reporting information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20e-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "(4) However, if the credit reporting information is, or was derived\nfrom, repayment history information about the individual, the\ncredit reporting body must not disclose the information under\nparagraph (3)(a) or (f) unless the recipient of the information is:\n\n(a) a credit provider who is a licensee or is prescribed by the\nregulations; or\n\n(b) a mortgage insurer.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) However, if the credit reporting information is, or was derived\nfrom, repayment history information about the individual, the\ncredit reporting body must not disclose the information under\nparagraph (3)(a) or (f) unless the recipient of the information is:\n\n(a) a credit provider who is a licensee or is prescribed by the\nregulations; or\n\n(b) a mortgage insurer.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20e"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20e-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20e-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6737f09aeb919a9ffb25fe80e813d07209369b85982d27fad89d915885ce0c93",
      "skos:note": "Credit reporting body must not disclose repayment history information unless recipient is a credit provider or mortgage insurer."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20e-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20E(4) Use or disclosure of credit reporting information",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "(4) However, if the credit reporting information is, or was derived\nfrom, repayment history information about the individual, the\ncredit reporting body must not disclose the information under\nparagraph (3)(a) or (f) unless the recipient of the information is:\n\n(a) a credit provider who is a licensee or is prescribed by the\nregulations; or\n\n(b) a mortgage insurer.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units."
    },
