    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20g-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20G(2) Use or disclosure of credit reporting information for the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20g-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.87",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the use by the credit reporting\nbody of credit information about the individual for the purposes of\ndirect marketing by, or on behalf of, a credit provider if:\n\n(a) the provider has an Australian link and is a licensee; and\n\n(b) the direct marketing is about consumer credit that the\nprovider provides in Australia; and\n\n(c) the information is not consumer credit liability information,\nor repayment history information, about the individual; and\n\n(d) the body uses the information to assess whether or not the\nindividual is eligible to receive the direct marketing\ncommunications of the credit provider; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(e) the individual has not made a request under subsection (5);\nand\n\n(f) the body complies with any requirements that are set out in\nthe registered CR code.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the use by the credit reporting\nbody of credit information about the individual for the purposes of\ndirect marketing by, or on behalf of, a credit provider if:\n\n(a) the provider has an Australian link and is a licensee; and\n\n(b) the direct marketing is about consumer credit that the\nprovider provides in Australia; and\n\n(c) the information is not consumer credit liability information,\nor repayment history information, about the individual; and\n\n(d) the body uses the information to assess whether or not the\nindividual is eligible to receive the direct marketing\ncommunications of the credit provider; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(e) the individual has not made a request under subsection (5);\nand\n\n(f) the body complies with any requirements that are set out in\nthe registered CR code.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20g"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20g-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20g-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4f5b50f0e4d55a0137894abd3e2f2cd8aa0dbce530d10e726f2896e672af581f",
      "skos:note": "Permits use of credit information for direct marketing by a licensed provider in Australia, under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20g-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20G(2) Use or disclosure of credit reporting information for the",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 87,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the use by the credit reporting\nbody of credit information about the individual for the purposes of\ndirect marketing by, or on behalf of, a credit provider if:\n\n(a) the provider has an Australian link and is a licensee; and\n\n(b) the direct marketing is about consumer credit that the\nprovider provides in Australia; and\n\n(c) the information is not consumer credit liability information,\nor repayment history information, about the individual; and\n\n(d) the body uses the information to assess whether or not the\nindividual is eligible to receive the direct marketing\ncommunications of the credit provider; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(e) the individual has not made a request under subsection (5);\nand\n\n(f) the body complies with any requirements that are set out in\nthe registered CR code."
    },
