    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20H Use or disclosure of pre-screening assessments",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.88",
      "values:originalText": "Use or disclosure by credit reporting bodies\n\n(1) If a credit reporting body makes a pre-screening assessment in\nrelation to direct marketing by, or on behalf of, a credit provider,\nthe body must not use or disclose the assessment.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) the credit reporting body discloses the pre-screening\nassessment for the purposes of the direct marketing by, or on\nbehalf of, the credit provider; and\n\n(b) the recipient of the assessment is an entity (other than the\nprovider) that has an Australian link.\n\n(3) If the credit reporting body discloses the pre-screening assessment\nunder subsection (2), the body must make a written note of that\ndisclosure.\nCivil penalty:\n500 penalty units.\nUse or disclosure by recipients\n\n(4) If the credit reporting body discloses the pre-screening assessment\nunder subsection (2), the recipient must not use or disclose the\nassessment.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) does not apply if the recipient uses the\npre-screening assessment for the purposes of the direct marketing\nby, or on behalf of, the credit provider.\n\n(6) If the recipient uses the pre-screening assessment under\nsubsection (5), the recipient must make a written note of that use.\nCivil penalty:\n500 penalty units.\nInteraction with the Australian Privacy Principles\n\n(7) If the recipient is an APP entity, Australian Privacy Principles 6, 7\nand 8 do not apply to the recipient in relation to a pre-screening\nassessment.",
      "skos:definition": "Use or disclosure by credit reporting bodies\n\n(1) If a credit reporting body makes a pre-screening assessment in\nrelation to direct marketing by, or on behalf of, a credit provider,\nthe body must not use or disclose the assessment.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) the credit reporting body discloses the pre-screening\nassessment for the purposes of the direct marketing by, or on\nbehalf of, the credit provider; and\n\n(b) the recipient of the assessment is an entity (other than the\nprovider) that has an Australian link.\n\n(3) If the credit reporting body discloses the pre-screening assessment\nunder subsection (2), the body must make a written note of that\ndisclosure.\nCivil penalty:\n500 penalty units.\nUse or disclosure by recipients\n\n(4) If the credit reporting body discloses the pre-screening assessment\nunder subsection (2), the recipient must not use or disclose the\nassessment.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) does not apply if the recipient uses the\npre-screening assessment for the purposes of the direct marketing\nby, or on behalf of, the credit provider.\n\n(6) If the recipient uses the pre-screening assessment under\nsubsection (5), the recipient must make a written note of that use.\nCivil penalty:\n500 penalty units.\nInteraction with the Australian Privacy Principles\n\n(7) If the recipient is an APP entity, Australian Privacy Principles 6, 7\nand 8 do not apply to the recipient in relation to a pre-screening\nassessment.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20h-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20h-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20h-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20h-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20h-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c414151c73281d15b3d63120e85971b9a2ce78c7bfd70b5dea79e95e2e070f69"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20H Use or disclosure of pre-screening assessments",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 88,
      "values:originalText": "Use or disclosure by credit reporting bodies\n\n(1) If a credit reporting body makes a pre-screening assessment in\nrelation to direct marketing by, or on behalf of, a credit provider,\nthe body must not use or disclose the assessment.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) the credit reporting body discloses the pre-screening\nassessment for the purposes of the direct marketing by, or on\nbehalf of, the credit provider; and\n\n(b) the recipient of the assessment is an entity (other than the\nprovider) that has an Australian link.\n\n(3) If the credit reporting body discloses the pre-screening assessment\nunder subsection (2), the body must make a written note of that\ndisclosure.\nCivil penalty:\n500 penalty units.\nUse or disclosure by recipients\n\n(4) If the credit reporting body discloses the pre-screening assessment\nunder subsection (2), the recipient must not use or disclose the\nassessment.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) does not apply if the recipient uses the\npre-screening assessment for the purposes of the direct marketing\nby, or on behalf of, the credit provider.\n\n(6) If the recipient uses the pre-screening assessment under\nsubsection (5), the recipient must make a written note of that use.\nCivil penalty:\n500 penalty units.\nInteraction with the Australian Privacy Principles\n\n(7) If the recipient is an APP entity, Australian Privacy Principles 6, 7\nand 8 do not apply to the recipient in relation to a pre-screening\nassessment."
    },
