    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20J Destruction of pre-screening assessment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an entity has possession or control of a pre-screening\nassessment, the entity must destroy the assessment if:\n\n(a) the entity no longer needs the assessment for any purpose for\nwhich it may be used or disclosed under section 20H; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) the entity is not required by or under an Australian law, or a\ncourt/tribunal order, to retain the assessment.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n\n(2) If the entity is an APP entity but not a credit reporting body,\nAustralian Privacy Principle 11.2 does not apply to the entity in\nrelation to the pre-screening assessment.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an entity has possession or control of a pre-screening\nassessment, the entity must destroy the assessment if:\n\n(a) the entity no longer needs the assessment for any purpose for\nwhich it may be used or disclosed under section 20H; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) the entity is not required by or under an Australian law, or a\ncourt/tribunal order, to retain the assessment.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n\n(2) If the entity is an APP entity but not a credit reporting body,\nAustralian Privacy Principle 11.2 does not apply to the entity in\nrelation to the pre-screening assessment.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20j-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6a2a6ac70cbce53fd2bdff881aed8370e0eb21daeec978b6b525abc4df481739"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20J Destruction of pre-screening assessment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an entity has possession or control of a pre-screening\nassessment, the entity must destroy the assessment if:\n\n(a) the entity no longer needs the assessment for any purpose for\nwhich it may be used or disclosed under section 20H; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) the entity is not required by or under an Australian law, or a\ncourt/tribunal order, to retain the assessment.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n\n(2) If the entity is an APP entity but not a credit reporting body,\nAustralian Privacy Principle 11.2 does not apply to the entity in\nrelation to the pre-screening assessment."
    },
