    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20K No use or disclosure of credit reporting information during a",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "ban period\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information\nabout an individual; and\n\n(b) the individual believes on reasonable grounds that the\nindividual has been, or is likely to be, a victim of fraud\n(including identity fraud); and\n\n(c) the individual requests the body not to use or disclose the\ninformation under this Division;\nthen, despite any other provision of this Division, the body must\nnot use or disclose the information during the ban period for the\ninformation.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the individual expressly consents, in writing, to the use or\ndisclosure of the credit reporting information under this\nDivision; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure of the credit reporting information is\nrequired by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal\norder.\nBan period\n\n(3) The ban period for credit reporting information about an individual\nis the period that:\n\n(a) starts when the individual makes a request under\nparagraph (1)(c); and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) ends:\n\n(i) 21 days after the day on which the request is made; or\n\n(ii) if the period is extended under subsection (4)—on the\nday after the extended period ends.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) there is a ban period for credit reporting information about an\nindividual that is held by a credit reporting body; and\n\n(b) before the ban period ends, the individual requests the body\nto extend that period; and\n\n(c) the body believes on reasonable grounds that the individual\nhas been, or is likely to be, a victim of fraud (including\nidentity fraud);\nthe body must:\n\n(d) extend the ban period by such period as the body considers is\nreasonable in the circumstances; and\n\n(e) give the individual written notification of the extension.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n\n(5) A ban period for credit reporting information may be extended\nmore than once under subsection (4).\nNo charge for request etc.\n\n(6) If an individual makes a request under paragraph (1)(c) or (4)(b), a\ncredit reporting body must not charge the individual for the making\nof the request or to give effect to the request.",
      "skos:definition": "ban period\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information\nabout an individual; and\n\n(b) the individual believes on reasonable grounds that the\nindividual has been, or is likely to be, a victim of fraud\n(including identity fraud); and\n\n(c) the individual requests the body not to use or disclose the\ninformation under this Division;\nthen, despite any other provision of this Division, the body must\nnot use or disclose the information during the ban period for the\ninformation.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the individual expressly consents, in writing, to the use or\ndisclosure of the credit reporting information under this\nDivision; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure of the credit reporting information is\nrequired by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal\norder.\nBan period\n\n(3) The ban period for credit reporting information about an individual\nis the period that:\n\n(a) starts when the individual makes a request under\nparagraph (1)(c); and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) ends:\n\n(i) 21 days after the day on which the request is made; or\n\n(ii) if the period is extended under subsection (4)—on the\nday after the extended period ends.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) there is a ban period for credit reporting information about an\nindividual that is held by a credit reporting body; and\n\n(b) before the ban period ends, the individual requests the body\nto extend that period; and\n\n(c) the body believes on reasonable grounds that the individual\nhas been, or is likely to be, a victim of fraud (including\nidentity fraud);\nthe body must:\n\n(d) extend the ban period by such period as the body considers is\nreasonable in the circumstances; and\n\n(e) give the individual written notification of the extension.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n\n(5) A ban period for credit reporting informati",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20k-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20k-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20k-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20k-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20k-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20k-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a061536bf5720b6a0b578ec679fb5df017b4e6f8c57f74dd4bcbf4e3cd1091cc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20k",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20K No use or disclosure of credit reporting information during a",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "ban period\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information\nabout an individual; and\n\n(b) the individual believes on reasonable grounds that the\nindividual has been, or is likely to be, a victim of fraud\n(including identity fraud); and\n\n(c) the individual requests the body not to use or disclose the\ninformation under this Division;\nthen, despite any other provision of this Division, the body must\nnot use or disclose the information during the ban period for the\ninformation.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the individual expressly consents, in writing, to the use or\ndisclosure of the credit reporting information under this\nDivision; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure of the credit reporting information is\nrequired by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal\norder.\nBan period\n\n(3) The ban period for credit reporting information about an individual\nis the period that:\n\n(a) starts when the individual makes a request under\nparagraph (1)(c); and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) ends:\n\n(i) 21 days after the day on which the request is made; or\n\n(ii) if the period is extended under subsection (4)—on the\nday after the extended period ends.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) there is a ban period for credit reporting information about an\nindividual that is held by a credit reporting body; and\n\n(b) before the ban period ends, the individual requests the body\nto extend that period; and\n\n(c) the body believes on reasonable grounds that the individual\nhas been, or is likely to be, a victim of fraud (including\nidentity fraud);\nthe body must:\n\n(d) extend the ban period by such period as the body considers is\nreasonable in the circumstances; and\n\n(e) give the individual written notification of the extension.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n\n(5) A ban period for credit reporting information may be extended\nmore than once under subsection (4).\nNo charge for request etc.\n\n(6) If an individual makes a request under paragraph (1)(c) or (4)(b), a\ncredit reporting body must not charge the individual for the making\nof the request or to give effect to the request."
    },
