    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20L Adoption of government related identifiers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.91",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information\nabout an individual; and\n\n(b) the information is a government related identifier of the\nindividual;\nthe body must not adopt the government related identifier as its\nown identifier of the individual.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the adoption of the government\nrelated identifier is required or authorised by or under an\nAustralian law or a court/tribunal order.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information\nabout an individual; and\n\n(b) the information is a government related identifier of the\nindividual;\nthe body must not adopt the government related identifier as its\nown identifier of the individual.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the adoption of the government\nrelated identifier is required or authorised by or under an\nAustralian law or a court/tribunal order.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20l-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "36a77a073ca62dccea9cd206447e433708f4d76906f09609ac0f176b333ee015"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20L Adoption of government related identifiers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 91,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information\nabout an individual; and\n\n(b) the information is a government related identifier of the\nindividual;\nthe body must not adopt the government related identifier as its\nown identifier of the individual.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the adoption of the government\nrelated identifier is required or authorised by or under an\nAustralian law or a court/tribunal order."
    },
