    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20n",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20N Quality of credit reporting information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20n"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.93",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A credit reporting body must take such steps as are reasonable in\nthe circumstances to ensure that the credit information the body\ncollects is accurate, up-to-date and complete.\n\n(2) A credit reporting body must take such steps as are reasonable in\nthe circumstances to ensure that the credit reporting information\nthe body uses or discloses is, having regard to the purpose of the\nuse or disclosure, accurate, up-to-date, complete and relevant.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsections (1) and (2), a credit reporting body\nmust:\n\n(a) enter into agreements with credit providers that require the\nproviders to ensure that credit information that they disclose\nto the body under section 21D is accurate, up-to-date and\ncomplete; and\n\n(b) ensure that regular audits are conducted by an independent\nperson to determine whether those agreements are being\ncomplied with; and\n\n(c) identify and deal with suspected breaches of those\nagreements.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A credit reporting body must take such steps as are reasonable in\nthe circumstances to ensure that the credit information the body\ncollects is accurate, up-to-date and complete.\n\n(2) A credit reporting body must take such steps as are reasonable in\nthe circumstances to ensure that the credit reporting information\nthe body uses or discloses is, having regard to the purpose of the\nuse or disclosure, accurate, up-to-date, complete and relevant.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsections (1) and (2), a credit reporting body\nmust:\n\n(a) enter into agreements with credit providers that require the\nproviders to ensure that credit information that they disclose\nto the body under section 21D is accurate, up-to-date and\ncomplete; and\n\n(b) ensure that regular audits are conducted by an independent\nperson to determine whether those agreements are being\ncomplied with; and\n\n(c) identify and deal with suspected breaches of those\nagreements.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20n-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20n-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20n-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d5a1a8d19bcd25699d0a5d4b3ca7fcb03562fc7360abe84575ff2b086f4c2d3f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20n",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20N Quality of credit reporting information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 93,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A credit reporting body must take such steps as are reasonable in\nthe circumstances to ensure that the credit information the body\ncollects is accurate, up-to-date and complete.\n\n(2) A credit reporting body must take such steps as are reasonable in\nthe circumstances to ensure that the credit reporting information\nthe body uses or discloses is, having regard to the purpose of the\nuse or disclosure, accurate, up-to-date, complete and relevant.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsections (1) and (2), a credit reporting body\nmust:\n\n(a) enter into agreements with credit providers that require the\nproviders to ensure that credit information that they disclose\nto the body under section 21D is accurate, up-to-date and\ncomplete; and\n\n(b) ensure that regular audits are conducted by an independent\nperson to determine whether those agreements are being\ncomplied with; and\n\n(c) identify and deal with suspected breaches of those\nagreements."
    },
