    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20Q Security of credit reporting information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.94",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information, the\nbody must take such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to\nprotect the information:\n\n(a) from misuse, interference and loss; and\n\n(b) from unauthorised access, modification or disclosure.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a credit reporting body must:\n\n(a) enter into agreements with credit providers that require the\nproviders to protect credit reporting information that is\ndisclosed to them under this Division:\n\n(i) from misuse, interference and loss; and\n\n(ii) from unauthorised access, modification or disclosure;\nand\n\n(b) ensure that regular audits are conducted by an independent\nperson to determine whether those agreements are being\ncomplied with; and\n\n(c) identify and deal with suspected breaches of those\nagreements.\nSubdivision F—Access to, and correction of, information",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information, the\nbody must take such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to\nprotect the information:\n\n(a) from misuse, interference and loss; and\n\n(b) from unauthorised access, modification or disclosure.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a credit reporting body must:\n\n(a) enter into agreements with credit providers that require the\nproviders to protect credit reporting information that is\ndisclosed to them under this Division:\n\n(i) from misuse, interference and loss; and\n\n(ii) from unauthorised access, modification or disclosure;\nand\n\n(b) ensure that regular audits are conducted by an independent\nperson to determine whether those agreements are being\ncomplied with; and\n\n(c) identify and deal with suspected breaches of those\nagreements.\nSubdivision F—Access to, and correction of, information",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20q-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "adc5ad6e56ef114f26fc8f09c37097b2ff31da559c64f0003fc125778815dc27"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20Q Security of credit reporting information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 94,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information, the\nbody must take such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to\nprotect the information:\n\n(a) from misuse, interference and loss; and\n\n(b) from unauthorised access, modification or disclosure.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a credit reporting body must:\n\n(a) enter into agreements with credit providers that require the\nproviders to protect credit reporting information that is\ndisclosed to them under this Division:\n\n(i) from misuse, interference and loss; and\n\n(ii) from unauthorised access, modification or disclosure;\nand\n\n(b) ensure that regular audits are conducted by an independent\nperson to determine whether those agreements are being\ncomplied with; and\n\n(c) identify and deal with suspected breaches of those\nagreements.\nSubdivision F—Access to, and correction of, information"
    },
