    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20q-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20Q(2) Security of credit reporting information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20q-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.94",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a credit reporting body must:\n\n(a) enter into agreements with credit providers that require the\nproviders to protect credit reporting information that is\ndisclosed to them under this Division:\n\n(i) from misuse, interference and loss; and\n\n(ii) from unauthorised access, modification or disclosure;\nand\n\n(b) ensure that regular audits are conducted by an independent\nperson to determine whether those agreements are being\ncomplied with; and\n\n(c) identify and deal with suspected breaches of those\nagreements.\nSubdivision F—Access to, and correction of, information",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a credit reporting body must:\n\n(a) enter into agreements with credit providers that require the\nproviders to protect credit reporting information that is\ndisclosed to them under this Division:\n\n(i) from misuse, interference and loss; and\n\n(ii) from unauthorised access, modification or disclosure;\nand\n\n(b) ensure that regular audits are conducted by an independent\nperson to determine whether those agreements are being\ncomplied with; and\n\n(c) identify and deal with suspected breaches of those\nagreements.\nSubdivision F—Access to, and correction of, information",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20q"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20q-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20q-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b2a26f3794cfd6508725bef4abac396d5d2ca629015ce38b4c2bc7d2411b4826",
      "skos:note": "Protect credit reporting information from misuse, interference, loss, unauthorized access, modification or disclosure."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20q-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20Q(2) Security of credit reporting information",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 94,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a credit reporting body must:\n\n(a) enter into agreements with credit providers that require the\nproviders to protect credit reporting information that is\ndisclosed to them under this Division:\n\n(i) from misuse, interference and loss; and\n\n(ii) from unauthorised access, modification or disclosure;\nand\n\n(b) ensure that regular audits are conducted by an independent\nperson to determine whether those agreements are being\ncomplied with; and\n\n(c) identify and deal with suspected breaches of those\nagreements.\nSubdivision F—Access to, and correction of, information"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20q-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20q-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20q-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must protect credit reporting information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20R Access to credit reporting information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.94",
      "values:originalText": "Access\n\n(1) If a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information about\nan individual, the body must, on request by an access seeker in\nrelation to the information, give the access seeker access to the\ninformation.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nExceptions to access\n\n(2) Despite subsection (1), the credit reporting body is not required to\ngive the access seeker access to the credit reporting information to\nthe extent that:\n\n(a) giving access would be unlawful; or\n\n(b) denying access is required or authorised by or under an\nAustralian law or a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(c) giving access would be likely to prejudice one or more\nenforcement related activities conducted by, or on behalf of,\nan enforcement body.\nDealing with requests for access\n\n(3) The credit reporting body must respond to the request within a\nreasonable period, but not longer than 10 days, after the request is\nmade.\nMeans of access\n\n(4) If the credit reporting body gives access to the credit reporting\ninformation, the access must be given in the manner set out in the\nregistered CR code.\nAccess charges\n\n(5) If a request under subsection (1) in relation to the individual has\nnot been made to the credit reporting body in the previous 12\nmonths, the body must not charge the access seeker for the making\nof the request or for giving access to the information.\n\n(6) If subsection (5) does not apply, any charge by the credit reporting\nbody for giving access to the information must not be excessive\nand must not apply to the making of the request.\nRefusal to give access\n\n(7) If the credit reporting body refuses to give access to the\ninformation because of subsection (2), the body must give the\naccess seeker a written notice that:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) sets out the reasons for the refusal except to the extent that,\nhaving regard to the grounds for the refusal, it would be\nunreasonable to do so; and\n\n(b) states that, if the access seeker is not satisfied with the\nresponse to the request, the access seeker may:\n\n(i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme\nof which the body is a member; or\n\n(ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V.",
      "skos:definition": "Access\n\n(1) If a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information about\nan individual, the body must, on request by an access seeker in\nrelation to the information, give the access seeker access to the\ninformation.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nExceptions to access\n\n(2) Despite subsection (1), the credit reporting body is not required to\ngive the access seeker access to the credit reporting information to\nthe extent that:\n\n(a) giving access would be unlawful; or\n\n(b) denying access is required or authorised by or under an\nAustralian law or a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(c) giving access would be likely to prejudice one or more\nenforcement related activities conducted by, or on behalf of,\nan enforcement body.\nDealing with requests for access\n\n(3) The credit reporting body must respond to the request within a\nreasonable period, but not longer than 10 days, after the request is\nmade.\nMeans of access\n\n(4) If the credit reporting body gives access to the credit reporting\ninformation, the access must be given in the manner set out in the\nregistered CR code.\nAccess charges\n\n(5) If a request under subsection (1) in relation to the individual has\nnot been made to the credit reporting body in the previous 12\nmonths, the body must not charge the access seeker for the making\nof the request or for giving access to the information.\n\n(6) If subsection (5) does not apply, any charge by the credit reporting\nbody for giving access to the information must not be excessive\nand must not apply to the making of the request.\nRefusal to give access\n\n(7) If the credit reporting body refuses to give access to the\ninformation because of subsection (2), the body must give the\naccess seeker a written notice that:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20r-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20r-ss-2"
        },
