    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20r-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20R(7) Access to credit reporting information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20r-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.94",
      "values:originalText": "(7) If the credit reporting body refuses to give access to the\ninformation because of subsection (2), the body must give the\naccess seeker a written notice that:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) sets out the reasons for the refusal except to the extent that,\nhaving regard to the grounds for the refusal, it would be\nunreasonable to do so; and\n\n(b) states that, if the access seeker is not satisfied with the\nresponse to the request, the access seeker may:\n\n(i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme\nof which the body is a member; or\n\n(ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V.",
      "skos:definition": "(7) If the credit reporting body refuses to give access to the\ninformation because of subsection (2), the body must give the\naccess seeker a written notice that:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) sets out the reasons for the refusal except to the extent that,\nhaving regard to the grounds for the refusal, it would be\nunreasonable to do so; and\n\n(b) states that, if the access seeker is not satisfied with the\nresponse to the request, the access seeker may:\n\n(i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme\nof which the body is a member; or\n\n(ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20r"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20r-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20r-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20r-ss-7-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20r-ss-7-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20r-ss-7-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eea7a261e39d0611121b3716d5f7d7081f4395f55ead40cd259b4eaa5f6bac01",
      "skos:note": "Credit reporting body must provide written notice with reasons for refusal of access to information.",
      "dc:description": "written notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20r-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20R(7) Access to credit reporting information",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 94,
      "values:originalText": "(7) If the credit reporting body refuses to give access to the\ninformation because of subsection (2), the body must give the\naccess seeker a written notice that:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) sets out the reasons for the refusal except to the extent that,\nhaving regard to the grounds for the refusal, it would be\nunreasonable to do so; and\n\n(b) states that, if the access seeker is not satisfied with the\nresponse to the request, the access seeker may:\n\n(i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme\nof which the body is a member; or\n\n(ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20r-ss-7-norm",
