      "cml:integrityHash": "4b8fa155fd624f10358cdfc73ab7e78abb3c53837b2ff8aceb251540b3c0ad4e",
      "skos:note": "Consultation with interested parties required for credit reporting information correction Exemption from notice under subsection (2) due to impracticability or legal requirement."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20s-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20S(3) Correction of credit reporting information",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if:\n\n(a) it is impracticable for the credit reporting body to give the\nnotice under that subsection; or\n\n(b) the credit reporting body is required by or under an\nAustralian law, or a court/tribunal order, not to give the\nnotice under that subsection.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n20T  Individual may request the correction of credit information etc.\nRequest"
    },
