    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20s-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20S(2) Correction of credit reporting information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20s-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the credit reporting body is satisfied that the personal\ninformation is inaccurate, out-of-date, incomplete, irrelevant or\nmisleading, the body must take such steps (if any) as are\nreasonable in the circumstances to correct the information within:\n\n(a) the period of 30 days that starts on the day on which the\nrequest is made; or\n\n(b) such longer period as the individual has agreed to in writing.\nConsultation",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If the credit reporting body is satisfied that the personal\ninformation is inaccurate, out-of-date, incomplete, irrelevant or\nmisleading, the body must take such steps (if any) as are\nreasonable in the circumstances to correct the information within:\n\n(a) the period of 30 days that starts on the day on which the\nrequest is made; or\n\n(b) such longer period as the individual has agreed to in writing.\nConsultation",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20s"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20s-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20s-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f7ec78ae49a3c7dc3c874d6b8457bb4607310441b6ad94e585f77ea45739d299",
      "skos:note": "Credit reporting body must correct inaccurate information within a specified period. Body must provide written notice of correction within a reasonable period.",
      "dc:description": "written notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20s-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20S(2) Correction of credit reporting information",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the credit reporting body is satisfied that the personal\ninformation is inaccurate, out-of-date, incomplete, irrelevant or\nmisleading, the body must take such steps (if any) as are\nreasonable in the circumstances to correct the information within:\n\n(a) the period of 30 days that starts on the day on which the\nrequest is made; or\n\n(b) such longer period as the individual has agreed to in writing.\nConsultation"
    },
