    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20y-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20Y(2) Destruction of credit reporting information in cases of fraud",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20y-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.103",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The credit reporting body must:\n\n(a) destroy the credit reporting information; and\n\n(b) within a reasonable period after the information is destroyed:\n\n(i) give the individual a written notice that states that the\ninformation has been destroyed and sets out the effect of\nsubsection (4); and\n\n(ii) give the credit provider a written notice that states that\nthe information has been destroyed.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The credit reporting body must:\n\n(a) destroy the credit reporting information; and\n\n(b) within a reasonable period after the information is destroyed:\n\n(i) give the individual a written notice that states that the\ninformation has been destroyed and sets out the effect of\nsubsection (4); and\n\n(ii) give the credit provider a written notice that states that\nthe information has been destroyed.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20y"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20y-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-20y-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9c5a3b7baba63e3da0e96494a7565503f1a598e16c9ae2f5ee2f81588788cb25",
      "skos:note": "Credit reporting body must destroy information and notify parties.",
      "dc:description": "Written notices to individual and credit provider."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-20y-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20Y(2) Destruction of credit reporting information in cases of fraud",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 103,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The credit reporting body must:\n\n(a) destroy the credit reporting information; and\n\n(b) within a reasonable period after the information is destroyed:\n\n(i) give the individual a written notice that states that the\ninformation has been destroyed and sets out the effect of\nsubsection (4); and\n\n(ii) give the credit provider a written notice that states that\nthe information has been destroyed.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units."
    },
    {
