      "cof:title": "20ZA(4) Dealing with information if an Australian law etc. requires it",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 106,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the credit reporting body uses or discloses the information under\nsubsection (3), the body must make a written note of the use or\ndisclosure.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nCivil penalty:\n500 penalty units.\nOther requirements"
    },
