    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Guide to this Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.107",
      "values:originalText": "This Division sets out rules that apply to credit providers in\nrelation to their handling of the following:\n\n(a)\ncredit information;\n\n(b)\ncredit eligibility information;\n\n(c)\nCRB derived information.\nIf a credit provider is an APP entity, the rules apply in relation to\nthat information in addition to, or instead of, any relevant\nAustralian Privacy Principles.",
      "skos:definition": "This Division sets out rules that apply to credit providers in\nrelation to their handling of the following:\n\n(a)\ncredit information;\n\n(b)\ncredit eligibility information;\n\n(c)\nCRB derived information.\nIf a credit provider is an APP entity, the rules apply in relation to\nthat information in addition to, or instead of, any relevant\nAustralian Privacy Principles.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6abfdd5166c2b8906622ed8d348d72d81a4318a68adfe2b3b417ffa28551707c",
      "skos:note": "Rules for credit providers' handling of credit information, eligibility information, and CRB-derived information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Guide to this Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 107,
      "values:originalText": "This Division sets out rules that apply to credit providers in\nrelation to their handling of the following:\n\n(a)\ncredit information;\n\n(b)\ncredit eligibility information;\n\n(c)\nCRB derived information.\nIf a credit provider is an APP entity, the rules apply in relation to\nthat information in addition to, or instead of, any relevant\nAustralian Privacy Principles."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to handle credit information correctly",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21A Application of this Division to credit providers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.107",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Division applies to a credit provider in relation to the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) credit information;\n\n(b) credit eligibility information;\n\n(c) CRB derived information.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) If the credit provider is an APP entity, this Division may apply to\nthe provider in relation to information referred to in subsection (1)\nin addition to, or instead of, the Australian Privacy Principles.\nSubdivision B—Consideration of information privacy\n21B  Open and transparent management of credit information etc.\n\n(1) The object of this section is to ensure that credit providers manage\ncredit information and credit eligibility information in an open and\ntransparent way.\nCompliance with this Division etc.\n\n(2) A credit provider must take such steps as are reasonable in the\ncircumstances to implement practices, procedures and systems\nrelating to the provider’s functions or activities as a credit provider\nthat:\n\n(a) will ensure that the provider complies with this Division and\nthe registered CR code if it binds the provider; and\n\n(b) will enable the provider to deal with inquiries or complaints\nfrom individuals about the provider’s compliance with this\nDivision or the registered CR code if it binds the provider.\nPolicy about the management of credit information etc.\n\n(3) A credit provider must have a clearly expressed and up-to-date\npolicy about the management of credit information and credit\neligibility information by the provider.\n\n(4) Without limiting subsection (3), the policy of the credit provider\nmust contain the following information:\n\n(a) the kinds of credit information that the provider collects and\nholds, and how the provider collects and holds that\ninformation;\n\n(b) the kinds of credit eligibility information that the provider\nholds and how the provider holds that information;\n\n(c) the kinds of CP derived information that the provider usually\nderives from credit reporting information disclosed to the\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nprovider by a credit reporting body under Division 2 of this\nPart;\n\n(d) the purposes for which the provider collects, holds, uses and\ndiscloses credit information and credit eligibility information;\n\n(e) how an individual may access credit eligibility information\nabout the individual that is held by the provider;\n\n(f) how an individual may seek the correction of credit\ninformation or credit eligibility information about the\nindividual that is held by the provider;\n\n(g) how an individual may complain about a failure of the\nprovider to comply with this Division or the registered CR\ncode if it binds the provider;\n\n(h) how the provider will deal with such a complaint;\n\n(i) whether the provider is likely to disclose credit information\nor credit eligibility information to entities that do not have an\nAustralian link;\n\n(j) if the provider is likely to disclose credit information or\ncredit eligibility information to such entities—the countries\nin which those entities are likely to be located if it is\npracticable to specify those countries in the policy.\nAvailability of policy etc.\n\n(5) A credit provider must take such steps as are reasonable in the\ncircumstances to make the policy available:\n\n(a) free of charge; and\n\n(b) in such form as is appropriate.\nNote:\nA credit provider will usually make the policy available on the\nprovider’s website.\n\n(6) If a person or body requests a copy, in a particular form, of the\npolicy of a credit provider, the provider must take such steps as are\nreasonable in the circumstances to give the person or body a copy\nin that form.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nInteraction with the Australian Privacy Principles\n\n(7) If a credit provider is an APP entity, Australian Privacy Principles",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This Division applies to a credit provider in relation to the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) credit information;\n\n(b) credit eligibility information;\n\n(c) CRB derived information.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) If the credit provider is an APP entity, this Division may apply to\nthe provider in relation to information referred to in subsection (1)\nin addition to, or instead of, the Australian Privacy Principles.\nSubdivision B—Consideration of information privacy\n21B  Open and transparent management of credit information etc.\n\n(1) The object of this section is to ensure that credit providers manage\ncredit information and credit eligibility information in an open and\ntransparent way.\nCompliance with this Division etc.\n\n(2) A credit provider must take such steps as are reasonable in the\ncircumstances to implement practices, procedures and systems\nrelating to the provider’s functions or activities as a credit provider\nthat:\n\n(a) will ensure that the provider complies with this Division and\nthe registered CR code if it binds the provider; and\n\n(b) will enable the provider to deal with inquiries or complaints\nfrom individuals about the provider’s compliance with this\nDivision or the registered CR code if it binds the provider.\nPolicy about the management of credit information etc.\n\n(3) A credit provider must have a clearly expressed and up-to-date\npolicy about the management of credit information and credit\neligibility information by the provider.\n\n(4) Without limiting subsection (3), the policy of the credit provider\nmust contain the following information:\n\n(a) the kinds of credit information that the provider collects and\nholds, and how the provider collects and holds that\ninformation;\n\n(b) the kinds of credit eligibility information that the provider\nholds and how the provider holds that information;\n\n(c) the kinds of CP derived informat",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "66a17a3a0c17b19cd66f203914bea1512dc39e54e09b469598c8bf910407e89f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21A Application of this Division to credit providers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 107,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Division applies to a credit provider in relation to the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) credit information;\n\n(b) credit eligibility information;\n\n(c) CRB derived information.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) If the credit provider is an APP entity, this Division may apply to\nthe provider in relation to information referred to in subsection (1)\nin addition to, or instead of, the Australian Privacy Principles.\nSubdivision B—Consideration of information privacy\n21B  Open and transparent management of credit information etc.\n\n(1) The object of this section is to ensure that credit providers manage\ncredit information and credit eligibility information in an open and\ntransparent way.\nCompliance with this Division etc.\n\n(2) A credit provider must take such steps as are reasonable in the\ncircumstances to implement practices, procedures and systems\nrelating to the provider’s functions or activities as a credit provider\nthat:\n\n(a) will ensure that the provider complies with this Division and\nthe registered CR code if it binds the provider; and\n\n(b) will enable the provider to deal with inquiries or complaints\nfrom individuals about the provider’s compliance with this\nDivision or the registered CR code if it binds the provider.\nPolicy about the management of credit information etc.\n\n(3) A credit provider must have a clearly expressed and up-to-date\npolicy about the management of credit information and credit\neligibility information by the provider.\n\n(4) Without limiting subsection (3), the policy of the credit provider\nmust contain the following information:\n\n(a) the kinds of credit information that the provider collects and\nholds, and how the provider collects and holds that\ninformation;\n\n(b) the kinds of credit eligibility information that the provider\nholds and how the provider holds that information;\n\n(c) the kinds of CP derived information that the provider usually\nderives from credit reporting information disclosed to the\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nprovider by a credit reporting body under Division 2 of this\nPart;\n\n(d) the purposes for which the provider collects, holds, uses and\ndiscloses credit information and credit eligibility information;\n\n(e) how an individual may access credit eligibility information\nabout the individual that is held by the provider;\n\n(f) how an individual may seek the correction of credit\ninformation or credit eligibility information about the\nindividual that is held by the provider;\n\n(g) how an individual may complain about a failure of the\nprovider to comply with this Division or the registered CR\ncode if it binds the provider;\n\n(h) how the provider will deal with such a complaint;\n\n(i) whether the provider is likely to disclose credit information\nor credit eligibility information to entities that do not have an\nAustralian link;\n\n(j) if the provider is likely to disclose credit information or\ncredit eligibility information to such entities—the countries\nin which those entities are likely to be located if it is\npracticable to specify those countries in the policy.\nAvailability of policy etc.\n\n(5) A credit provider must take such steps as are reasonable in the\ncircumstances to make the policy available:\n\n(a) free of charge; and\n\n(b) in such form as is appropriate.\nNote:\nA credit provider will usually make the policy available on the\nprovider’s website.\n\n(6) If a person or body requests a copy, in a particular form, of the\npolicy of a credit provider, the provider must take such steps as are\nreasonable in the circumstances to give the person or body a copy\nin that form.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nInteraction with the Australian Privacy Principles\n\n(7) If a credit provider is an APP entity, Australian Privacy Principles"
    },
