      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to have a policy",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21A(4) Application of this Division to credit providers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21a-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.107",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Without limiting subsection (3), the policy of the credit provider\nmust contain the following information:\n\n(a) the kinds of credit information that the provider collects and\nholds, and how the provider collects and holds that\ninformation;\n\n(b) the kinds of credit eligibility information that the provider\nholds and how the provider holds that information;\n\n(c) the kinds of CP derived information that the provider usually\nderives from credit reporting information disclosed to the\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nprovider by a credit reporting body under Division 2 of this\nPart;\n\n(d) the purposes for which the provider collects, holds, uses and\ndiscloses credit information and credit eligibility information;\n\n(e) how an individual may access credit eligibility information\nabout the individual that is held by the provider;\n\n(f) how an individual may seek the correction of credit\ninformation or credit eligibility information about the\nindividual that is held by the provider;\n\n(g) how an individual may complain about a failure of the\nprovider to comply with this Division or the registered CR\ncode if it binds the provider;\n\n(h) how the provider will deal with such a complaint;\n\n(i) whether the provider is likely to disclose credit information\nor credit eligibility information to entities that do not have an\nAustralian link;\n\n(j) if the provider is likely to disclose credit information or\ncredit eligibility information to such entities—the countries\nin which those entities are likely to be located if it is\npracticable to specify those countries in the policy.\nAvailability of policy etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Without limiting subsection (3), the policy of the credit provider\nmust contain the following information:\n\n(a) the kinds of credit information that the provider collects and\nholds, and how the provider collects and holds that\ninformation;\n\n(b) the kinds of credit eligibility information that the provider\nholds and how the provider holds that information;\n\n(c) the kinds of CP derived information that the provider usually\nderives from credit reporting information disclosed to the\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nprovider by a credit reporting body under Division 2 of this\nPart;\n\n(d) the purposes for which the provider collects, holds, uses and\ndiscloses credit information and credit eligibility information;\n\n(e) how an individual may access credit eligibility information\nabout the individual that is held by the provider;\n\n(f) how an individual may seek the correction of credit\ninformation or credit eligibility information about the\nindividual that is held by the provider;\n\n(g) how an individual may complain about a failure of the\nprovider to comply with this Division or the registered CR\ncode if it binds the provider;\n\n(h) how the provider will deal with such a complaint;\n\n(i) whether the provider is likely to disclose credit information\nor credit eligibility information to entities that do not have an\nAustralian link;\n\n(j) if the provider is likely to disclose credit information or\ncredit eligibility information to such entities—the countries\nin which those entities are likely to be located if it is\npracticable to specify those countries in the policy.\nAvailability of policy etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bd74f7cc3db3fa986e038460d2623e49e9b66c27f1f22347d3d727a788000ac1",
      "skos:note": "Credit provider must provide specific information to individuals about their credit data.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21A(4) Application of this Division to credit providers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 107,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Without limiting subsection (3), the policy of the credit provider\nmust contain the following information:\n\n(a) the kinds of credit information that the provider collects and\nholds, and how the provider collects and holds that\ninformation;\n\n(b) the kinds of credit eligibility information that the provider\nholds and how the provider holds that information;\n\n(c) the kinds of CP derived information that the provider usually\nderives from credit reporting information disclosed to the\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nprovider by a credit reporting body under Division 2 of this\nPart;\n\n(d) the purposes for which the provider collects, holds, uses and\ndiscloses credit information and credit eligibility information;\n\n(e) how an individual may access credit eligibility information\nabout the individual that is held by the provider;\n\n(f) how an individual may seek the correction of credit\ninformation or credit eligibility information about the\nindividual that is held by the provider;\n\n(g) how an individual may complain about a failure of the\nprovider to comply with this Division or the registered CR\ncode if it binds the provider;\n\n(h) how the provider will deal with such a complaint;\n\n(i) whether the provider is likely to disclose credit information\nor credit eligibility information to entities that do not have an\nAustralian link;\n\n(j) if the provider is likely to disclose credit information or\ncredit eligibility information to such entities—the countries\nin which those entities are likely to be located if it is\npracticable to specify those countries in the policy.\nAvailability of policy etc."
    },
    {
