    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21c-ss-2-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Applicable",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to notify APP entity",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) If a credit provider is an APP entity, subsection (1) applies to the provider in relation to personal information in addition to Australian Privacy Principle 5.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The credit provider must notify other parties of its status as an APP entity."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21c-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21C(3) Additional notification requirements for the collection of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21c-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.110",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If a credit provider is an APP entity, then the matters for the\npurposes of Australian Privacy Principle 5.1 include the following\nmatters to the extent that the personal information referred to in\nthat principle is credit information or credit eligibility information:\n\n(a) that the policy (the credit reporting policy) of the provider\nthat is referred to in subsection 21B(3) contains information\nabout how an individual may access the credit eligibility\ninformation about the individual that is held by the provider;\n\n(b) that the credit reporting policy of the provider contains\ninformation about how an individual may seek the correction\nof credit information or credit eligibility information about\nthe individual that is held by the provider;\n\n(c) that the credit reporting policy of the provider contains\ninformation about how an individual may complain about a\nfailure of the provider to comply with this Division or the\nregistered CR code if it binds the provider;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) that the credit reporting policy of the provider contains\ninformation about how the provider will deal with such a\ncomplaint;\n\n(e) whether the provider is likely to disclose credit information\nor credit eligibility information to entities that do not have an\nAustralian link;\n\n(f) if the provider is likely to disclose credit information or\ncredit eligibility information to such entities—the countries\nin which those entities are likely to be located if it is\npracticable to specify those countries in the credit reporting\npolicy.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If a credit provider is an APP entity, then the matters for the\npurposes of Australian Privacy Principle 5.1 include the following\nmatters to the extent that the personal information referred to in\nthat principle is credit information or credit eligibility information:\n\n(a) that the policy (the credit reporting policy) of the provider\nthat is referred to in subsection 21B(3) contains information\nabout how an individual may access the credit eligibility\ninformation about the individual that is held by the provider;\n\n(b) that the credit reporting policy of the provider contains\ninformation about how an individual may seek the correction\nof credit information or credit eligibility information about\nthe individual that is held by the provider;\n\n(c) that the credit reporting policy of the provider contains\ninformation about how an individual may complain about a\nfailure of the provider to comply with this Division or the\nregistered CR code if it binds the provider;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) that the credit reporting policy of the provider contains\ninformation about how the provider will deal with such a\ncomplaint;\n\n(e) whether the provider is likely to disclose credit information\nor credit eligibility information to entities that do not have an\nAustralian link;\n\n(f) if the provider is likely to disclose credit information or\ncredit eligibility information to such entities—the countries\nin which those entities are likely to be located if it is\npracticable to specify those countries in the credit reporting\npolicy.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21c-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21c-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f4f3a81f0d51bd106089ec4fb3849468b1f4fd26b6c46bbd460e9fe40c8d4403",
      "skos:note": "Credit provider must notify about credit reporting policy and procedures.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21c-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21C(3) Additional notification requirements for the collection of",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 110,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If a credit provider is an APP entity, then the matters for the\npurposes of Australian Privacy Principle 5.1 include the following\nmatters to the extent that the personal information referred to in\nthat principle is credit information or credit eligibility information:\n\n(a) that the policy (the credit reporting policy) of the provider\nthat is referred to in subsection 21B(3) contains information\nabout how an individual may access the credit eligibility\ninformation about the individual that is held by the provider;\n\n(b) that the credit reporting policy of the provider contains\ninformation about how an individual may seek the correction\nof credit information or credit eligibility information about\nthe individual that is held by the provider;\n\n(c) that the credit reporting policy of the provider contains\ninformation about how an individual may complain about a\nfailure of the provider to comply with this Division or the\nregistered CR code if it binds the provider;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) that the credit reporting policy of the provider contains\ninformation about how the provider will deal with such a\ncomplaint;\n\n(e) whether the provider is likely to disclose credit information\nor credit eligibility information to entities that do not have an\nAustralian link;\n\n(f) if the provider is likely to disclose credit information or\ncredit eligibility information to such entities—the countries\nin which those entities are likely to be located if it is\npracticable to specify those countries in the credit reporting\npolicy."
    },
