    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21E Payment information must be disclosed to a credit reporting",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.113",
      "values:originalText": "body\n\nIf:\n\n(a) a credit provider has disclosed default information about an\nindividual to a credit reporting body under section 21D; and\n\n(b) after the default information was disclosed, the amount of the\noverdue payment to which the information relates is paid;\nthe provider must, within a reasonable period after the amount is\npaid, disclose payment information about the amount to the body\nunder that section.\nCivil penalty:\n500 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "body\n\nIf:\n\n(a) a credit provider has disclosed default information about an\nindividual to a credit reporting body under section 21D; and\n\n(b) after the default information was disclosed, the amount of the\noverdue payment to which the information relates is paid;\nthe provider must, within a reasonable period after the amount is\npaid, disclose payment information about the amount to the body\nunder that section.\nCivil penalty:\n500 penalty units.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21e-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21e-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ca5e0aed35fca6a5f3d7bfcc3bfc15b2987ca2e62f6fd6c766ba8655f71dc916",
      "skos:note": "Credit provider must disclose payment information after overdue payment is made.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21E Payment information must be disclosed to a credit reporting",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 113,
      "values:originalText": "body\n\nIf:\n\n(a) a credit provider has disclosed default information about an\nindividual to a credit reporting body under section 21D; and\n\n(b) after the default information was disclosed, the amount of the\noverdue payment to which the information relates is paid;\nthe provider must, within a reasonable period after the amount is\npaid, disclose payment information about the amount to the body\nunder that section.\nCivil penalty:\n500 penalty units."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21e-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21e"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21e-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide payment information",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21F Limitation on the disclosure of credit information during a ban",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.113",
      "values:originalText": "period\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information\nabout an individual; and\n\n(b) a credit provider requests the body to disclose the\ninformation to the provider for the purpose of assessing an\napplication for consumer credit made to the provider by the\nindividual, or a person purporting to be the individual; and\n\n(c) the body is not permitted to disclose the information because\nthere is a ban period for the information; and\n\n(d) during the ban period, the provider provides the consumer\ncredit to which the application relates to the individual, or the\nperson purporting to be the individual.\n\n(2) If the credit provider holds credit information about the individual\nthat relates to the consumer credit, the provider must not, despite\nsections 21D and 21E, disclose the information to a credit\nreporting body.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the credit provider has taken such\nsteps as are reasonable in the circumstances to verify the identity of\nthe individual.\nSubdivision D—Dealing with credit eligibility information etc.",
      "skos:definition": "period\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information\nabout an individual; and\n\n(b) a credit provider requests the body to disclose the\ninformation to the provider for the purpose of assessing an\napplication for consumer credit made to the provider by the\nindividual, or a person purporting to be the individual; and\n\n(c) the body is not permitted to disclose the information because\nthere is a ban period for the information; and\n\n(d) during the ban period, the provider provides the consumer\ncredit to which the application relates to the individual, or the\nperson purporting to be the individual.\n\n(2) If the credit provider holds credit information about the individual\nthat relates to the consumer credit, the provider must not, despite\nsections 21D and 21E, disclose the information to a credit\nreporting body.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the credit provider has taken such\nsteps as are reasonable in the circumstances to verify the identity of\nthe individual.\nSubdivision D—Dealing with credit eligibility information etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21f-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "514cb13f603464f97849ba88d2d4f9698003a9323de9b7a3d162ef76f6998122"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21F Limitation on the disclosure of credit information during a ban",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 113,
      "values:originalText": "period\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information\nabout an individual; and\n\n(b) a credit provider requests the body to disclose the\ninformation to the provider for the purpose of assessing an\napplication for consumer credit made to the provider by the\nindividual, or a person purporting to be the individual; and\n\n(c) the body is not permitted to disclose the information because\nthere is a ban period for the information; and\n\n(d) during the ban period, the provider provides the consumer\ncredit to which the application relates to the individual, or the\nperson purporting to be the individual.\n\n(2) If the credit provider holds credit information about the individual\nthat relates to the consumer credit, the provider must not, despite\nsections 21D and 21E, disclose the information to a credit\nreporting body.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the credit provider has taken such\nsteps as are reasonable in the circumstances to verify the identity of\nthe individual.\nSubdivision D—Dealing with credit eligibility information etc."
    },
