    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21H Permitted CP uses in relation to individuals",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "A use by a credit provider of credit eligibility information about an\nindividual is a permitted CP use in relation to the individual if:\n\n(a) the relevant credit reporting information was disclosed to the\nprovider under a provision specified in column 1 of the table\nfor the purpose (if any) specified in that column; and\n\n(b) the provider uses the credit eligibility information for the\npurpose specified in column 2 of the table.\n\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nPermitted CP uses\n\nColumn 1\nColumn 2\nItem\nThe relevant credit reporting\ninformation was disclosed to the\ncredit provider under ...\nThe credit provider uses the credit\neligibility information for ...\nitem 1 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for the purpose of\nassessing an application for\nconsumer credit made by the\nindividual to the provider.\n(a) a securitisation related purpose of\nthe provider in relation to the\nindividual; or\n(b) the internal management purposes\nof the provider that are directly\nrelated to the provision or\nmanagement of consumer credit by\nthe provider.\nitem 2 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for a particular\ncommercial credit related purpose\nof the provider in relation to the\nindividual.\nthat particular commercial credit\nrelated purpose.\n\nitem 2 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for the purpose of\nassessing an application for\ncommercial credit made by a\nperson to the provider.\nthe internal management purposes of\nthe provider that are directly related to\nthe provision or management of\ncommercial credit by the provider.\nitem 3 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for a credit guarantee\npurpose of the provider in relation\nto the individual.\n(a) the credit guarantee purpose; or\n(b) the internal management purposes\nof the provider that are directly\nrelated to the provision or\nmanagement of any credit by the\nprovider.\nitem 5 of the table in subsection\n20F(1).\nthe purpose of assisting the individual\nto avoid defaulting on his or her\nobligations in relation to consumer\ncredit provided by the provider to the\nindividual.\nitem 6 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for a particular\nsecuritisation related purpose of\nthe provider in relation to the\nindividual.\nthat particular securitisation related\npurpose.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "skos:definition": "A use by a credit provider of credit eligibility information about an\nindividual is a permitted CP use in relation to the individual if:\n\n(a) the relevant credit reporting information was disclosed to the\nprovider under a provision specified in column 1 of the table\nfor the purpose (if any) specified in that column; and\n\n(b) the provider uses the credit eligibility information for the\npurpose specified in column 2 of the table.\n\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nPermitted CP uses\n\nColumn 1\nColumn 2\nItem\nThe relevant credit reporting\ninformation was disclosed to the\ncredit provider under ...\nThe credit provider uses the credit\neligibility information for ...\nitem 1 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for the purpose of\nassessing an application for\nconsumer credit made by the\nindividual to the provider.\n(a) a securitisation related purpose of\nthe provider in relation to the\nindividual; or\n(b) the internal management purposes\nof the provider that are directly\nrelated to the provision or\nmanagement of consumer credit by\nthe provider.\nitem 2 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for a particular\ncommercial credit related purpose\nof the provider in relation to the\nindividual.\nthat particular commercial credit\nrelated purpose.\n\nitem 2 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for the purpose of\nassessing an application for\ncommercial credit made by a\nperson to the provider.\nthe internal management purposes of\nthe provider that are directly related to\nthe provision or management of\ncommercial credit by the provider.\nitem 3 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for a credit guarantee\npurpose of the provider in relation\nto the individual.\n(a) the credit guarantee purpose; or\n(b) the internal management purposes\nof the provider that are directly\nrelated to the provision or\nmanagement of any credit by the\nprovider.\nitem 5 of the table in subsection\n20F(1).\nthe",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21h-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21h-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21h-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21h-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21h-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "64dde3b7a66a4917d236c807d20c2e9895919cd7a70496cf8574ea140bc440c1",
      "skos:note": "Permitted CP uses in relation to individuals"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21H Permitted CP uses in relation to individuals",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "A use by a credit provider of credit eligibility information about an\nindividual is a permitted CP use in relation to the individual if:\n\n(a) the relevant credit reporting information was disclosed to the\nprovider under a provision specified in column 1 of the table\nfor the purpose (if any) specified in that column; and\n\n(b) the provider uses the credit eligibility information for the\npurpose specified in column 2 of the table.\n\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nPermitted CP uses\n\nColumn 1\nColumn 2\nItem\nThe relevant credit reporting\ninformation was disclosed to the\ncredit provider under ...\nThe credit provider uses the credit\neligibility information for ...\nitem 1 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for the purpose of\nassessing an application for\nconsumer credit made by the\nindividual to the provider.\n(a) a securitisation related purpose of\nthe provider in relation to the\nindividual; or\n(b) the internal management purposes\nof the provider that are directly\nrelated to the provision or\nmanagement of consumer credit by\nthe provider.\nitem 2 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for a particular\ncommercial credit related purpose\nof the provider in relation to the\nindividual.\nthat particular commercial credit\nrelated purpose.\n\nitem 2 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for the purpose of\nassessing an application for\ncommercial credit made by a\nperson to the provider.\nthe internal management purposes of\nthe provider that are directly related to\nthe provision or management of\ncommercial credit by the provider.\nitem 3 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for a credit guarantee\npurpose of the provider in relation\nto the individual.\n(a) the credit guarantee purpose; or\n(b) the internal management purposes\nof the provider that are directly\nrelated to the provision or\nmanagement of any credit by the\nprovider.\nitem 5 of the table in subsection\n20F(1).\nthe purpose of assisting the individual\nto avoid defaulting on his or her\nobligations in relation to consumer\ncredit provided by the provider to the\nindividual.\nitem 6 of the table in subsection\n20F(1) for a particular\nsecuritisation related purpose of\nthe provider in relation to the\nindividual.\nthat particular securitisation related\npurpose.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15"
    },
