    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21j-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21J(3) Permitted CP disclosures between credit providers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21j-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.118",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information\nabout an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the\nindividual if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is to a person who:\n\n(i) is a guarantor in relation to credit provided by the\nprovider to the individual; or\n\n(ii) has provided property as security for such credit; and\n\n(b) the person has an Australian link; and\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) the individual expressly consents to the disclosure of the\ninformation to the person; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(ii) if subparagraph (a)(i) applies—the information is\ndisclosed to the person for a purpose related to the\nenforcement, or proposed enforcement, of the guarantee.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information\nabout an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the\nindividual if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is to a person who:\n\n(i) is a guarantor in relation to credit provided by the\nprovider to the individual; or\n\n(ii) has provided property as security for such credit; and\n\n(b) the person has an Australian link; and\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) the individual expressly consents to the disclosure of the\ninformation to the person; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(ii) if subparagraph (a)(i) applies—the information is\ndisclosed to the person for a purpose related to the\nenforcement, or proposed enforcement, of the guarantee.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21j"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21j-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21j-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21j-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "47c0d9759e59ede2d673f2a10581bd9bcf0819cd20167874763bc92224b2b3b2",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of credit eligibility information is permitted to certain individuals under specific conditions. Permitted CP disclosures between credit providers"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21j-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21J(3) Permitted CP disclosures between credit providers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 118,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information\nabout an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the\nindividual if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is to a person who:\n\n(i) is a guarantor in relation to credit provided by the\nprovider to the individual; or\n\n(ii) has provided property as security for such credit; and\n\n(b) the person has an Australian link; and\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) the individual expressly consents to the disclosure of the\ninformation to the person; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(ii) if subparagraph (a)(i) applies—the information is\ndisclosed to the person for a purpose related to the\nenforcement, or proposed enforcement, of the guarantee."
    },
