      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21l-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permits",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permits disclosure by credit provider",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21M Permitted CP disclosures to debt collectors",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.121",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information\nabout an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the\nindividual if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is to a person or body that carries on a business\nor undertaking that involves the collection of debts on behalf\nof others; and\n\n(c) the information is disclosed to the person or body for the\nprimary purpose of the person or body collecting payments\nthat are overdue in relation to:\n\n(i) consumer credit provided by the provider to the\nindividual; or\n\n(ii) commercial credit provided by the provider to a person;\nand\n\n(d) the information is information of a kind referred to in\nsubsection (2).\nNote:\nSee section 21NA for additional rules about the disclosure of credit\neligibility information under this subsection.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) The information for the purposes of paragraph (1)(d) is:\n\n(a) identification information about the individual; or\n\n(b) court proceedings information about the individual; or\n\n(c) personal insolvency information about the individual; or\n\n(d) if subparagraph (1)(c)(i) applies—default information about\nthe individual if:\n\n(i) the information relates to a payment that the individual\nis overdue in making in relation to consumer credit that\nhas been provided by the credit provider to the\nindividual; and\n\n(ii) the provider does not hold, or has not held, payment\ninformation about the individual that relates to that\noverdue payment.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information\nabout an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the\nindividual if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is to a person or body that carries on a business\nor undertaking that involves the collection of debts on behalf\nof others; and\n\n(c) the information is disclosed to the person or body for the\nprimary purpose of the person or body collecting payments\nthat are overdue in relation to:\n\n(i) consumer credit provided by the provider to the\nindividual; or\n\n(ii) commercial credit provided by the provider to a person;\nand\n\n(d) the information is information of a kind referred to in\nsubsection (2).\nNote:\nSee section 21NA for additional rules about the disclosure of credit\neligibility information under this subsection.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) The information for the purposes of paragraph (1)(d) is:\n\n(a) identification information about the individual; or\n\n(b) court proceedings information about the individual; or\n\n(c) personal insolvency information about the individual; or\n\n(d) if subparagraph (1)(c)(i) applies—default information about\nthe individual if:\n\n(i) the information relates to a payment that the individual\nis overdue in making in relation to consumer credit that\nhas been provided by the credit provider to the\nindividual; and\n\n(ii) the provider does not hold, or has not held, payment\ninformation about the individual that relates to that\noverdue payment.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21m-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21m-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "70e10544eeecba0668d003f5ac28bc9025360ff5c8c2d1294060dbccf7ea4984"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21M Permitted CP disclosures to debt collectors",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 121,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A disclosure by a credit provider of credit eligibility information\nabout an individual is a permitted CP disclosure in relation to the\nindividual if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is to a person or body that carries on a business\nor undertaking that involves the collection of debts on behalf\nof others; and\n\n(c) the information is disclosed to the person or body for the\nprimary purpose of the person or body collecting payments\nthat are overdue in relation to:\n\n(i) consumer credit provided by the provider to the\nindividual; or\n\n(ii) commercial credit provided by the provider to a person;\nand\n\n(d) the information is information of a kind referred to in\nsubsection (2).\nNote:\nSee section 21NA for additional rules about the disclosure of credit\neligibility information under this subsection.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) The information for the purposes of paragraph (1)(d) is:\n\n(a) identification information about the individual; or\n\n(b) court proceedings information about the individual; or\n\n(c) personal insolvency information about the individual; or\n\n(d) if subparagraph (1)(c)(i) applies—default information about\nthe individual if:\n\n(i) the information relates to a payment that the individual\nis overdue in making in relation to consumer credit that\nhas been provided by the credit provider to the\nindividual; and\n\n(ii) the provider does not hold, or has not held, payment\ninformation about the individual that relates to that\noverdue payment."
    },
