    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21p-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21P(2) Notification of a refusal of an application for consumer credit",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21p-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.125",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The credit provider must, within a reasonable period after refusing\nthe application, give the individual a written notice that:\n\n(a) states that the application has been refused; and\n\n(b) states that the refusal is based wholly or partly on credit\neligibility information about one or more of the persons\nreferred to in paragraph (1)(b); and\n\n(c) if that information is about the individual—sets out:\n\n(i) the name and contact details of the credit reporting body\nthat disclosed the relevant credit reporting information\nto the provider; and\n\n(ii) any other matter specified in the registered CR code.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nSubdivision E—Integrity of credit information and credit\neligibility information",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The credit provider must, within a reasonable period after refusing\nthe application, give the individual a written notice that:\n\n(a) states that the application has been refused; and\n\n(b) states that the refusal is based wholly or partly on credit\neligibility information about one or more of the persons\nreferred to in paragraph (1)(b); and\n\n(c) if that information is about the individual—sets out:\n\n(i) the name and contact details of the credit reporting body\nthat disclosed the relevant credit reporting information\nto the provider; and\n\n(ii) any other matter specified in the registered CR code.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nSubdivision E—Integrity of credit information and credit\neligibility information",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21p"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21p-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21p-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "27319af992057ba7bdd69ffc17c62c91e751ab0d649f8c27d218a356c5e12979",
      "skos:note": "Credit provider must notify individual of refusal with specific details.",
      "dc:description": "written notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21p-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21P(2) Notification of a refusal of an application for consumer credit",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 125,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The credit provider must, within a reasonable period after refusing\nthe application, give the individual a written notice that:\n\n(a) states that the application has been refused; and\n\n(b) states that the refusal is based wholly or partly on credit\neligibility information about one or more of the persons\nreferred to in paragraph (1)(b); and\n\n(c) if that information is about the individual—sets out:\n\n(i) the name and contact details of the credit reporting body\nthat disclosed the relevant credit reporting information\nto the provider; and\n\n(ii) any other matter specified in the registered CR code.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nSubdivision E—Integrity of credit information and credit\neligibility information"
    },
