    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21Q Quality of credit eligibility information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.126",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A credit provider must take such steps (if any) as are reasonable in\nthe circumstances to ensure that the credit eligibility information\nthe provider collects is accurate, up-to-date and complete.\n\n(2) A credit provider must take such steps (if any) as are reasonable in\nthe circumstances to ensure that the credit eligibility information\nthe provider uses or discloses is, having regard to the purpose of\nthe use or disclosure, accurate, up-to-date, complete and relevant.\n\n(3) If a credit provider is an APP entity, Australian Privacy Principle\n10 does not apply to the provider in relation to credit eligibility\ninformation.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A credit provider must take such steps (if any) as are reasonable in\nthe circumstances to ensure that the credit eligibility information\nthe provider collects is accurate, up-to-date and complete.\n\n(2) A credit provider must take such steps (if any) as are reasonable in\nthe circumstances to ensure that the credit eligibility information\nthe provider uses or discloses is, having regard to the purpose of\nthe use or disclosure, accurate, up-to-date, complete and relevant.\n\n(3) If a credit provider is an APP entity, Australian Privacy Principle\n10 does not apply to the provider in relation to credit eligibility\ninformation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21q-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21q-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c2a6c6f98ebfa477af2e7ad67ece37961cc32ae5403306aba285f168dbfab016"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21Q Quality of credit eligibility information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 126,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A credit provider must take such steps (if any) as are reasonable in\nthe circumstances to ensure that the credit eligibility information\nthe provider collects is accurate, up-to-date and complete.\n\n(2) A credit provider must take such steps (if any) as are reasonable in\nthe circumstances to ensure that the credit eligibility information\nthe provider uses or discloses is, having regard to the purpose of\nthe use or disclosure, accurate, up-to-date, complete and relevant.\n\n(3) If a credit provider is an APP entity, Australian Privacy Principle\n10 does not apply to the provider in relation to credit eligibility\ninformation."
    },
