    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21R False or misleading credit information or credit eligibility",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.126",
      "values:originalText": "information\nOffences\n\n(1) A credit provider commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the provider discloses credit information under section 21D;\nand\n\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\n\n(2) A credit provider commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the provider uses or discloses credit eligibility information\nunder this Division; and\n\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nCivil penalties\n\n(3) A credit provider must not disclose credit information under\nsection 21D if the information is false or misleading in a material\nparticular.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(4) A credit provider must not use or disclose credit eligibility\ninformation under this Division if the information is false or\nmisleading in a material particular.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "information\nOffences\n\n(1) A credit provider commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the provider discloses credit information under section 21D;\nand\n\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\n\n(2) A credit provider commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the provider uses or discloses credit eligibility information\nunder this Division; and\n\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nCivil penalties\n\n(3) A credit provider must not disclose credit information under\nsection 21D if the information is false or misleading in a material\nparticular.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(4) A credit provider must not use or disclose credit eligibility\ninformation under this Division if the information is false or\nmisleading in a material particular.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21r-ss-1"
        },
