    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21t-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21T(7) Access to credit eligibility information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21t-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.128",
      "values:originalText": "(7) If the provider refuses to give access to the information because of\nsubsection (2), the provider must give the access seeker a written\nnotice that:\n\n(a) sets out the reasons for the refusal except to the extent that,\nhaving regard to the grounds for the refusal, it would be\nunreasonable to do so; and\n\n(b) states that, if the access seeker is not satisfied with the\nresponse to the request, the access seeker may:\n\n(i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme\nof which the provider is a member; or\n\n(ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V.\nInteraction with the Australian Privacy Principles",
      "skos:definition": "(7) If the provider refuses to give access to the information because of\nsubsection (2), the provider must give the access seeker a written\nnotice that:\n\n(a) sets out the reasons for the refusal except to the extent that,\nhaving regard to the grounds for the refusal, it would be\nunreasonable to do so; and\n\n(b) states that, if the access seeker is not satisfied with the\nresponse to the request, the access seeker may:\n\n(i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme\nof which the provider is a member; or\n\n(ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V.\nInteraction with the Australian Privacy Principles",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21t"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21t-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21t-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "30bd8da9868dd1c3f40f9e0b058c9c016ce9f426e37ea642fc491d177fa7f00d",
      "skos:note": "Provider must give written notice if refusing access to credit eligibility information",
      "dc:description": "written notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21t-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21T(7) Access to credit eligibility information",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 128,
      "values:originalText": "(7) If the provider refuses to give access to the information because of\nsubsection (2), the provider must give the access seeker a written\nnotice that:\n\n(a) sets out the reasons for the refusal except to the extent that,\nhaving regard to the grounds for the refusal, it would be\nunreasonable to do so; and\n\n(b) states that, if the access seeker is not satisfied with the\nresponse to the request, the access seeker may:\n\n(i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme\nof which the provider is a member; or\n\n(ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V.\nInteraction with the Australian Privacy Principles"
    },
