    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21w-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21W(3) Notice of correction etc. must be given",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21w-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the credit provider does not correct the personal information\nunder subsection 21V(2), the provider must, within a reasonable\nperiod, give the individual written notice that:\n\n(a) states that the correction has not been made; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) sets out the provider’s reasons for not correcting the\ninformation (including evidence substantiating the\ncorrectness of the information); and\n\n(c) states that, if the individual is not satisfied with the response\nto the request, the individual may:\n\n(i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme\nof which the provider is a member; or\n\n(ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V.\nExceptions",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If the credit provider does not correct the personal information\nunder subsection 21V(2), the provider must, within a reasonable\nperiod, give the individual written notice that:\n\n(a) states that the correction has not been made; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) sets out the provider’s reasons for not correcting the\ninformation (including evidence substantiating the\ncorrectness of the information); and\n\n(c) states that, if the individual is not satisfied with the response\nto the request, the individual may:\n\n(i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme\nof which the provider is a member; or\n\n(ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V.\nExceptions",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21w"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21w-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-21w-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "17c41a786162382842f4c8f09e9d3a86c4fe87885be8067fa449174478c83416",
      "skos:note": "Correct personal information within a reasonable period",
      "dc:description": "Written notice with reasons for non-correction"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-21w-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21W(3) Notice of correction etc. must be given",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 132,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the credit provider does not correct the personal information\nunder subsection 21V(2), the provider must, within a reasonable\nperiod, give the individual written notice that:\n\n(a) states that the correction has not been made; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) sets out the provider’s reasons for not correcting the\ninformation (including evidence substantiating the\ncorrectness of the information); and\n\n(c) states that, if the individual is not satisfied with the response\nto the request, the individual may:\n\n(i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme\nof which the provider is a member; or\n\n(ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V.\nExceptions"
    },
