      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-22b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22B Additional notification requirements for affected information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-22b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.135",
      "values:originalText": "recipients\n\nIf an affected information recipient is an APP entity, then the\nmatters for the purposes of Australian Privacy Principle 5.1 include\nthe following matters to the extent that the personal information\nreferred to in that principle is regulated information of the\nrecipient:\n\n(a) that the policy (the credit reporting policy) of the recipient\nthat is referred to in subsection 22A(3) contains information\nabout how an individual may access the regulated\ninformation about the individual that is held by the recipient,\nand seek the correction of such information;\n\n(b) that the credit reporting policy of the recipient contains\ninformation about how an individual may complain about a\nfailure of the recipient to comply with this Division or the\nregistered CR code if it binds the recipient; and\n\n(c) that the credit reporting policy of the recipient contains\ninformation about how the recipient will deal with such a\ncomplaint.",
      "skos:definition": "recipients\n\nIf an affected information recipient is an APP entity, then the\nmatters for the purposes of Australian Privacy Principle 5.1 include\nthe following matters to the extent that the personal information\nreferred to in that principle is regulated information of the\nrecipient:\n\n(a) that the policy (the credit reporting policy) of the recipient\nthat is referred to in subsection 22A(3) contains information\nabout how an individual may access the regulated\ninformation about the individual that is held by the recipient,\nand seek the correction of such information;\n\n(b) that the credit reporting policy of the recipient contains\ninformation about how an individual may complain about a\nfailure of the recipient to comply with this Division or the\nregistered CR code if it binds the recipient; and\n\n(c) that the credit reporting policy of the recipient contains\ninformation about how the recipient will deal with such a\ncomplaint.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-22b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-22b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "783d6cc83a55a7c47946a33c9eb18729adf3d6a7ea6138e173f61d7044b64e40",
      "skos:note": "Recipient must provide information about access and complaint procedures",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-22b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22B Additional notification requirements for affected information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 135,
      "values:originalText": "recipients\n\nIf an affected information recipient is an APP entity, then the\nmatters for the purposes of Australian Privacy Principle 5.1 include\nthe following matters to the extent that the personal information\nreferred to in that principle is regulated information of the\nrecipient:\n\n(a) that the policy (the credit reporting policy) of the recipient\nthat is referred to in subsection 22A(3) contains information\nabout how an individual may access the regulated\ninformation about the individual that is held by the recipient,\nand seek the correction of such information;\n\n(b) that the credit reporting policy of the recipient contains\ninformation about how an individual may complain about a\nfailure of the recipient to comply with this Division or the\nregistered CR code if it binds the recipient; and\n\n(c) that the credit reporting policy of the recipient contains\ninformation about how the recipient will deal with such a\ncomplaint."
    },
    {
