    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-22d-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22D(3) Use or disclosure of information by a related body corporate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-22d-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.137",
      "values:originalText": "(3) In determining whether the body corporate would be permitted to\nuse or disclose the information under section 21G, assume that the\nbody is whichever of the following is applicable:\n\n(a) the credit provider that has provided the relevant credit to the\nindividual;\n\n(b) the credit provider to which the relevant application for credit\nwas made by the individual.\nInteraction with the Australian Privacy Principles",
      "skos:definition": "(3) In determining whether the body corporate would be permitted to\nuse or disclose the information under section 21G, assume that the\nbody is whichever of the following is applicable:\n\n(a) the credit provider that has provided the relevant credit to the\nindividual;\n\n(b) the credit provider to which the relevant application for credit\nwas made by the individual.\nInteraction with the Australian Privacy Principles",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-22d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-22d-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-22d-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-22d-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4171fba2052c6d1c3210b46eb46b209b2c1607cfc0e192403cfd12e219963c67",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of information to credit provider or under Australian law is permitted. Permits use or disclosure of information by a related body corporate Disclosure of information is permitted if required or authorised by an Australian law or court/tribunal order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-22d-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22D(3) Use or disclosure of information by a related body corporate",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 137,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In determining whether the body corporate would be permitted to\nuse or disclose the information under section 21G, assume that the\nbody is whichever of the following is applicable:\n\n(a) the credit provider that has provided the relevant credit to the\nindividual;\n\n(b) the credit provider to which the relevant application for credit\nwas made by the individual.\nInteraction with the Australian Privacy Principles"
    },
