      "cml:integrityHash": "8aa0d975bccdccce529daf15a7486ab82e40b414e745dc2e6000797dd35676c1",
      "skos:note": "Prohibition on using or disclosing credit information without consent. Recipient must not use or disclose credit eligibility information. Body corporate must not use or disclose credit eligibility information about an individual."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-22d-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22D(1) Use or disclosure of information by a related body corporate",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 137,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) any of the following (the recipient) holds or held credit\neligibility information about an individual:\n\n(i) an entity;\n\n(ii) a professional legal adviser of the entity;\n\n(iii) a professional financial adviser of the entity; and\n\n(b) the information was disclosed to the recipient by a credit\nprovider under subsection 21N(2);\nthe recipient must not use or disclose the information, or any\npersonal information about the individual derived from that\ninformation.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\nPermitted uses"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-22d-ss-1-norm",
