      "cml:integrityHash": "a1d84566b262ac741e552984893ba059640837d2ec99e18b9f789b51ae3c1c0a",
      "skos:note": "Respondent must make a decision and give written notice to individual within specified period.",
      "dc:description": "written notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-23b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23B(4) Dealing with complaints",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 142,
      "values:originalText": "(4) After investigating the complaint, the respondent must, within the\nperiod referred to in subsection (5), make a decision about the\ncomplaint and give the individual a written notice that:\n\n(a) sets out the decision; and\n\n(b) states that, if the individual is not satisfied with the decision,\nthe individual may:\n\n(i) access a recognised external dispute resolution scheme\nof which the respondent is a member; or\n\n(ii) make a complaint to the Commissioner under Part V."
    },
    {
