    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-24a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24A Obtaining credit eligibility information from a credit provider",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-24a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.145",
      "values:originalText": "Offences\n\n(1) An entity commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the entity obtains credit eligibility information; and\n\n(b) the information is obtained from a credit provider; and\n\n(c) the entity is not:\n\n(i) an entity to which the provider is permitted to disclose\nthe information under Division 3 of this Part; or\n\n(ii) an access seeker for the information.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) An entity commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the entity obtains credit eligibility information; and\n\n(b) the information is obtained from a credit provider; and\n\n(c) the information is obtained by false pretence.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nCivil penalties\n\n(3) An entity must not obtain credit eligibility information from a\ncredit provider if the entity is not:\n\n(a) an entity to which the provider is permitted to disclose the\ninformation under Division 3 of this Part; or\n\n(b) an access seeker for the information.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(4) An entity must not obtain, by false pretence, credit eligibility\ninformation from a credit provider.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "Offences\n\n(1) An entity commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the entity obtains credit eligibility information; and\n\n(b) the information is obtained from a credit provider; and\n\n(c) the entity is not:\n\n(i) an entity to which the provider is permitted to disclose\nthe information under Division 3 of this Part; or\n\n(ii) an access seeker for the information.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) An entity commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the entity obtains credit eligibility information; and\n\n(b) the information is obtained from a credit provider; and\n\n(c) the information is obtained by false pretence.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nCivil penalties\n\n(3) An entity must not obtain credit eligibility information from a\ncredit provider if the entity is not:\n\n(a) an entity to which the provider is permitted to disclose the\ninformation under Division 3 of this Part; or\n\n(b) an access seeker for the information.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(4) An entity must not obtain, by false pretence, credit eligibility\ninformation from a credit provider.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-24a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-24a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-24a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-24a-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "87d390231948a0c49033f78db1046b1c0ea049452008ec1792ea0a263799dcc6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-24a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24A Obtaining credit eligibility information from a credit provider",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 145,
      "values:originalText": "Offences\n\n(1) An entity commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the entity obtains credit eligibility information; and\n\n(b) the information is obtained from a credit provider; and\n\n(c) the entity is not:\n\n(i) an entity to which the provider is permitted to disclose\nthe information under Division 3 of this Part; or\n\n(ii) an access seeker for the information.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 2  Credit reporting\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) An entity commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the entity obtains credit eligibility information; and\n\n(b) the information is obtained from a credit provider; and\n\n(c) the information is obtained by false pretence.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nCivil penalties\n\n(3) An entity must not obtain credit eligibility information from a\ncredit provider if the entity is not:\n\n(a) an entity to which the provider is permitted to disclose the\ninformation under Division 3 of this Part; or\n\n(b) an access seeker for the information.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units.\n\n(4) An entity must not obtain, by false pretence, credit eligibility\ninformation from a credit provider.\nCivil penalty:\n2,000 penalty units."
    },
