    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-25-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25 Compensation orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-25-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.146",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Federal Court or the Federal Magistrates Court may order an\nentity to compensate a person for loss or damage (including injury\nto the person’s feelings or humiliation) suffered by the person if:\n\n(a) either:\n\n(i) a civil penalty order has been made against the entity for\na contravention of a civil penalty provision (other than\nsection 13G); or\n\n(ii) the entity is found guilty of an offence against this Part;\nand\n\n(b) that loss or damage resulted from the contravention or\ncommission of the offence.\nThe order must specify the amount of compensation.\n\n(2) The court may make the order only if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) the person applies for an order under this section; and\n\n(b) the application is made within 6 years of the day the cause of\naction that relates to the contravention or commission of the\noffence accrued.\n\n(3) If the court makes the order, the amount of compensation specified\nin the order that is to be paid to the person may be recovered as a\ndebt due to the person.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Federal Court or the Federal Magistrates Court may order an\nentity to compensate a person for loss or damage (including injury\nto the person’s feelings or humiliation) suffered by the person if:\n\n(a) either:\n\n(i) a civil penalty order has been made against the entity for\na contravention of a civil penalty provision (other than\nsection 13G); or\n\n(ii) the entity is found guilty of an offence against this Part;\nand\n\n(b) that loss or damage resulted from the contravention or\ncommission of the offence.\nThe order must specify the amount of compensation.\n\n(2) The court may make the order only if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) the person applies for an order under this section; and\n\n(b) the application is made within 6 years of the day the cause of\naction that relates to the contravention or commission of the\noffence accrued.\n\n(3) If the court makes the order, the amount of compensation specified\nin the order that is to be paid to the person may be recovered as a\ndebt due to the person.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-25-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-25-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-2-sec-25-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1836f808d00f1253bf7fc114b39860f5494403eafe290fcf465baedd7f4d5d01"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-2-sec-25-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25 Compensation orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 146,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Federal Court or the Federal Magistrates Court may order an\nentity to compensate a person for loss or damage (including injury\nto the person’s feelings or humiliation) suffered by the person if:\n\n(a) either:\n\n(i) a civil penalty order has been made against the entity for\na contravention of a civil penalty provision (other than\nsection 13G); or\n\n(ii) the entity is found guilty of an offence against this Part;\nand\n\n(b) that loss or damage resulted from the contravention or\ncommission of the offence.\nThe order must specify the amount of compensation.\n\n(2) The court may make the order only if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nCredit reporting  Schedule 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) the person applies for an order under this section; and\n\n(b) the application is made within 6 years of the day the cause of\naction that relates to the contravention or commission of the\noffence accrued.\n\n(3) If the court makes the order, the amount of compensation specified\nin the order that is to be paid to the person may be recovered as a\ndebt due to the person."
    },
