    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26 Guide to this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.152",
      "values:originalText": "This Part deals with privacy codes.\nDivision 2 deals with codes of practice about information privacy,\ncalled APP codes. APP code developers or the Commissioner may\ndevelop APP codes, which:\n\n(a)\nmust set out how one or more of the Australian\nPrivacy Principles are to be applied or complied\nwith; and\n\n(b)\nmay impose additional requirements to those\nimposed by the Australian Privacy Principles; and\n\n(c)\nmay deal with other specified matters.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nIf the Commissioner includes an APP code on the Codes Register,\nan APP entity bound by the code must not breach it. A breach of a\nregistered APP code is an interference with the privacy of an\nindividual.\nDivision 3 deals with a code of practice about credit reporting,\ncalled a CR code. CR code developers or the Commissioner may\ndevelop a CR code, which:\n\n(a)\nmust set out how one or more of the provisions of\nPart IIIA are to be applied or complied with; and\n\n(b)\nmust deal with matters required or permitted by\nPart IIIA to be provided for by the registered CR\ncode; and\n\n(c)\nmay deal with other specified matters.\nIf the Commissioner includes a CR code on the Codes Register, an\nentity bound by the code must not breach it. A breach of the\nregistered CR code is an interference with the privacy of an\nindividual.\nDivision 4 deals with the Codes Register, guidelines relating to\ncodes and the review of the operation of registered codes.",
      "skos:definition": "This Part deals with privacy codes.\nDivision 2 deals with codes of practice about information privacy,\ncalled APP codes. APP code developers or the Commissioner may\ndevelop APP codes, which:\n\n(a)\nmust set out how one or more of the Australian\nPrivacy Principles are to be applied or complied\nwith; and\n\n(b)\nmay impose additional requirements to those\nimposed by the Australian Privacy Principles; and\n\n(c)\nmay deal with other specified matters.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nIf the Commissioner includes an APP code on the Codes Register,\nan APP entity bound by the code must not breach it. A breach of a\nregistered APP code is an interference with the privacy of an\nindividual.\nDivision 3 deals with a code of practice about credit reporting,\ncalled a CR code. CR code developers or the Commissioner may\ndevelop a CR code, which:\n\n(a)\nmust set out how one or more of the provisions of\nPart IIIA are to be applied or complied with; and\n\n(b)\nmust deal with matters required or permitted by\nPart IIIA to be provided for by the registered CR\ncode; and\n\n(c)\nmay deal with other specified matters.\nIf the Commissioner includes a CR code on the Codes Register, an\nentity bound by the code must not breach it. A breach of the\nregistered CR code is an interference with the privacy of an\nindividual.\nDivision 4 deals with the Codes Register, guidelines relating to\ncodes and the review of the operation of registered codes.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a064012f9345ca7735457900e93375fe6b5f5b051bfe4a103fd00831b6e592fc",
      "skos:note": "An APP entity must not breach a registered APP code."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26 Guide to this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 152,
      "values:originalText": "This Part deals with privacy codes.\nDivision 2 deals with codes of practice about information privacy,\ncalled APP codes. APP code developers or the Commissioner may\ndevelop APP codes, which:\n\n(a)\nmust set out how one or more of the Australian\nPrivacy Principles are to be applied or complied\nwith; and\n\n(b)\nmay impose additional requirements to those\nimposed by the Australian Privacy Principles; and\n\n(c)\nmay deal with other specified matters.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nIf the Commissioner includes an APP code on the Codes Register,\nan APP entity bound by the code must not breach it. A breach of a\nregistered APP code is an interference with the privacy of an\nindividual.\nDivision 3 deals with a code of practice about credit reporting,\ncalled a CR code. CR code developers or the Commissioner may\ndevelop a CR code, which:\n\n(a)\nmust set out how one or more of the provisions of\nPart IIIA are to be applied or complied with; and\n\n(b)\nmust deal with matters required or permitted by\nPart IIIA to be provided for by the registered CR\ncode; and\n\n(c)\nmay deal with other specified matters.\nIf the Commissioner includes a CR code on the Codes Register, an\nentity bound by the code must not breach it. A breach of the\nregistered CR code is an interference with the privacy of an\nindividual.\nDivision 4 deals with the Codes Register, guidelines relating to\ncodes and the review of the operation of registered codes."
    },
