    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26B What is a registered APP code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.153",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A registered APP code is an APP code:\n\n(a) that is included on the Codes Register; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) that is in force.\n\n(2) A registered APP code is a legislative instrument.\n\n(3) Despite subsection 12(2) of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003, a\nregistered APP code may be expressed to take effect before the\ndate it is registered under that Act.\nNote:\nAn APP code cannot come into force before it is included on the\nCodes Register: see paragraph 26C(2)(c).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A registered APP code is an APP code:\n\n(a) that is included on the Codes Register; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) that is in force.\n\n(2) A registered APP code is a legislative instrument.\n\n(3) Despite subsection 12(2) of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003, a\nregistered APP code may be expressed to take effect before the\ndate it is registered under that Act.\nNote:\nAn APP code cannot come into force before it is included on the\nCodes Register: see paragraph 26C(2)(c).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d0c44fa4fce8c3bbdd70774eba8c7350068ba4c72c1d52a27b221d406555ed8c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26B What is a registered APP code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 153,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A registered APP code is an APP code:\n\n(a) that is included on the Codes Register; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) that is in force.\n\n(2) A registered APP code is a legislative instrument.\n\n(3) Despite subsection 12(2) of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003, a\nregistered APP code may be expressed to take effect before the\ndate it is registered under that Act.\nNote:\nAn APP code cannot come into force before it is included on the\nCodes Register: see paragraph 26C(2)(c)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26b-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
