      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26B(3) What is a registered APP code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26b-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.153",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Despite subsection 12(2) of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003, a\nregistered APP code may be expressed to take effect before the\ndate it is registered under that Act.\nNote:\nAn APP code cannot come into force before it is included on the\nCodes Register: see paragraph 26C(2)(c).",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Despite subsection 12(2) of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003, a\nregistered APP code may be expressed to take effect before the\ndate it is registered under that Act.\nNote:\nAn APP code cannot come into force before it is included on the\nCodes Register: see paragraph 26C(2)(c).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26b-ss-3-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "802c0d9e4d4b7d85b4b6992d5eaa244d812855fa5edd283bf42158cac9a47c8f",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions for registered APP code"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26B(3) What is a registered APP code",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 153,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Despite subsection 12(2) of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003, a\nregistered APP code may be expressed to take effect before the\ndate it is registered under that Act.\nNote:\nAn APP code cannot come into force before it is included on the\nCodes Register: see paragraph 26C(2)(c)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26b-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
