      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26C What is an APP code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.154",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An APP code is a written code of practice about information\nprivacy.\n\n(2) An APP code must:\n\n(a) set out how one or more of the Australian Privacy Principles\nare to be applied or complied with; and\n\n(b) specify the APP entities that are bound by the code, or a way\nof determining the APP entities that are bound by the code;\nand\n\n(c) set out the period during which the code is in force (which\nmust not start before the day the code is registered under\nsection 26H).\n\n(3) An APP code may do one or more of the following:\n\n(a) impose additional requirements to those imposed by one or\nmore of the Australian Privacy Principles, so long as the\nadditional requirements are not contrary to, or inconsistent\nwith, those principles;\n\n(b) cover an act or practice that is exempt within the meaning of\nsubsection 7B(1), (2) or (3);\n\n(c) deal with the internal handling of complaints;\n\n(d) provide for the reporting to the Commissioner about\ncomplaints;\n\n(e) deal with any other relevant matters.\n\n(4) An APP code may be expressed to apply to any one or more of the\nfollowing:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) all personal information or a specified type of personal\ninformation;\n\n(b) a specified activity, or a specified class of activities, of an\nAPP entity;\n\n(c) a specified industry sector or profession, or a specified class\nof industry sectors or professions;\n\n(d) APP entities that use technology of a specified kind.\n\n(5) An APP code is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An APP code is a written code of practice about information\nprivacy.\n\n(2) An APP code must:\n\n(a) set out how one or more of the Australian Privacy Principles\nare to be applied or complied with; and\n\n(b) specify the APP entities that are bound by the code, or a way\nof determining the APP entities that are bound by the code;\nand\n\n(c) set out the period during which the code is in force (which\nmust not start before the day the code is registered under\nsection 26H).\n\n(3) An APP code may do one or more of the following:\n\n(a) impose additional requirements to those imposed by one or\nmore of the Australian Privacy Principles, so long as the\nadditional requirements are not contrary to, or inconsistent\nwith, those principles;\n\n(b) cover an act or practice that is exempt within the meaning of\nsubsection 7B(1), (2) or (3);\n\n(c) deal with the internal handling of complaints;\n\n(d) provide for the reporting to the Commissioner about\ncomplaints;\n\n(e) deal with any other relevant matters.\n\n(4) An APP code may be expressed to apply to any one or more of the\nfollowing:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) all personal information or a specified type of personal\ninformation;\n\n(b) a specified activity, or a specified class of activities, of an\nAPP entity;\n\n(c) a specified industry sector or profession, or a specified class\nof industry sectors or professions;\n\n(d) APP entities that use technology of a specified kind.\n\n(5) An APP code is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26c-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26c-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26c-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e32d21d1f8d33fbc1f8e7ccab3c0c14f9129a823f731934c552496ea01a0f580"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26C What is an APP code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 154,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An APP code is a written code of practice about information\nprivacy.\n\n(2) An APP code must:\n\n(a) set out how one or more of the Australian Privacy Principles\nare to be applied or complied with; and\n\n(b) specify the APP entities that are bound by the code, or a way\nof determining the APP entities that are bound by the code;\nand\n\n(c) set out the period during which the code is in force (which\nmust not start before the day the code is registered under\nsection 26H).\n\n(3) An APP code may do one or more of the following:\n\n(a) impose additional requirements to those imposed by one or\nmore of the Australian Privacy Principles, so long as the\nadditional requirements are not contrary to, or inconsistent\nwith, those principles;\n\n(b) cover an act or practice that is exempt within the meaning of\nsubsection 7B(1), (2) or (3);\n\n(c) deal with the internal handling of complaints;\n\n(d) provide for the reporting to the Commissioner about\ncomplaints;\n\n(e) deal with any other relevant matters.\n\n(4) An APP code may be expressed to apply to any one or more of the\nfollowing:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(a) all personal information or a specified type of personal\ninformation;\n\n(b) a specified activity, or a specified class of activities, of an\nAPP entity;\n\n(c) a specified industry sector or profession, or a specified class\nof industry sectors or professions;\n\n(d) APP entities that use technology of a specified kind.\n\n(5) An APP code is not a legislative instrument."
    },
