    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26D Extension of Act to exempt acts or practices covered by",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.155",
      "values:originalText": "registered APP codes\n\nIf a registered APP code covers an act or practice that is exempt\nwithin the meaning of subsection 7B(1), (2) or (3), this Act applies\nin relation to the code as if that act or practice were not exempt.\nSubdivision B—Development and registration of APP codes",
      "skos:definition": "registered APP codes\n\nIf a registered APP code covers an act or practice that is exempt\nwithin the meaning of subsection 7B(1), (2) or (3), this Act applies\nin relation to the code as if that act or practice were not exempt.\nSubdivision B—Development and registration of APP codes",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26d-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26d-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1a0fc2638fc89ed1909ef8436b402d1c67ae02485911746b300dfc7393a4f96a",
      "skos:note": "This Act applies in relation to the code as if that act or practice were not exempt."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26D Extension of Act to exempt acts or practices covered by",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 155,
      "values:originalText": "registered APP codes\n\nIf a registered APP code covers an act or practice that is exempt\nwithin the meaning of subsection 7B(1), (2) or (3), this Act applies\nin relation to the code as if that act or practice were not exempt.\nSubdivision B—Development and registration of APP codes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26d-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26d"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26d-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If a registered APP code covers an act or practice that is exempt, this Act applies.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "A registered APP code covers an act or practice that is exempt.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "This Act applies in relation to the code as if that act or practice were not exempt."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26E Development of APP codes by APP code developers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.155",
      "values:originalText": "Own initiative\n\n(1) An APP code developer may develop an APP code.\nAt the Commissioner’s request\n\n(2) The Commissioner may, in writing, request an APP code developer\nto develop an APP code, and apply to the Commissioner for the\ncode to be registered, if the Commissioner is satisfied it is in the\npublic interest for the code to be developed.\n\n(3) The request must:\n\n(a) specify the period within which the request must be complied\nwith; and\n\n(b) set out the effect of section 26A.\n\n(4) The period:\n\n(a) must run for at least 120 days from the date the request is\nmade; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) may be extended by the Commissioner.\n\n(5) The request may:\n\n(a) specify one or more matters that the APP code must deal\nwith; and\n\n(b) specify the APP entities, or a class of APP entities, that\nshould be bound by the code.\n\n(6) Despite paragraph (5)(a), the Commissioner must not require an\nAPP code to cover an act or practice that is exempt within the\nmeaning of subsection 7B(1), (2) or (3). However, the APP code\nthat is developed by the APP code developer may cover such an act\nor practice.\n\n(7) The Commissioner must make a copy of the request publicly\navailable as soon as practicable after the request is made.",
      "skos:definition": "Own initiative\n\n(1) An APP code developer may develop an APP code.\nAt the Commissioner’s request\n\n(2) The Commissioner may, in writing, request an APP code developer\nto develop an APP code, and apply to the Commissioner for the\ncode to be registered, if the Commissioner is satisfied it is in the\npublic interest for the code to be developed.\n\n(3) The request must:\n\n(a) specify the period within which the request must be complied\nwith; and\n\n(b) set out the effect of section 26A.\n\n(4) The period:\n\n(a) must run for at least 120 days from the date the request is\nmade; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) may be extended by the Commissioner.\n\n(5) The request may:\n\n(a) specify one or more matters that the APP code must deal\nwith; and\n\n(b) specify the APP entities, or a class of APP entities, that\nshould be bound by the code.\n\n(6) Despite paragraph (5)(a), the Commissioner must not require an\nAPP code to cover an act or practice that is exempt within the\nmeaning of subsection 7B(1), (2) or (3). However, the APP code\nthat is developed by the APP code developer may cover such an act\nor practice.\n\n(7) The Commissioner must make a copy of the request publicly\navailable as soon as practicable after the request is made.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26e-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26e-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26e-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26e-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26e-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e2dbca176244a70ec14555c4d57bb4a543d24d5d53fa1e2e30c8032660dce3c3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26E Development of APP codes by APP code developers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 155,
      "values:originalText": "Own initiative\n\n(1) An APP code developer may develop an APP code.\nAt the Commissioner’s request\n\n(2) The Commissioner may, in writing, request an APP code developer\nto develop an APP code, and apply to the Commissioner for the\ncode to be registered, if the Commissioner is satisfied it is in the\npublic interest for the code to be developed.\n\n(3) The request must:\n\n(a) specify the period within which the request must be complied\nwith; and\n\n(b) set out the effect of section 26A.\n\n(4) The period:\n\n(a) must run for at least 120 days from the date the request is\nmade; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) may be extended by the Commissioner.\n\n(5) The request may:\n\n(a) specify one or more matters that the APP code must deal\nwith; and\n\n(b) specify the APP entities, or a class of APP entities, that\nshould be bound by the code.\n\n(6) Despite paragraph (5)(a), the Commissioner must not require an\nAPP code to cover an act or practice that is exempt within the\nmeaning of subsection 7B(1), (2) or (3). However, the APP code\nthat is developed by the APP code developer may cover such an act\nor practice.\n\n(7) The Commissioner must make a copy of the request publicly\navailable as soon as practicable after the request is made."
    },
    {
