    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26H Commissioner may register APP codes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.157",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an application for registration of an APP code is made under\nsection 26F; or\n\n(b) the Commissioner develops an APP code under section 26G;\nthe Commissioner may register the code by including it on the\nCodes Register.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to register the APP code, the Commissioner\nmay:\n\n(a) consult any person the Commissioner considers appropriate;\nand\n\n(b) consider the matters specified in any relevant guidelines\nmade under section 26V.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(3) If the Commissioner decides not to register an APP code developed\nby an APP code developer, the Commissioner must give written\nnotice of the decision to the developer, including reasons for the\ndecision.\nSubdivision C—Variation and removal of registered APP codes",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an application for registration of an APP code is made under\nsection 26F; or\n\n(b) the Commissioner develops an APP code under section 26G;\nthe Commissioner may register the code by including it on the\nCodes Register.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to register the APP code, the Commissioner\nmay:\n\n(a) consult any person the Commissioner considers appropriate;\nand\n\n(b) consider the matters specified in any relevant guidelines\nmade under section 26V.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(3) If the Commissioner decides not to register an APP code developed\nby an APP code developer, the Commissioner must give written\nnotice of the decision to the developer, including reasons for the\ndecision.\nSubdivision C—Variation and removal of registered APP codes",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26h-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c4fe29200d990b0a06fa31ccd13b76353cef21cdfd7744868404e7a6729f5625"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26H Commissioner may register APP codes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 157,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an application for registration of an APP code is made under\nsection 26F; or\n\n(b) the Commissioner develops an APP code under section 26G;\nthe Commissioner may register the code by including it on the\nCodes Register.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to register the APP code, the Commissioner\nmay:\n\n(a) consult any person the Commissioner considers appropriate;\nand\n\n(b) consider the matters specified in any relevant guidelines\nmade under section 26V.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(3) If the Commissioner decides not to register an APP code developed\nby an APP code developer, the Commissioner must give written\nnotice of the decision to the developer, including reasons for the\ndecision.\nSubdivision C—Variation and removal of registered APP codes"
    },
