    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26J Variation of registered APP codes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may, in writing, approve a variation of a\nregistered APP code:\n\n(a) on his or her own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application by an APP entity that is bound by the code; or\n\n(c) on application by a body or association representing one or\nmore APP entities that are bound by the code.\n\n(2) An application under paragraph (1)(b) or (c) must:\n\n(a) be made in the form and manner specified by the\nCommissioner; and\n\n(b) be accompanied by such information as is specified by the\nCommissioner.\n\n(3) If the Commissioner varies a registered APP code on his or her\nown initiative, then, despite subsection 26C(3)(b), the variation\nmust not deal with an act or practice that is exempt within the\nmeaning of subsection 7B(1), (2) or (3).\n\n(4) Before deciding whether to approve a variation, the Commissioner\nmust:\n\n(a) make a draft of the variation publicly available; and\n\n(b) consult any person the Commissioner considers appropriate\nabout the variation; and\n\n(c)  consider the extent to which members of the public have\nbeen given an opportunity to comment on the variation.\n\n(5) In deciding whether to approve a variation, the Commissioner may\nconsider the matters specified in any relevant guidelines made\nunder section 26V.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(6) If the Commissioner approves a variation of a registered APP code\n(the original code), the Commissioner must:\n\n(a) remove the original code from the Codes Register; and\n\n(b) register the APP code, as varied, by including it on the\nRegister.\n\n(7) If the Commissioner approves a variation, the variation comes into\neffect on the day specified in the approval, which must not be\nbefore the day on which the APP code, as varied, is included on the\nCodes Register.\n\n(8) An approval is not a legislative instrument.\nNote:\nThe APP code, as varied, is a legislative instrument once it is included\non the Codes Register: see section 26B.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may, in writing, approve a variation of a\nregistered APP code:\n\n(a) on his or her own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application by an APP entity that is bound by the code; or\n\n(c) on application by a body or association representing one or\nmore APP entities that are bound by the code.\n\n(2) An application under paragraph (1)(b) or (c) must:\n\n(a) be made in the form and manner specified by the\nCommissioner; and\n\n(b) be accompanied by such information as is specified by the\nCommissioner.\n\n(3) If the Commissioner varies a registered APP code on his or her\nown initiative, then, despite subsection 26C(3)(b), the variation\nmust not deal with an act or practice that is exempt within the\nmeaning of subsection 7B(1), (2) or (3).\n\n(4) Before deciding whether to approve a variation, the Commissioner\nmust:\n\n(a) make a draft of the variation publicly available; and\n\n(b) consult any person the Commissioner considers appropriate\nabout the variation; and\n\n(c)  consider the extent to which members of the public have\nbeen given an opportunity to comment on the variation.\n\n(5) In deciding whether to approve a variation, the Commissioner may\nconsider the matters specified in any relevant guidelines made\nunder section 26V.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(6) If the Commissioner approves a variation of a registered APP code\n(the original code), the Commissioner must:\n\n(a) remove the original code from the Codes Register; and\n\n(b) register the APP code, as varied, by including it on the\nRegister.\n\n(7) If the Commissioner approves a variation, the variation comes into\neffect on the day specified in the approval, which must not be\nbefore the day on which the APP code, as varied, is included on the\nCodes Register.\n\n(8) An approval is not a legislative instrument.\nNote:\nThe APP code, as varied, is a legislative instrument once it is included\non ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26j-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26j-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26j-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26j-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26j-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26j-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26j-ss-8"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1837ffd8bad563f13d171e881aff19018ce44129cacf40a003b8f9a02c5f5486"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26J Variation of registered APP codes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 158,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may, in writing, approve a variation of a\nregistered APP code:\n\n(a) on his or her own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application by an APP entity that is bound by the code; or\n\n(c) on application by a body or association representing one or\nmore APP entities that are bound by the code.\n\n(2) An application under paragraph (1)(b) or (c) must:\n\n(a) be made in the form and manner specified by the\nCommissioner; and\n\n(b) be accompanied by such information as is specified by the\nCommissioner.\n\n(3) If the Commissioner varies a registered APP code on his or her\nown initiative, then, despite subsection 26C(3)(b), the variation\nmust not deal with an act or practice that is exempt within the\nmeaning of subsection 7B(1), (2) or (3).\n\n(4) Before deciding whether to approve a variation, the Commissioner\nmust:\n\n(a) make a draft of the variation publicly available; and\n\n(b) consult any person the Commissioner considers appropriate\nabout the variation; and\n\n(c)  consider the extent to which members of the public have\nbeen given an opportunity to comment on the variation.\n\n(5) In deciding whether to approve a variation, the Commissioner may\nconsider the matters specified in any relevant guidelines made\nunder section 26V.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(6) If the Commissioner approves a variation of a registered APP code\n(the original code), the Commissioner must:\n\n(a) remove the original code from the Codes Register; and\n\n(b) register the APP code, as varied, by including it on the\nRegister.\n\n(7) If the Commissioner approves a variation, the variation comes into\neffect on the day specified in the approval, which must not be\nbefore the day on which the APP code, as varied, is included on the\nCodes Register.\n\n(8) An approval is not a legislative instrument.\nNote:\nThe APP code, as varied, is a legislative instrument once it is included\non the Codes Register: see section 26B."
    },
