    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26K Removal of registered APP codes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.159",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may remove a registered APP code from the\nCodes Register:\n\n(a) on his or her own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application by an APP entity that is bound by the code; or\n\n(c) on application by a body or association representing one or\nmore APP entities that are bound by the code.\n\n(2) An application under paragraph (1)(b) or (c) must:\n\n(a) be made in the form and manner specified by the\nCommissioner; and\n\n(b) be accompanied by such information as is specified by the\nCommissioner.\n\n(3) Before deciding whether to remove the registered APP code, the\nCommissioner must:\n\n(a) consult any person the Commissioner considers appropriate\nabout the proposed removal; and\n\n(b)  consider the extent to which members of the public have\nbeen given an opportunity to comment on the proposed\nremoval.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(4) In deciding whether to remove the registered APP code, the\nCommissioner may consider the matters specified in any relevant\nguidelines made under section 26V.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may remove a registered APP code from the\nCodes Register:\n\n(a) on his or her own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application by an APP entity that is bound by the code; or\n\n(c) on application by a body or association representing one or\nmore APP entities that are bound by the code.\n\n(2) An application under paragraph (1)(b) or (c) must:\n\n(a) be made in the form and manner specified by the\nCommissioner; and\n\n(b) be accompanied by such information as is specified by the\nCommissioner.\n\n(3) Before deciding whether to remove the registered APP code, the\nCommissioner must:\n\n(a) consult any person the Commissioner considers appropriate\nabout the proposed removal; and\n\n(b)  consider the extent to which members of the public have\nbeen given an opportunity to comment on the proposed\nremoval.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(4) In deciding whether to remove the registered APP code, the\nCommissioner may consider the matters specified in any relevant\nguidelines made under section 26V.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26k-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26k-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26k-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26k-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5d439b3d34ce6d29214edb461d4d876cdcc462f7d11c6fb5eec6e14e94913f45"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26k",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26K Removal of registered APP codes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 159,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may remove a registered APP code from the\nCodes Register:\n\n(a) on his or her own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application by an APP entity that is bound by the code; or\n\n(c) on application by a body or association representing one or\nmore APP entities that are bound by the code.\n\n(2) An application under paragraph (1)(b) or (c) must:\n\n(a) be made in the form and manner specified by the\nCommissioner; and\n\n(b) be accompanied by such information as is specified by the\nCommissioner.\n\n(3) Before deciding whether to remove the registered APP code, the\nCommissioner must:\n\n(a) consult any person the Commissioner considers appropriate\nabout the proposed removal; and\n\n(b)  consider the extent to which members of the public have\nbeen given an opportunity to comment on the proposed\nremoval.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(4) In deciding whether to remove the registered APP code, the\nCommissioner may consider the matters specified in any relevant\nguidelines made under section 26V."
    },
