    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26n",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26N What is a CR code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26n"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CR code is a written code of practice about credit reporting.\n\n(2) A CR code must:\n\n(a) set out how one or more of the provisions of Part IIIA are to\nbe applied or complied with; and\n\n(b) make provision for, or in relation to, matters required or\npermitted by Part IIIA to be provided for by the registered\nCR code; and\n\n(c) bind all credit reporting bodies; and\n\n(d) specify the credit providers that are bound by the code, or a\nway of determining which credit providers are bound; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(e) specify any other entities subject to Part IIIA that are bound\nby the code, or a way of determining which of those entities\nare bound.\n\n(3) A CR code may do one or more of the following:\n\n(a) impose additional requirements to those imposed by",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A CR code is a written code of practice about credit reporting.\n\n(2) A CR code must:\n\n(a) set out how one or more of the provisions of Part IIIA are to\nbe applied or complied with; and\n\n(b) make provision for, or in relation to, matters required or\npermitted by Part IIIA to be provided for by the registered\nCR code; and\n\n(c) bind all credit reporting bodies; and\n\n(d) specify the credit providers that are bound by the code, or a\nway of determining which credit providers are bound; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(e) specify any other entities subject to Part IIIA that are bound\nby the code, or a way of determining which of those entities\nare bound.\n\n(3) A CR code may do one or more of the following:\n\n(a) impose additional requirements to those imposed by",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26n-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26n-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26n-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bc577c4a3d0edb5dae277b7f945ef67e79dccd8d85d5c7c28f50d6f75e57e704"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26n",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26N What is a CR code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A CR code is a written code of practice about credit reporting.\n\n(2) A CR code must:\n\n(a) set out how one or more of the provisions of Part IIIA are to\nbe applied or complied with; and\n\n(b) make provision for, or in relation to, matters required or\npermitted by Part IIIA to be provided for by the registered\nCR code; and\n\n(c) bind all credit reporting bodies; and\n\n(d) specify the credit providers that are bound by the code, or a\nway of determining which credit providers are bound; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(e) specify any other entities subject to Part IIIA that are bound\nby the code, or a way of determining which of those entities\nare bound.\n\n(3) A CR code may do one or more of the following:\n\n(a) impose additional requirements to those imposed by"
    },
