      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) A CR code may do one or more of the following:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26P Development of CR code by CR code developers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.161",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may, in writing, request a CR code developer to\ndevelop a CR code and apply to the Commissioner for the code to\nbe registered.\n\n(2) The request must:\n\n(a) specify the period within which the request must be complied\nwith; and\n\n(b) set out the effect of section 26L.\n\n(3) The period:\n\n(a) must run for at least 120 days from the date the request is\nmade; and\n\n(b) may be extended by the Commissioner.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(4) The request may:\n\n(a) specify one or more matters that the CR code must deal with;\nand\n\n(b) specify the credit providers, or a class of credit providers,\nthat should be bound by the code; and\n\n(c) specify the other entities, or a class of other entities, subject\nto Part IIIA that should be bound by the code.\n\n(5) The Commissioner must make a copy of the request publicly\navailable as soon as practicable after the request is made.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may, in writing, request a CR code developer to\ndevelop a CR code and apply to the Commissioner for the code to\nbe registered.\n\n(2) The request must:\n\n(a) specify the period within which the request must be complied\nwith; and\n\n(b) set out the effect of section 26L.\n\n(3) The period:\n\n(a) must run for at least 120 days from the date the request is\nmade; and\n\n(b) may be extended by the Commissioner.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(4) The request may:\n\n(a) specify one or more matters that the CR code must deal with;\nand\n\n(b) specify the credit providers, or a class of credit providers,\nthat should be bound by the code; and\n\n(c) specify the other entities, or a class of other entities, subject\nto Part IIIA that should be bound by the code.\n\n(5) The Commissioner must make a copy of the request publicly\navailable as soon as practicable after the request is made.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26p-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26p-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26p-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26p-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "da691b2cc62e672e12d348522180cb6c3049294e6b6bfe667b6fe53d8b1fee25"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26P Development of CR code by CR code developers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 161,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may, in writing, request a CR code developer to\ndevelop a CR code and apply to the Commissioner for the code to\nbe registered.\n\n(2) The request must:\n\n(a) specify the period within which the request must be complied\nwith; and\n\n(b) set out the effect of section 26L.\n\n(3) The period:\n\n(a) must run for at least 120 days from the date the request is\nmade; and\n\n(b) may be extended by the Commissioner.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(4) The request may:\n\n(a) specify one or more matters that the CR code must deal with;\nand\n\n(b) specify the credit providers, or a class of credit providers,\nthat should be bound by the code; and\n\n(c) specify the other entities, or a class of other entities, subject\nto Part IIIA that should be bound by the code.\n\n(5) The Commissioner must make a copy of the request publicly\navailable as soon as practicable after the request is made."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26p-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26P(1) Development of CR code by CR code developers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26p-ss-1"
