    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26Q Application for registration of CR code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.162",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a CR code developer develops a CR code, the developer may\napply to the Commissioner for registration of the code.\n\n(2) Before making the application, the CR code developer must:\n\n(a) make a draft of the CR code publicly available; and\n\n(b) invite the public to make submissions to the developer about\nthe draft within a specified period (which must run for at\nleast 28 days); and\n\n(c) give consideration to any submissions made within the\nspecified period.\n\n(3) The application must:\n\n(a) be made in the form and manner specified by the\nCommissioner; and\n\n(b) be accompanied by such information as is specified by the\nCommissioner.\n\n(4) The CR code developer may vary the CR code at any time before\nthe Commissioner registers the code, but only with the consent of\nthe Commissioner.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a CR code developer develops a CR code, the developer may\napply to the Commissioner for registration of the code.\n\n(2) Before making the application, the CR code developer must:\n\n(a) make a draft of the CR code publicly available; and\n\n(b) invite the public to make submissions to the developer about\nthe draft within a specified period (which must run for at\nleast 28 days); and\n\n(c) give consideration to any submissions made within the\nspecified period.\n\n(3) The application must:\n\n(a) be made in the form and manner specified by the\nCommissioner; and\n\n(b) be accompanied by such information as is specified by the\nCommissioner.\n\n(4) The CR code developer may vary the CR code at any time before\nthe Commissioner registers the code, but only with the consent of\nthe Commissioner.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26q-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26q-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26q-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "793594f92f88c9ed3a9629b56dc430b3aed77f4deea1e2f635d005cb6d50223f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26Q Application for registration of CR code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 162,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a CR code developer develops a CR code, the developer may\napply to the Commissioner for registration of the code.\n\n(2) Before making the application, the CR code developer must:\n\n(a) make a draft of the CR code publicly available; and\n\n(b) invite the public to make submissions to the developer about\nthe draft within a specified period (which must run for at\nleast 28 days); and\n\n(c) give consideration to any submissions made within the\nspecified period.\n\n(3) The application must:\n\n(a) be made in the form and manner specified by the\nCommissioner; and\n\n(b) be accompanied by such information as is specified by the\nCommissioner.\n\n(4) The CR code developer may vary the CR code at any time before\nthe Commissioner registers the code, but only with the consent of\nthe Commissioner."
    },
    {
