    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26R Development of CR code by the Commissioner",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.162",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may develop a CR code if the Commissioner\nmade a request under section 26P and either:\n\n(a) the request has not been complied with; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) the request has been complied with but the Commissioner has\ndecided not to register, under section 26S, the CR code that\nwas developed as requested.\n\n(2) Before registering the CR code under section 26S, the\nCommissioner must:\n\n(a) make a draft of the code publicly available; and\n\n(b) invite the public to make submissions to the Commissioner\nabout the draft within a specified period (which must run for\nat least 28 days); and\n\n(c) give consideration to any submissions made within the\nspecified period.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may develop a CR code if the Commissioner\nmade a request under section 26P and either:\n\n(a) the request has not been complied with; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) the request has been complied with but the Commissioner has\ndecided not to register, under section 26S, the CR code that\nwas developed as requested.\n\n(2) Before registering the CR code under section 26S, the\nCommissioner must:\n\n(a) make a draft of the code publicly available; and\n\n(b) invite the public to make submissions to the Commissioner\nabout the draft within a specified period (which must run for\nat least 28 days); and\n\n(c) give consideration to any submissions made within the\nspecified period.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26r-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26r-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dd4f7ea6e1e7c7fef995e358ea6d7e09ac72da318e183d964e3b9e8684ad501a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26r",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26R Development of CR code by the Commissioner",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 162,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may develop a CR code if the Commissioner\nmade a request under section 26P and either:\n\n(a) the request has not been complied with; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nPrivacy codes  Schedule 3\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) the request has been complied with but the Commissioner has\ndecided not to register, under section 26S, the CR code that\nwas developed as requested.\n\n(2) Before registering the CR code under section 26S, the\nCommissioner must:\n\n(a) make a draft of the code publicly available; and\n\n(b) invite the public to make submissions to the Commissioner\nabout the draft within a specified period (which must run for\nat least 28 days); and\n\n(c) give consideration to any submissions made within the\nspecified period."
    },
    {
