    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26S Commissioner may register CR code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.163",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an application for registration of a CR code is made under\nsection 26Q; or\n\n(b) the Commissioner develops a CR code under section 26R;\nthe Commissioner may register the code by including it on the\nCodes Register.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to register the CR code, the Commissioner\nmay:\n\n(a) consult any person the Commissioner considers appropriate;\nand\n\n(b) consider the matters specified in any guidelines made under\nsection 26V.\n\n(3) If the Commissioner decides not to register a CR code developed\nby a CR code developer, the Commissioner must give written\nnotice of the decision to the developer, including reasons for the\ndecision.\n\n(4) The Commissioner must ensure that there is one, and only one,\nregistered CR code at all times after this Part commences.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nSubdivision C—Variation of the registered CR code",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an application for registration of a CR code is made under\nsection 26Q; or\n\n(b) the Commissioner develops a CR code under section 26R;\nthe Commissioner may register the code by including it on the\nCodes Register.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to register the CR code, the Commissioner\nmay:\n\n(a) consult any person the Commissioner considers appropriate;\nand\n\n(b) consider the matters specified in any guidelines made under\nsection 26V.\n\n(3) If the Commissioner decides not to register a CR code developed\nby a CR code developer, the Commissioner must give written\nnotice of the decision to the developer, including reasons for the\ndecision.\n\n(4) The Commissioner must ensure that there is one, and only one,\nregistered CR code at all times after this Part commences.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nSubdivision C—Variation of the registered CR code",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26s-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26s-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26s-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26s-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f722c807375faa79555fab6cc8fa9c4851ed34fd820a9c4ef398c83bbdec738f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26s",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26S Commissioner may register CR code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 163,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an application for registration of a CR code is made under\nsection 26Q; or\n\n(b) the Commissioner develops a CR code under section 26R;\nthe Commissioner may register the code by including it on the\nCodes Register.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to register the CR code, the Commissioner\nmay:\n\n(a) consult any person the Commissioner considers appropriate;\nand\n\n(b) consider the matters specified in any guidelines made under\nsection 26V.\n\n(3) If the Commissioner decides not to register a CR code developed\nby a CR code developer, the Commissioner must give written\nnotice of the decision to the developer, including reasons for the\ndecision.\n\n(4) The Commissioner must ensure that there is one, and only one,\nregistered CR code at all times after this Part commences.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nSubdivision C—Variation of the registered CR code"
    },
