    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26v",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26V Guidelines relating to codes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26v"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.165",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may make written guidelines:\n\n(a) to assist APP code developers to develop APP codes; or\n\n(b) to assist APP entities bound by registered APP codes to apply\nor comply with the codes; or\n\n(c) to assist CR code developers to develop a CR code; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) to assist entities bound by the registered CR code to apply or\ncomply with the code.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may make written guidelines about matters the\nCommissioner may consider in deciding whether:\n\n(a) to register an APP code or a CR code; or\n\n(b) to approve a variation of a registered APP code or the\nregistered CR code; or\n\n(c) to remove a registered APP code from the Codes Register.\n\n(3) The Commissioner may publish any such guidelines on the\nCommissioner’s website.\n\n(4) Guidelines are not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may make written guidelines:\n\n(a) to assist APP code developers to develop APP codes; or\n\n(b) to assist APP entities bound by registered APP codes to apply\nor comply with the codes; or\n\n(c) to assist CR code developers to develop a CR code; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) to assist entities bound by the registered CR code to apply or\ncomply with the code.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may make written guidelines about matters the\nCommissioner may consider in deciding whether:\n\n(a) to register an APP code or a CR code; or\n\n(b) to approve a variation of a registered APP code or the\nregistered CR code; or\n\n(c) to remove a registered APP code from the Codes Register.\n\n(3) The Commissioner may publish any such guidelines on the\nCommissioner’s website.\n\n(4) Guidelines are not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26v-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26v-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26v-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-3-sec-26v-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "36422a49f759d9e42b73f9c536c09388b176840dc93cc70b5316e367cab5b680"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-3-sec-26v",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26V Guidelines relating to codes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 165,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may make written guidelines:\n\n(a) to assist APP code developers to develop APP codes; or\n\n(b) to assist APP entities bound by registered APP codes to apply\nor comply with the codes; or\n\n(c) to assist CR code developers to develop a CR code; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 3  Privacy codes\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) to assist entities bound by the registered CR code to apply or\ncomply with the code.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may make written guidelines about matters the\nCommissioner may consider in deciding whether:\n\n(a) to register an APP code or a CR code; or\n\n(b) to approve a variation of a registered APP code or the\nregistered CR code; or\n\n(c) to remove a registered APP code from the Codes Register.\n\n(3) The Commissioner may publish any such guidelines on the\nCommissioner’s website.\n\n(4) Guidelines are not a legislative instrument."
    },
