    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 Subsections 5B(1) and (1A)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.168",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nAgencies\n\n(1) This Act, a registered APP code and the registered CR code extend\nto an act done, or practice engaged in, outside Australia and the\nexternal Territories by an agency.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nNote:\nThe act or practice overseas will not breach an Australian Privacy\nPrinciple or a registered APP code if the act or practice is required by\nan applicable foreign law (see sections 6A and 6B).\nOrganisations and small business operators\n\n(1A) This Act, a registered APP code and the registered CR code extend\nto an act done, or practice engaged in, outside Australia and the\nexternal Territories by an organisation, or small business operator,\nthat has an Australian link.\nNote:\nThe act or practice overseas will not breach an Australian Privacy\nPrinciple or a registered APP code if the act or practice is required by\nan applicable foreign law (see sections 6A and 6B).",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nAgencies\n\n(1) This Act, a registered APP code and the registered CR code extend\nto an act done, or practice engaged in, outside Australia and the\nexternal Territories by an agency.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nNote:\nThe act or practice overseas will not breach an Australian Privacy\nPrinciple or a registered APP code if the act or practice is required by\nan applicable foreign law (see sections 6A and 6B).\nOrganisations and small business operators\n\n(1A) This Act, a registered APP code and the registered CR code extend\nto an act done, or practice engaged in, outside Australia and the\nexternal Territories by an organisation, or small business operator,\nthat has an Australian link.\nNote:\nThe act or practice overseas will not breach an Australian Privacy\nPrinciple or a registered APP code if the act or practice is required by\nan applicable foreign law (see sections 6A and 6B).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-2-ss-1a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a9f6dacd4f07ca2f47d04e1bc0c9aeae9013d483750df2bf3c7d6058db4f40fb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Subsections 5B(1) and (1A)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 168,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nAgencies\n\n(1) This Act, a registered APP code and the registered CR code extend\nto an act done, or practice engaged in, outside Australia and the\nexternal Territories by an agency.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nNote:\nThe act or practice overseas will not breach an Australian Privacy\nPrinciple or a registered APP code if the act or practice is required by\nan applicable foreign law (see sections 6A and 6B).\nOrganisations and small business operators\n\n(1A) This Act, a registered APP code and the registered CR code extend\nto an act done, or practice engaged in, outside Australia and the\nexternal Territories by an organisation, or small business operator,\nthat has an Australian link.\nNote:\nThe act or practice overseas will not breach an Australian Privacy\nPrinciple or a registered APP code if the act or practice is required by\nan applicable foreign law (see sections 6A and 6B)."
    },
