      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.170",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the definitions, substitute:\nbreach:\n\n(a) in relation to an Australian Privacy Principle, has the\nmeaning given by section 6A; and\n\n(b) in relation to a registered APP code, has the meaning given\nby section 6B; and\n\n(c)  in relation to the registered CR code, has the meaning given\nby section 6BA.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the definitions, substitute:\nbreach:\n\n(a) in relation to an Australian Privacy Principle, has the\nmeaning given by section 6A; and\n\n(b) in relation to a registered APP code, has the meaning given\nby section 6B; and\n\n(c)  in relation to the registered CR code, has the meaning given\nby section 6BA.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-11-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-11-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aad564120ebfc1476d1bb2dee8207f4a32df511b39637b2d410b6236b65c6489",
      "skos:note": "Repeal definitions, substitute new meanings for breach"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11 Subsection 6(1) (all the definitions of breach)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 170,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the definitions, substitute:\nbreach:\n\n(a) in relation to an Australian Privacy Principle, has the\nmeaning given by section 6A; and\n\n(b) in relation to a registered APP code, has the meaning given\nby section 6B; and\n\n(c)  in relation to the registered CR code, has the meaning given\nby section 6BA."
    },
