    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-35",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35 Subsections 12B(1) and (2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-35"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.173",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) Without limiting its effect apart from this section, this Act has\neffect in relation to the following (the regulated entities) as\nprovided by this section:\n\n(a) an agency;\n\n(b) an organisation;\n\n(c) a small business operator;\n\n(d) a body politic.\nNote:\nSubsection 27(4) applies in relation to an investigation of an act or\npractice referred to in subsection 29(1) of the Healthcare Identifiers\nAct 2010.\n\n(2) This Act also has the effect it would have if its operation in relation\nto regulated entities were expressly confined to an operation to\ngive effect to the following:\n\n(a) the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights done\nat New York on 16 December 1966 ([1980] ATS 23), and in\nparticular Articles 17 and 24(1) of the Covenant;\n\n(b) Article 16 of the Convention on the Rights of the Child done\nat New York on 20 November 1989 ([1991] ATS 4).\nNote:\nIn 2012, the text of the Covenant and Convention in the Australian\nTreaty Series was accessible through the Australian Treaties Library\non the AustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au).",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) Without limiting its effect apart from this section, this Act has\neffect in relation to the following (the regulated entities) as\nprovided by this section:\n\n(a) an agency;\n\n(b) an organisation;\n\n(c) a small business operator;\n\n(d) a body politic.\nNote:\nSubsection 27(4) applies in relation to an investigation of an act or\npractice referred to in subsection 29(1) of the Healthcare Identifiers\nAct 2010.\n\n(2) This Act also has the effect it would have if its operation in relation\nto regulated entities were expressly confined to an operation to\ngive effect to the following:\n\n(a) the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights done\nat New York on 16 December 1966 ([1980] ATS 23), and in\nparticular Articles 17 and 24(1) of the Covenant;\n\n(b) Article 16 of the Convention on the Rights of the Child done\nat New York on 20 November 1989 ([1991] ATS 4).\nNote:\nIn 2012, the text of the Covenant and Convention in the Australian\nTreaty Series was accessible through the Australian Treaties Library\non the AustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-35-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-35-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "45006b563b2fa2182b7ea81cca2aac16faa404d7946d1c0f51f91fbff6cf069d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-35",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35 Subsections 12B(1) and (2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 173,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) Without limiting its effect apart from this section, this Act has\neffect in relation to the following (the regulated entities) as\nprovided by this section:\n\n(a) an agency;\n\n(b) an organisation;\n\n(c) a small business operator;\n\n(d) a body politic.\nNote:\nSubsection 27(4) applies in relation to an investigation of an act or\npractice referred to in subsection 29(1) of the Healthcare Identifiers\nAct 2010.\n\n(2) This Act also has the effect it would have if its operation in relation\nto regulated entities were expressly confined to an operation to\ngive effect to the following:\n\n(a) the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights done\nat New York on 16 December 1966 ([1980] ATS 23), and in\nparticular Articles 17 and 24(1) of the Covenant;\n\n(b) Article 16 of the Convention on the Rights of the Child done\nat New York on 20 November 1989 ([1991] ATS 4).\nNote:\nIn 2012, the text of the Covenant and Convention in the Australian\nTreaty Series was accessible through the Australian Treaties Library\non the AustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-35-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35(1) Subsections 12B(1) and (2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
