    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13(3) Interferences with privacy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "(3) An act or practice of an organisation is an interference with the\nprivacy of an individual if:\n\n(a) the act or practice relates to personal information about the\nindividual; and\n\n(b) the organisation is a contracted service provider for a\nCommonwealth contract (whether or not the organisation is a\nparty to the contract); and\n\n(c) the act or practice does not breach:\n\n(i) an Australian Privacy Principle; or\n\n(ii) a registered APP code that binds the organisation;\n\nin relation to the personal information because of a provision\nof the contract that is inconsistent with the principle or code;\nand\n\n(d) the act is done, or the practice is engaged in, in a manner\ncontrary to, or inconsistent with, that provision.\nNote:\nSee subsections 6A(2) and 6B(2) for when an act or practice does not\nbreach an Australian Privacy Principle or a registered APP code.\nTax file numbers",
      "skos:definition": "(3) An act or practice of an organisation is an interference with the\nprivacy of an individual if:\n\n(a) the act or practice relates to personal information about the\nindividual; and\n\n(b) the organisation is a contracted service provider for a\nCommonwealth contract (whether or not the organisation is a\nparty to the contract); and\n\n(c) the act or practice does not breach:\n\n(i) an Australian Privacy Principle; or\n\n(ii) a registered APP code that binds the organisation;\n\nin relation to the personal information because of a provision\nof the contract that is inconsistent with the principle or code;\nand\n\n(d) the act is done, or the practice is engaged in, in a manner\ncontrary to, or inconsistent with, that provision.\nNote:\nSee subsections 6A(2) and 6B(2) for when an act or practice does not\nbreach an Australian Privacy Principle or a registered APP code.\nTax file numbers",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-13-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-3-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-3-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7a29513a4160654cea5d34368f2e5f523780f5054e1a3773ffc5e3a79fd55acc",
      "skos:note": "Interference with privacy is prohibited if it breaches an Australian Privacy Principle or a registered APP code."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13(3) Interferences with privacy",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "(3) An act or practice of an organisation is an interference with the\nprivacy of an individual if:\n\n(a) the act or practice relates to personal information about the\nindividual; and\n\n(b) the organisation is a contracted service provider for a\nCommonwealth contract (whether or not the organisation is a\nparty to the contract); and\n\n(c) the act or practice does not breach:\n\n(i) an Australian Privacy Principle; or\n\n(ii) a registered APP code that binds the organisation;\n\nin relation to the personal information because of a provision\nof the contract that is inconsistent with the principle or code;\nand\n\n(d) the act is done, or the practice is engaged in, in a manner\ncontrary to, or inconsistent with, that provision.\nNote:\nSee subsections 6A(2) and 6B(2) for when an act or practice does not\nbreach an Australian Privacy Principle or a registered APP code.\nTax file numbers"
    },
