    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13(5) Interferences with privacy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "(5) An act or practice is an interference with the privacy of an\nindividual if the act or practice:\n\n(a) constitutes a breach of Part 2 of the Data-matching Program\n(Assistance and Tax) Act 1990 or the rules issued under\nsection 12 of that Act; or\n\n(b) constitutes a breach of the rules issued under section 135AA\nof the National Health Act 1953.\nNote:\nOther Acts may provide that an act or practice is an interference with\nthe privacy of an individual. For example, see the Healthcare\nIdentifiers Act 2010, the Anti-Money Laundering and\nCounter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006 and the Personal Property\nSecurities Act 2009.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) An act or practice is an interference with the privacy of an\nindividual if the act or practice:\n\n(a) constitutes a breach of Part 2 of the Data-matching Program\n(Assistance and Tax) Act 1990 or the rules issued under\nsection 12 of that Act; or\n\n(b) constitutes a breach of the rules issued under section 135AA\nof the National Health Act 1953.\nNote:\nOther Acts may provide that an act or practice is an interference with\nthe privacy of an individual. For example, see the Healthcare\nIdentifiers Act 2010, the Anti-Money Laundering and\nCounter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006 and the Personal Property\nSecurities Act 2009.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-13-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a806f70684af64edc18e1c8763f236345d359399ed7297ad68922e2aa6aee8d3",
      "skos:note": "Interference with privacy defined as breach of specific Acts or rules."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-13-2-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13(5) Interferences with privacy",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "(5) An act or practice is an interference with the privacy of an\nindividual if the act or practice:\n\n(a) constitutes a breach of Part 2 of the Data-matching Program\n(Assistance and Tax) Act 1990 or the rules issued under\nsection 12 of that Act; or\n\n(b) constitutes a breach of the rules issued under section 135AA\nof the National Health Act 1953.\nNote:\nOther Acts may provide that an act or practice is an interference with\nthe privacy of an individual. For example, see the Healthcare\nIdentifiers Act 2010, the Anti-Money Laundering and\nCounter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006 and the Personal Property\nSecurities Act 2009."
    },
