    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-27-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "27 Functions of the Commissioner",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-27-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.178",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner has the following functions:\n\n(a) the functions that are conferred on the Commissioner by or\nunder:\n\n(i) this Act; or\n\n(ii) any other law of the Commonwealth;\n\n(b) the guidance related functions;\n\n(c) the monitoring related functions;\n\n(d) the advice related functions;\n\n(e) to do anything incidental or conducive to the performance of\nany of the above functions.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) The Commissioner has power to do all things necessary or\nconvenient to be done for, or in connection with, the performance\nof the Commissioner’s functions.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (2), the Commissioner may establish a\npanel of persons with expertise in relation to a particular matter to\nassist the Commissioner in performing any of the Commissioner’s\nfunctions.\n\n(4) Section 38 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010, rather than\nsection 12B of this Act, applies in relation to an investigation of an\nact or practice referred to in subsection 29(1) of that Act in the\nsame way as it applies to Parts 3 and 4 of that Act.\nNote:\nSection 38 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010 deals with the\nadditional effect of Parts 3 and 4 of that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner has the following functions:\n\n(a) the functions that are conferred on the Commissioner by or\nunder:\n\n(i) this Act; or\n\n(ii) any other law of the Commonwealth;\n\n(b) the guidance related functions;\n\n(c) the monitoring related functions;\n\n(d) the advice related functions;\n\n(e) to do anything incidental or conducive to the performance of\nany of the above functions.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) The Commissioner has power to do all things necessary or\nconvenient to be done for, or in connection with, the performance\nof the Commissioner’s functions.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (2), the Commissioner may establish a\npanel of persons with expertise in relation to a particular matter to\nassist the Commissioner in performing any of the Commissioner’s\nfunctions.\n\n(4) Section 38 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010, rather than\nsection 12B of this Act, applies in relation to an investigation of an\nact or practice referred to in subsection 29(1) of that Act in the\nsame way as it applies to Parts 3 and 4 of that Act.\nNote:\nSection 38 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010 deals with the\nadditional effect of Parts 3 and 4 of that Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-27-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-27-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-27-2-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-27-2-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0897147789da389b629a66d1061878932805e33fa157ab4485aef96b4d471132"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-27-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "27 Functions of the Commissioner",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 178,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner has the following functions:\n\n(a) the functions that are conferred on the Commissioner by or\nunder:\n\n(i) this Act; or\n\n(ii) any other law of the Commonwealth;\n\n(b) the guidance related functions;\n\n(c) the monitoring related functions;\n\n(d) the advice related functions;\n\n(e) to do anything incidental or conducive to the performance of\nany of the above functions.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) The Commissioner has power to do all things necessary or\nconvenient to be done for, or in connection with, the performance\nof the Commissioner’s functions.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (2), the Commissioner may establish a\npanel of persons with expertise in relation to a particular matter to\nassist the Commissioner in performing any of the Commissioner’s\nfunctions.\n\n(4) Section 38 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010, rather than\nsection 12B of this Act, applies in relation to an investigation of an\nact or practice referred to in subsection 29(1) of that Act in the\nsame way as it applies to Parts 3 and 4 of that Act.\nNote:\nSection 38 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010 deals with the\nadditional effect of Parts 3 and 4 of that Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-27-2-ss-1",
