    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-64",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "64 After section 33B",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-64"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.183",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 4  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 4  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-64-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "26d0fd940a35ab48d91c0898b2c8a1c34928261d99c9a6bb5d09c343b28fccf8",
      "skos:note": "Inserts amendments of the Privacy Act 1988"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-64",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "64 After section 33B",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 183,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 4  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-64-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-64"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-33c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "33C Commissioner may conduct an assessment relating to the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-33c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.184",
      "values:originalText": "Australian Privacy Principles etc.\n\n(1) The Commissioner may conduct an assessment of the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) whether personal information held by an APP entity is being\nmaintained and handled in accordance with the following:\n\n(i) the Australian Privacy Principles;\n\n(ii) a registered APP code that binds the entity;\n\n(b) whether information held by an entity is being maintained\nand handled in accordance with the following to the extent\nthat they apply to the information:\n\n(i) the provisions of Part IIIA;\n\n(ii) the registered CR code if it binds the entity;\n\n(c) whether tax file number information held by a file number\nrecipient is being maintained and handled in accordance with\nany relevant rules issued under section 17;\n\n(d) whether the data matching program (within the meaning of\nthe Data-matching Program (Assistance and Tax) Act 1990)\nof an agency complies with Part 2 of that Act and the rules\nissued under section 12 of that Act;\n\n(e) whether information to which section 135AA of the National\nHealth Act 1953 applies is being maintained and handled in\naccordance with the rules issued under that section.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may conduct the assessment in such manner as\nthe Commissioner considers fit.",
      "skos:definition": "Australian Privacy Principles etc.\n\n(1) The Commissioner may conduct an assessment of the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) whether personal information held by an APP entity is being\nmaintained and handled in accordance with the following:\n\n(i) the Australian Privacy Principles;\n\n(ii) a registered APP code that binds the entity;\n\n(b) whether information held by an entity is being maintained\nand handled in accordance with the following to the extent\nthat they apply to the information:\n\n(i) the provisions of Part IIIA;\n\n(ii) the registered CR code if it binds the entity;\n\n(c) whether tax file number information held by a file number\nrecipient is being maintained and handled in accordance with\nany relevant rules issued under section 17;\n\n(d) whether the data matching program (within the meaning of\nthe Data-matching Program (Assistance and Tax) Act 1990)\nof an agency complies with Part 2 of that Act and the rules\nissued under section 12 of that Act;\n\n(e) whether information to which section 135AA of the National\nHealth Act 1953 applies is being maintained and handled in\naccordance with the rules issued under that section.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may conduct the assessment in such manner as\nthe Commissioner considers fit.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-33c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-33c-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "70eb18d5dc8aae9f03c425652ff953482f0e6e219c49eed1fa7e6606b33990d5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-33c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "33C Commissioner may conduct an assessment relating to the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 184,
      "values:originalText": "Australian Privacy Principles etc.\n\n(1) The Commissioner may conduct an assessment of the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) whether personal information held by an APP entity is being\nmaintained and handled in accordance with the following:\n\n(i) the Australian Privacy Principles;\n\n(ii) a registered APP code that binds the entity;\n\n(b) whether information held by an entity is being maintained\nand handled in accordance with the following to the extent\nthat they apply to the information:\n\n(i) the provisions of Part IIIA;\n\n(ii) the registered CR code if it binds the entity;\n\n(c) whether tax file number information held by a file number\nrecipient is being maintained and handled in accordance with\nany relevant rules issued under section 17;\n\n(d) whether the data matching program (within the meaning of\nthe Data-matching Program (Assistance and Tax) Act 1990)\nof an agency complies with Part 2 of that Act and the rules\nissued under section 12 of that Act;\n\n(e) whether information to which section 135AA of the National\nHealth Act 1953 applies is being maintained and handled in\naccordance with the rules issued under that section.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may conduct the assessment in such manner as\nthe Commissioner considers fit."
    },
