    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-33d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "33D Commissioner may direct an agency to give a privacy impact",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-33d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.184",
      "values:originalText": "assessment\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) an agency proposes to engage in an activity or function\ninvolving the handling of personal information about\nindividuals; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) the Commissioner considers that the activity or function\nmight have a significant impact on the privacy of individuals;\nthe Commissioner may, in writing, direct the agency to give the\nCommissioner, within a specified period, a privacy impact\nassessment about the activity or function.\n\n(2) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.\nPrivacy impact assessment\n\n(3) A privacy impact assessment is a written assessment of an activity\nor function that:\n\n(a) identifies the impact that the activity or function might have\non the privacy of individuals; and\n\n(b) sets out recommendations for managing, minimising or\neliminating that impact.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) does not limit the matters that the privacy impact\nassessment may deal with.\n\n(5) A privacy impact assessment is not a legislative instrument.\nFailure to comply with a direction\n\n(6) If an agency does not comply with a direction under subsection (1),\nthe Commissioner must advise both of the following of the failure:\n\n(a) the Minister;\n\n(b) if another Minister is responsible for the agency—that other\nMinister.\nReview\n\n(7) Before the fifth anniversary of the commencement of this section,\nthe Minister must cause a review to be undertaken of whether this\nsection should apply in relation to organisations.",
      "skos:definition": "assessment\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) an agency proposes to engage in an activity or function\ninvolving the handling of personal information about\nindividuals; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) the Commissioner considers that the activity or function\nmight have a significant impact on the privacy of individuals;\nthe Commissioner may, in writing, direct the agency to give the\nCommissioner, within a specified period, a privacy impact\nassessment about the activity or function.\n\n(2) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.\nPrivacy impact assessment\n\n(3) A privacy impact assessment is a written assessment of an activity\nor function that:\n\n(a) identifies the impact that the activity or function might have\non the privacy of individuals; and\n\n(b) sets out recommendations for managing, minimising or\neliminating that impact.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) does not limit the matters that the privacy impact\nassessment may deal with.\n\n(5) A privacy impact assessment is not a legislative instrument.\nFailure to comply with a direction\n\n(6) If an agency does not comply with a direction under subsection (1),\nthe Commissioner must advise both of the following of the failure:\n\n(a) the Minister;\n\n(b) if another Minister is responsible for the agency—that other\nMinister.\nReview\n\n(7) Before the fifth anniversary of the commencement of this section,\nthe Minister must cause a review to be undertaken of whether this\nsection should apply in relation to organisations.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-33d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-33d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-33d-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-33d-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-33d-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-33d-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-33d-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "89c08f7a02989db85066486407e81228ddadae03a30b293e5298cd050bd92db7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-33d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "33D Commissioner may direct an agency to give a privacy impact",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 184,
      "values:originalText": "assessment\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) an agency proposes to engage in an activity or function\ninvolving the handling of personal information about\nindividuals; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) the Commissioner considers that the activity or function\nmight have a significant impact on the privacy of individuals;\nthe Commissioner may, in writing, direct the agency to give the\nCommissioner, within a specified period, a privacy impact\nassessment about the activity or function.\n\n(2) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.\nPrivacy impact assessment\n\n(3) A privacy impact assessment is a written assessment of an activity\nor function that:\n\n(a) identifies the impact that the activity or function might have\non the privacy of individuals; and\n\n(b) sets out recommendations for managing, minimising or\neliminating that impact.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) does not limit the matters that the privacy impact\nassessment may deal with.\n\n(5) A privacy impact assessment is not a legislative instrument.\nFailure to comply with a direction\n\n(6) If an agency does not comply with a direction under subsection (1),\nthe Commissioner must advise both of the following of the failure:\n\n(a) the Minister;\n\n(b) if another Minister is responsible for the agency—that other\nMinister.\nReview\n\n(7) Before the fifth anniversary of the commencement of this section,\nthe Minister must cause a review to be undertaken of whether this\nsection should apply in relation to organisations."
    },
