    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-36a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36A Guide to this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-36a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.188",
      "values:originalText": "In general, this Part deals with complaints and investigations about\nacts or practices that may be an interference with the privacy of an\nindividual.\nAn individual may complain to the Commissioner about an act or\npractice that may be an interference with the privacy of the\nindividual. If a complaint is made, the Commissioner is required to\ninvestigate the act or practice except in certain circumstances.\nThe Commissioner may also, on his or her own initiative,\ninvestigate an act or practice that may be an interference with the\nprivacy of an individual or a breach of Australian Privacy Principle\n1.\nThe Commissioner has a range powers relating to the conduct of\ninvestigations including powers:\n\n(a)\nto conciliate complaints; and\n\n(b)\nto make preliminary inquiries of any person; and\n\n(c)\nto require a person to give information or\ndocuments, or to attend a compulsory conference;\nand\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d)\nto transfer matters to an alternative complaint body\nin certain circumstances.\nAfter an investigation, the Commissioner may make a\ndetermination in relation to the investigation. An entity to which a\ndetermination relates must comply with certain declarations\nincluded in the determination. Court proceedings may be\ncommenced to enforce a determination.",
      "skos:definition": "In general, this Part deals with complaints and investigations about\nacts or practices that may be an interference with the privacy of an\nindividual.\nAn individual may complain to the Commissioner about an act or\npractice that may be an interference with the privacy of the\nindividual. If a complaint is made, the Commissioner is required to\ninvestigate the act or practice except in certain circumstances.\nThe Commissioner may also, on his or her own initiative,\ninvestigate an act or practice that may be an interference with the\nprivacy of an individual or a breach of Australian Privacy Principle\n1.\nThe Commissioner has a range powers relating to the conduct of\ninvestigations including powers:\n\n(a)\nto conciliate complaints; and\n\n(b)\nto make preliminary inquiries of any person; and\n\n(c)\nto require a person to give information or\ndocuments, or to attend a compulsory conference;\nand\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d)\nto transfer matters to an alternative complaint body\nin certain circumstances.\nAfter an investigation, the Commissioner may make a\ndetermination in relation to the investigation. An entity to which a\ndetermination relates must comply with certain declarations\nincluded in the determination. Court proceedings may be\ncommenced to enforce a determination.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-36a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-36a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-36a-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-36a-logic-linearlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-36a-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cddd5bed9ccf578d4246aff5a4e39747bd1d87a2416ed972fdba5d42256995ba",
      "skos:note": "Individuals have a right to complain about privacy interference and the Commissioner must investigate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-36a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36A Guide to this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 188,
      "values:originalText": "In general, this Part deals with complaints and investigations about\nacts or practices that may be an interference with the privacy of an\nindividual.\nAn individual may complain to the Commissioner about an act or\npractice that may be an interference with the privacy of the\nindividual. If a complaint is made, the Commissioner is required to\ninvestigate the act or practice except in certain circumstances.\nThe Commissioner may also, on his or her own initiative,\ninvestigate an act or practice that may be an interference with the\nprivacy of an individual or a breach of Australian Privacy Principle\n1.\nThe Commissioner has a range powers relating to the conduct of\ninvestigations including powers:\n\n(a)\nto conciliate complaints; and\n\n(b)\nto make preliminary inquiries of any person; and\n\n(c)\nto require a person to give information or\ndocuments, or to attend a compulsory conference;\nand\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d)\nto transfer matters to an alternative complaint body\nin certain circumstances.\nAfter an investigation, the Commissioner may make a\ndetermination in relation to the investigation. An entity to which a\ndetermination relates must comply with certain declarations\nincluded in the determination. Court proceedings may be\ncommenced to enforce a determination."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-36a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
