    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-109",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "109 Subsection 52(1A)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-109"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.196",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1A) After investigating an act or practice of a person or entity under\nsubsection 40(2), the Commissioner may make a determination\nthat includes one or more of the following:\n\n(a) a declaration that:\n\n(i) the act or practice is an interference with the privacy of\none or more individuals; and\n\n(ii) the person or entity must not repeat or continue the act\nor practice;\n\n(b) a declaration that the person or entity must take specified\nsteps within a specified period to ensure that the act or\npractice is not repeated or continued;\n\n(c) a declaration that the person or entity must perform any\nreasonable act or course of conduct to redress any loss or\ndamage suffered by one or more of those individuals;\n\n(d) a declaration that one or more of those individuals are\nentitled to a specified amount by way of compensation for\nany loss or damage suffered by reason of the act or practice;\n\n(e) a declaration that it would be inappropriate for any further\naction to be taken in the matter.\n\n(1AA) The steps specified by the Commissioner under\nsubparagraph (1)(b)(ia) or paragraph (1A)(b) must be reasonable\nand appropriate.\n\n(1AB) The loss or damage referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or\nsubsection (1A) includes:\n\n(a) injury to the feelings of the complainant or individual; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) humiliation suffered by the complainant or individual.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1A) After investigating an act or practice of a person or entity under\nsubsection 40(2), the Commissioner may make a determination\nthat includes one or more of the following:\n\n(a) a declaration that:\n\n(i) the act or practice is an interference with the privacy of\none or more individuals; and\n\n(ii) the person or entity must not repeat or continue the act\nor practice;\n\n(b) a declaration that the person or entity must take specified\nsteps within a specified period to ensure that the act or\npractice is not repeated or continued;\n\n(c) a declaration that the person or entity must perform any\nreasonable act or course of conduct to redress any loss or\ndamage suffered by one or more of those individuals;\n\n(d) a declaration that one or more of those individuals are\nentitled to a specified amount by way of compensation for\nany loss or damage suffered by reason of the act or practice;\n\n(e) a declaration that it would be inappropriate for any further\naction to be taken in the matter.\n\n(1AA) The steps specified by the Commissioner under\nsubparagraph (1)(b)(ia) or paragraph (1A)(b) must be reasonable\nand appropriate.\n\n(1AB) The loss or damage referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or\nsubsection (1A) includes:\n\n(a) injury to the feelings of the complainant or individual; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) humiliation suffered by the complainant or individual.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-109-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-109-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-109-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "23da938614c37ae60219dc0547c79165210cae936051b832f81299af098cc9f7",
      "skos:note": "Commissioner may make a determination that includes one or more of the following declarations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-109",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "109 Subsection 52(1A)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 196,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1A) After investigating an act or practice of a person or entity under\nsubsection 40(2), the Commissioner may make a determination\nthat includes one or more of the following:\n\n(a) a declaration that:\n\n(i) the act or practice is an interference with the privacy of\none or more individuals; and\n\n(ii) the person or entity must not repeat or continue the act\nor practice;\n\n(b) a declaration that the person or entity must take specified\nsteps within a specified period to ensure that the act or\npractice is not repeated or continued;\n\n(c) a declaration that the person or entity must perform any\nreasonable act or course of conduct to redress any loss or\ndamage suffered by one or more of those individuals;\n\n(d) a declaration that one or more of those individuals are\nentitled to a specified amount by way of compensation for\nany loss or damage suffered by reason of the act or practice;\n\n(e) a declaration that it would be inappropriate for any further\naction to be taken in the matter.\n\n(1AA) The steps specified by the Commissioner under\nsubparagraph (1)(b)(ia) or paragraph (1A)(b) must be reasonable\nand appropriate.\n\n(1AB) The loss or damage referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or\nsubsection (1A) includes:\n\n(a) injury to the feelings of the complainant or individual; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(b) humiliation suffered by the complainant or individual."
    },
