    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80w-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80W(3) Civil penalty orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-80w-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.207",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the court is satisfied that the entity has contravened the civil\npenalty provision, the court may order the entity to pay to the\nCommonwealth such pecuniary penalty for the contravention as the\ncourt determines to be appropriate.\nNote:\nSubsection (5) sets out the maximum penalty that the court may order\nthe entity to pay.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If the court is satisfied that the entity has contravened the civil\npenalty provision, the court may order the entity to pay to the\nCommonwealth such pecuniary penalty for the contravention as the\ncourt determines to be appropriate.\nNote:\nSubsection (5) sets out the maximum penalty that the court may order\nthe entity to pay.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80w"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80w-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80w-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3c548aa0a2d4c08adc0e92919a7912c61abe4fef42e0fb2ad025623ff220bb10",
      "skos:note": "Entity must pay pecuniary penalty to the Commonwealth if found contravening civil penalty provision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-80w-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80W(3) Civil penalty orders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 207,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the court is satisfied that the entity has contravened the civil\npenalty provision, the court may order the entity to pay to the\nCommonwealth such pecuniary penalty for the contravention as the\ncourt determines to be appropriate.\nNote:\nSubsection (5) sets out the maximum penalty that the court may order\nthe entity to pay."
    },
