    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80z",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80Z Multiple contraventions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-80z"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.209",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Federal Court or Federal Magistrates Court may make a single\ncivil penalty order against an entity for multiple contraventions of a\ncivil penalty provision if:\n\n(a) proceedings for the contraventions are founded on the same\nfacts; or\n\n(b) the contraventions form, or are part of, a series of\ncontraventions of the same or a similar character.\n\n(2) However, the pecuniary penalty must not exceed the sum of the\nmaximum pecuniary penalties that could be ordered if a separate\ncivil penalty order were made for each of the contraventions.\nNote:\nIn determining the pecuniary penalty, the court must take into account\nall relevant matters including the matters mentioned in subsection\n80W(6).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Federal Court or Federal Magistrates Court may make a single\ncivil penalty order against an entity for multiple contraventions of a\ncivil penalty provision if:\n\n(a) proceedings for the contraventions are founded on the same\nfacts; or\n\n(b) the contraventions form, or are part of, a series of\ncontraventions of the same or a similar character.\n\n(2) However, the pecuniary penalty must not exceed the sum of the\nmaximum pecuniary penalties that could be ordered if a separate\ncivil penalty order were made for each of the contraventions.\nNote:\nIn determining the pecuniary penalty, the court must take into account\nall relevant matters including the matters mentioned in subsection\n80W(6).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80z-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80z-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "626389b26981b4e4ff46ea7dcf75cace387a0c65b66b0c807aaaa01866982381"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-80z",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80Z Multiple contraventions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 209,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Federal Court or Federal Magistrates Court may make a single\ncivil penalty order against an entity for multiple contraventions of a\ncivil penalty provision if:\n\n(a) proceedings for the contraventions are founded on the same\nfacts; or\n\n(b) the contraventions form, or are part of, a series of\ncontraventions of the same or a similar character.\n\n(2) However, the pecuniary penalty must not exceed the sum of the\nmaximum pecuniary penalties that could be ordered if a separate\ncivil penalty order were made for each of the contraventions.\nNote:\nIn determining the pecuniary penalty, the court must take into account\nall relevant matters including the matters mentioned in subsection\n80W(6)."
    },
