    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80zf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80ZF Criminal proceedings after civil proceedings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-80zf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.210",
      "values:originalText": "Criminal proceedings may be commenced against an entity for\nconduct that is the same, or substantially the same, as conduct that\nwould constitute a contravention of a civil penalty provision\nregardless of whether a civil penalty order has been made against\nthe entity in relation to the contravention.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "skos:definition": "Criminal proceedings may be commenced against an entity for\nconduct that is the same, or substantially the same, as conduct that\nwould constitute a contravention of a civil penalty provision\nregardless of whether a civil penalty order has been made against\nthe entity in relation to the contravention.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80zf-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80zf-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6bb292cd46cd63d8352dabb6a6f4b1180b862c379de0ff7b9bfc09f5c9112c3d",
      "skos:note": "Criminal proceedings may be commenced against an entity for conduct that is the same, or substantially the same, as conduct that would constitute a contravention of a civil penalty provision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-80zf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80ZF Criminal proceedings after civil proceedings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 210,
      "values:originalText": "Criminal proceedings may be commenced against an entity for\nconduct that is the same, or substantially the same, as conduct that\nwould constitute a contravention of a civil penalty provision\nregardless of whether a civil penalty order has been made against\nthe entity in relation to the contravention.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80zf-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80zf"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80zf-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits conduct that would constitute a contravention of a civil penalty provision.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80zg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80ZG Evidence given in proceedings for civil penalty order not",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-80zg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.211",
      "values:originalText": "admissible in criminal proceedings\n\n(1) Evidence of information given, or evidence of production of\ndocuments, by an individual is not admissible in criminal\nproceedings against the individual if:\n\n(a) the individual previously gave the evidence or produced the\ndocuments in proceedings for a civil penalty order against the\nindividual for an alleged contravention of a civil penalty\nprovision (whether or not the order was made); and\n\n(b) the conduct alleged to constitute the offence is the same, or\nsubstantially the same, as the conduct alleged to constitute\nthe contravention.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply to criminal proceedings in\nrelation to the falsity of the evidence given by the individual in the\nproceedings for the civil penalty order.",
      "skos:definition": "admissible in criminal proceedings\n\n(1) Evidence of information given, or evidence of production of\ndocuments, by an individual is not admissible in criminal\nproceedings against the individual if:\n\n(a) the individual previously gave the evidence or produced the\ndocuments in proceedings for a civil penalty order against the\nindividual for an alleged contravention of a civil penalty\nprovision (whether or not the order was made); and\n\n(b) the conduct alleged to constitute the offence is the same, or\nsubstantially the same, as the conduct alleged to constitute\nthe contravention.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply to criminal proceedings in\nrelation to the falsity of the evidence given by the individual in the\nproceedings for the civil penalty order.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80zg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-80zg-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4380e9575e41a8337595f58e71d5d11d3547c873f4f1d87bfe9e851ba6b3498f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-80zg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80ZG Evidence given in proceedings for civil penalty order not",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 211,
      "values:originalText": "admissible in criminal proceedings\n\n(1) Evidence of information given, or evidence of production of\ndocuments, by an individual is not admissible in criminal\nproceedings against the individual if:\n\n(a) the individual previously gave the evidence or produced the\ndocuments in proceedings for a civil penalty order against the\nindividual for an alleged contravention of a civil penalty\nprovision (whether or not the order was made); and\n\n(b) the conduct alleged to constitute the offence is the same, or\nsubstantially the same, as the conduct alleged to constitute\nthe contravention.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply to criminal proceedings in\nrelation to the falsity of the evidence given by the individual in the\nproceedings for the civil penalty order."
    },
    {
