    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "96 Review by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-96-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.212",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application may be made to the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal for review of the following decisions of the\nCommissioner:\n\n(a) a decision under subsection 26H(1) not to register an APP\ncode developed by an APP code developer;\n\n(b) a decision under subsection 26S(1) not to register a CR code\ndeveloped by a CR code developer;\n\n(c) a decision under subsection 52(1) or (1A) to make a\ndetermination;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) a decision under subsection 73(1A) to dismiss an application;\n\n(e) a decision under section 95 to refuse to approve the issue of\nguidelines;\n\n(f) a decision under subsection 95A(2) or (4) or 95AA(2) to\nrefuse to approve guidelines;\n\n(g) a decision under subsection 95A(6) to revoke an approval of\nguidelines.\n\n(2) An application under paragraph (1)(a) may only be made by the\nAPP code developer that developed the APP code.\n\n(3) An application under paragraph (1)(b) may only be made by the\nCR code developer that developed the CR code.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An application may be made to the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal for review of the following decisions of the\nCommissioner:\n\n(a) a decision under subsection 26H(1) not to register an APP\ncode developed by an APP code developer;\n\n(b) a decision under subsection 26S(1) not to register a CR code\ndeveloped by a CR code developer;\n\n(c) a decision under subsection 52(1) or (1A) to make a\ndetermination;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) a decision under subsection 73(1A) to dismiss an application;\n\n(e) a decision under section 95 to refuse to approve the issue of\nguidelines;\n\n(f) a decision under subsection 95A(2) or (4) or 95AA(2) to\nrefuse to approve guidelines;\n\n(g) a decision under subsection 95A(6) to revoke an approval of\nguidelines.\n\n(2) An application under paragraph (1)(a) may only be made by the\nAPP code developer that developed the APP code.\n\n(3) An application under paragraph (1)(b) may only be made by the\nCR code developer that developed the CR code.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fb186d7914a0eb3faa471267d1cd114dab0ea10c5fd67889ad0a4cef26fceada"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-96-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "96 Review by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 212,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application may be made to the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal for review of the following decisions of the\nCommissioner:\n\n(a) a decision under subsection 26H(1) not to register an APP\ncode developed by an APP code developer;\n\n(b) a decision under subsection 26S(1) not to register a CR code\ndeveloped by a CR code developer;\n\n(c) a decision under subsection 52(1) or (1A) to make a\ndetermination;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(d) a decision under subsection 73(1A) to dismiss an application;\n\n(e) a decision under section 95 to refuse to approve the issue of\nguidelines;\n\n(f) a decision under subsection 95A(2) or (4) or 95AA(2) to\nrefuse to approve guidelines;\n\n(g) a decision under subsection 95A(6) to revoke an approval of\nguidelines.\n\n(2) An application under paragraph (1)(a) may only be made by the\nAPP code developer that developed the APP code.\n\n(3) An application under paragraph (1)(b) may only be made by the\nCR code developer that developed the CR code."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-96-2-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "96(1) Review by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-96-2-ss-1"
      },
