      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.213",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A partner does not commit an offence against this Act because of\nsubsection (2), or contravene a civil penalty provision because of\nsubsection (3), if the partner:\n\n(a) does not know of the circumstances that constitute the\ncontravention of the provision concerned; or\n\n(b) knows of those circumstances but takes all reasonable steps\nto correct the contravention as soon as possible after the\npartner becomes aware of those circumstances.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 4  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nNote:\nIn criminal proceedings, a defendant bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to the matters in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code).",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A partner does not commit an offence against this Act because of\nsubsection (2), or contravene a civil penalty provision because of\nsubsection (3), if the partner:\n\n(a) does not know of the circumstances that constitute the\ncontravention of the provision concerned; or\n\n(b) knows of those circumstances but takes all reasonable steps\nto correct the contravention as soon as possible after the\npartner becomes aware of those circumstances.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 4  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nNote:\nIn criminal proceedings, a defendant bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to the matters in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98a-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98a-ss-4-logic-epistemic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98a-ss-4-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1f579ea2c77bc39cd4b4f12381ba426a87ce5bfaed247852d6616c6dbac587a4",
      "skos:note": "A partner does not commit an offence if they do not know of the circumstances or take reasonable steps to correct them."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-98a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "98A(4) Treatment of partnerships",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 213,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A partner does not commit an offence against this Act because of\nsubsection (2), or contravene a civil penalty provision because of\nsubsection (3), if the partner:\n\n(a) does not know of the circumstances that constitute the\ncontravention of the provision concerned; or\n\n(b) knows of those circumstances but takes all reasonable steps\nto correct the contravention as soon as possible after the\npartner becomes aware of those circumstances.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 4  Other amendments of the Privacy Act 1988\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\n\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\nNote:\nIn criminal proceedings, a defendant bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to the matters in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code)."
    },
