      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Association would have violated a civil penalty provision",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Member is liable"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "98B(4) Treatment of unincorporated associations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-98b-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.214",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A member of an unincorporated association’s committee of\nmanagement does not commit an offence against this Act because\nof subsection (2), or contravene a civil penalty provision because\nof subsection (3), if the member:\n\n(a) does not know of the circumstances that constitute the\ncontravention of the provision concerned; or\n\n(b) knows of those circumstances but takes all reasonable steps\nto correct the contravention as soon as possible after the\nmember becomes aware of those circumstances.\nNote:\nIn criminal proceedings, a defendant bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to the matters in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code).",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A member of an unincorporated association’s committee of\nmanagement does not commit an offence against this Act because\nof subsection (2), or contravene a civil penalty provision because\nof subsection (3), if the member:\n\n(a) does not know of the circumstances that constitute the\ncontravention of the provision concerned; or\n\n(b) knows of those circumstances but takes all reasonable steps\nto correct the contravention as soon as possible after the\nmember becomes aware of those circumstances.\nNote:\nIn criminal proceedings, a defendant bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to the matters in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98b-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98b-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98b-ss-4-logic-epistemic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98b-ss-4-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "17e7ab46782ccd55a55e9240ac0d7631930e0e6b3b0e162c9bf1e709b20c66bd",
      "skos:note": "Member of unincorporated association's committee of management has an obligation to correct contravention as soon as possible after becoming aware."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-98b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "98B(4) Treatment of unincorporated associations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 214,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A member of an unincorporated association’s committee of\nmanagement does not commit an offence against this Act because\nof subsection (2), or contravene a civil penalty provision because\nof subsection (3), if the member:\n\n(a) does not know of the circumstances that constitute the\ncontravention of the provision concerned; or\n\n(b) knows of those circumstances but takes all reasonable steps\nto correct the contravention as soon as possible after the\nmember becomes aware of those circumstances.\nNote:\nIn criminal proceedings, a defendant bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to the matters in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98b-ss-4-norm",
