      },
      "cml:operator": "trace",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Trace of reasonable steps taken to correct contravention",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Member takes all reasonable steps",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Correct action taken"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "98C Treatment of trusts",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-98c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.214",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, apart from this subsection, this Act would impose an obligation\non a trust, the obligation is imposed instead on each trustee of the\ntrust but may be discharged by any of the trustees.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) If, apart from this subsection, an offence against this Act would be\ncommitted by a trust, the offence is taken to have been committed\nby each trustee of the trust.\n\n(3) If, apart from this subsection, a trust would contravene a civil\npenalty provision, the contravention is taken to have been\ncommitted by each trustee of the trust.\n\n(4) A trustee of a trust does not commit an offence against this Act\nbecause of subsection (2), or contravene a civil penalty provision\nbecause of subsection (3), if the trustee:\n\n(a) does not know of the circumstances that constitute the\ncontravention of the provision concerned; or\n\n(b) knows of those circumstances but takes all reasonable steps\nto correct the contravention as soon as possible after the\ntrustee becomes aware of those circumstances.\nNote:\nIn criminal proceedings, a defendant bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to the matters in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If, apart from this subsection, this Act would impose an obligation\non a trust, the obligation is imposed instead on each trustee of the\ntrust but may be discharged by any of the trustees.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nOther amendments of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15\n\n(2) If, apart from this subsection, an offence against this Act would be\ncommitted by a trust, the offence is taken to have been committed\nby each trustee of the trust.\n\n(3) If, apart from this subsection, a trust would contravene a civil\npenalty provision, the contravention is taken to have been\ncommitted by each trustee of the trust.\n\n(4) A trustee of a trust does not commit an offence against this Act\nbecause of subsection (2), or contravene a civil penalty provision\nbecause of subsection (3), if the trustee:\n\n(a) does not know of the circumstances that constitute the\ncontravention of the provision concerned; or\n\n(b) knows of those circumstances but takes all reasonable steps\nto correct the contravention as soon as possible after the\ntrustee becomes aware of those circumstances.\nNote:\nIn criminal proceedings, a defendant bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to the matters in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98c-ss-2"
        },
