      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Liability for contravention of civil penalty provisions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Trustee is a trustee of the trust.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Trustee is liable for contravention."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98c-ss-3-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "State is responsible for enforcing civil penalty provisions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "State has jurisdiction over trusts.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "State enforces liability on trustee."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "98C(4) Treatment of trusts",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-98c-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.214",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A trustee of a trust does not commit an offence against this Act\nbecause of subsection (2), or contravene a civil penalty provision\nbecause of subsection (3), if the trustee:\n\n(a) does not know of the circumstances that constitute the\ncontravention of the provision concerned; or\n\n(b) knows of those circumstances but takes all reasonable steps\nto correct the contravention as soon as possible after the\ntrustee becomes aware of those circumstances.\nNote:\nIn criminal proceedings, a defendant bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to the matters in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code).",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A trustee of a trust does not commit an offence against this Act\nbecause of subsection (2), or contravene a civil penalty provision\nbecause of subsection (3), if the trustee:\n\n(a) does not know of the circumstances that constitute the\ncontravention of the provision concerned; or\n\n(b) knows of those circumstances but takes all reasonable steps\nto correct the contravention as soon as possible after the\ntrustee becomes aware of those circumstances.\nNote:\nIn criminal proceedings, a defendant bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to the matters in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98c-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98c-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98c-ss-4-logic-epistemic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dc8ff1559f65f71eb187cf8500688b183fa95004ddeaccadfdddbf7f8317544a",
      "skos:note": "Trustee has an obligation to correct contravention as soon as possible after becoming aware of the circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-4-sec-98c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "98C(4) Treatment of trusts",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 214,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A trustee of a trust does not commit an offence against this Act\nbecause of subsection (2), or contravene a civil penalty provision\nbecause of subsection (3), if the trustee:\n\n(a) does not know of the circumstances that constitute the\ncontravention of the provision concerned; or\n\n(b) knows of those circumstances but takes all reasonable steps\nto correct the contravention as soon as possible after the\ntrustee becomes aware of those circumstances.\nNote:\nIn criminal proceedings, a defendant bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to the matters in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-4-sec-98c-ss-4-norm",
