    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-1-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-6-sec-1-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.244",
      "values:originalText": "In this Schedule:\ncommencement time means the time Schedule 1 to this Act\ncommences.\nPrivacy Act means the Privacy Act 1988.\ntransition period means the period:\n\n(a) starting on the day this Act receives the Royal Assent; and\n\n(b) ending immediately before the commencement time.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nApplication, transitional and savings provisions  Schedule 6\nProvisions relating to Schedule 1 to this Act  Part 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "skos:definition": "In this Schedule:\ncommencement time means the time Schedule 1 to this Act\ncommences.\nPrivacy Act means the Privacy Act 1988.\ntransition period means the period:\n\n(a) starting on the day this Act receives the Royal Assent; and\n\n(b) ending immediately before the commencement time.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nApplication, transitional and savings provisions  Schedule 6\nProvisions relating to Schedule 1 to this Act  Part 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-1-3-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a20627e571d9b92bdae14ff55c714824388e90505a9bee7bdaf0387036e1e882",
      "skos:note": "Defines terms for Schedule 1 to this Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-6-sec-1-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 244,
      "values:originalText": "In this Schedule:\ncommencement time means the time Schedule 1 to this Act\ncommences.\nPrivacy Act means the Privacy Act 1988.\ntransition period means the period:\n\n(a) starting on the day this Act receives the Royal Assent; and\n\n(b) ending immediately before the commencement time.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nApplication, transitional and savings provisions  Schedule 6\nProvisions relating to Schedule 1 to this Act  Part 2\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-1-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-1-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-2-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 Application—court/tribunal orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-6-sec-2-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.245",
      "values:originalText": "The definition of court/tribunal order in subsection 6(1) of the Privacy\nAct, as inserted by Schedule 1 to this Act, applies in relation to an\norder, direction or other instrument made before or after the\ncommencement time.\n3  Saving—guidelines relating to medical research etc.\n(1)\nThis item applies to guidelines if:\n\n(a) the guidelines were issued or approved under subsection\n95(1), 95A(2), 95A(4) or 95AA(2) of the Privacy Act; and\n\n(b) the guidelines were in force immediately before the\ncommencement time.\n(2)\nThe guidelines have effect, after that time, as if they had been issued or\napproved under that subsection, as amended by Schedule 1 to this Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 6  Application, transitional and savings provisions",
      "skos:definition": "The definition of court/tribunal order in subsection 6(1) of the Privacy\nAct, as inserted by Schedule 1 to this Act, applies in relation to an\norder, direction or other instrument made before or after the\ncommencement time.\n3  Saving—guidelines relating to medical research etc.\n(1)\nThis item applies to guidelines if:\n\n(a) the guidelines were issued or approved under subsection\n95(1), 95A(2), 95A(4) or 95AA(2) of the Privacy Act; and\n\n(b) the guidelines were in force immediately before the\ncommencement time.\n(2)\nThe guidelines have effect, after that time, as if they had been issued or\napproved under that subsection, as amended by Schedule 1 to this Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 6  Application, transitional and savings provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-2-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-2-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-2-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "94bbe44ac8b5bd217d0d994638451f04b617fb0cc7e834a762fd5633da7e067c",
      "skos:note": "Definition of court/tribunal order applies to orders made before or after commencement time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-6-sec-2-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Application—court/tribunal orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 245,
      "values:originalText": "The definition of court/tribunal order in subsection 6(1) of the Privacy\nAct, as inserted by Schedule 1 to this Act, applies in relation to an\norder, direction or other instrument made before or after the\ncommencement time.\n3  Saving—guidelines relating to medical research etc.\n(1)\nThis item applies to guidelines if:\n\n(a) the guidelines were issued or approved under subsection\n95(1), 95A(2), 95A(4) or 95AA(2) of the Privacy Act; and\n\n(b) the guidelines were in force immediately before the\ncommencement time.\n(2)\nThe guidelines have effect, after that time, as if they had been issued or\napproved under that subsection, as amended by Schedule 1 to this Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 6  Application, transitional and savings provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-2-3-norm",
