      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Application—credit reporting",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-6-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.246",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nTo the extent that the amendments of the Privacy Act made by\nSchedule 2 to this Act apply in relation to credit, they apply in relation\nto credit applied for, or provided, before or after the commencement\ntime.\n(2)\nThe definition of court proceedings information in subsection 6(1) of\nthe Privacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act, applies in relation\nto a judgement of an Australian court made or given before or after the\ncommencement time.\n(3)\nThe definition of serious credit infringement in subsection 6(1) of the\nPrivacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act, applies in relation to\nan act done before or after the commencement time.\n(4)\nParagraph 6N(k) of the Privacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this\nAct, applies in relation to activities done before or after the\ncommencement time.\n(5)\nSection 6R of the Privacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act,\napplies in relation to an information request made before or after the\ncommencement time.\n(6)\nSection 6V of the Privacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act,\napplies in relation to a monthly payment that is due and payable on or\nafter the day this Act receives the Royal Assent.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nApplication, transitional and savings provisions  Schedule 6\nProvisions relating to Schedule 3 to this Act  Part 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nTo the extent that the amendments of the Privacy Act made by\nSchedule 2 to this Act apply in relation to credit, they apply in relation\nto credit applied for, or provided, before or after the commencement\ntime.\n(2)\nThe definition of court proceedings information in subsection 6(1) of\nthe Privacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act, applies in relation\nto a judgement of an Australian court made or given before or after the\ncommencement time.\n(3)\nThe definition of serious credit infringement in subsection 6(1) of the\nPrivacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act, applies in relation to\nan act done before or after the commencement time.\n(4)\nParagraph 6N(k) of the Privacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this\nAct, applies in relation to activities done before or after the\ncommencement time.\n(5)\nSection 6R of the Privacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act,\napplies in relation to an information request made before or after the\ncommencement time.\n(6)\nSection 6V of the Privacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act,\napplies in relation to a monthly payment that is due and payable on or\nafter the day this Act receives the Royal Assent.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nApplication, transitional and savings provisions  Schedule 6\nProvisions relating to Schedule 3 to this Act  Part 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-4-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-4-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-4-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-4-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "952b58498dc31cb87d2c252335747ae07f28eeec0d1f30ebd92b34248b8595cb",
      "skos:note": "Applicability of amendments to credit reporting"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-6-sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Application—credit reporting",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 246,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nTo the extent that the amendments of the Privacy Act made by\nSchedule 2 to this Act apply in relation to credit, they apply in relation\nto credit applied for, or provided, before or after the commencement\ntime.\n(2)\nThe definition of court proceedings information in subsection 6(1) of\nthe Privacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act, applies in relation\nto a judgement of an Australian court made or given before or after the\ncommencement time.\n(3)\nThe definition of serious credit infringement in subsection 6(1) of the\nPrivacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act, applies in relation to\nan act done before or after the commencement time.\n(4)\nParagraph 6N(k) of the Privacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this\nAct, applies in relation to activities done before or after the\ncommencement time.\n(5)\nSection 6R of the Privacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act,\napplies in relation to an information request made before or after the\ncommencement time.\n(6)\nSection 6V of the Privacy Act, as inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act,\napplies in relation to a monthly payment that is due and payable on or\nafter the day this Act receives the Royal Assent.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nApplication, transitional and savings provisions  Schedule 6\nProvisions relating to Schedule 3 to this Act  Part 4\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Enhancing Privacy Protection) Act 2012\nCompilation date: 12/3/14\nRegistered: 6/3/15"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-4-norm",
