    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-12-13",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 Saving—public interest determinations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-6-sec-12-13"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012.pdf, p.249",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies to a determination if:\n\n(a) the determination was made under section 72 of the Privacy\nAct; and\n\n(b) the determination was in force immediately before the\ncommencement time.\n(2)\nThe determination has effect, after the commencement time, as if it had\nbeen made under that section, as amended by Schedule 4 to this Act.\n(3)\nThe Commissioner may, by legislative instrument, vary the\ndetermination after the commencement time to take account of the\namendments of the Privacy Act made by this Act.\n(4)\nIn deciding whether to vary the determination, the Commissioner may:\n\n(a) consult any person or entity; and\n\n(b) take into account any matter that the Commissioner considers\nrelevant.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 6  Application, transitional and savings provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThis item applies to a determination if:\n\n(a) the determination was made under section 72 of the Privacy\nAct; and\n\n(b) the determination was in force immediately before the\ncommencement time.\n(2)\nThe determination has effect, after the commencement time, as if it had\nbeen made under that section, as amended by Schedule 4 to this Act.\n(3)\nThe Commissioner may, by legislative instrument, vary the\ndetermination after the commencement time to take account of the\namendments of the Privacy Act made by this Act.\n(4)\nIn deciding whether to vary the determination, the Commissioner may:\n\n(a) consult any person or entity; and\n\n(b) take into account any matter that the Commissioner considers\nrelevant.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 6  Application, transitional and savings provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-12-13-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-12-13-logic-alleninterval-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-12-13-logic-ltl-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-12-13-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-12-13-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9d0029bdc1484992b5df501d59d73dfa27eb409ff4df9f66008a16f12071cf54",
      "skos:note": "Saving—public interest determinations"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012#sch-6-sec-12-13",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 Saving—public interest determinations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 249,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies to a determination if:\n\n(a) the determination was made under section 72 of the Privacy\nAct; and\n\n(b) the determination was in force immediately before the\ncommencement time.\n(2)\nThe determination has effect, after the commencement time, as if it had\nbeen made under that section, as amended by Schedule 4 to this Act.\n(3)\nThe Commissioner may, by legislative instrument, vary the\ndetermination after the commencement time to take account of the\namendments of the Privacy Act made by this Act.\n(4)\nIn deciding whether to vary the determination, the Commissioner may:\n\n(a) consult any person or entity; and\n\n(b) take into account any matter that the Commissioner considers\nrelevant.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00053\n\nSchedule 6  Application, transitional and savings provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-enhancing-privacy-protection-act-2012-sch-6-sec-12-13-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
